E["npc:braelyn-firehand"] = {t="npc",n="Braelyn Firehand",z="stonetalon",s="Braelyn Firehand is an elven practitioner of the arcane residing quietly among the Horde at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Claiming an interest in clearing mystical obstructions across the highlands, she enlists travelers to strike against the night elven guardians of Stonetalon Peak.",h="Braelyn Firehand is an elven practitioner of the arcane residing quietly among the Horde at Sun Rock Retreat...",sec={{t="An Unlikely Guest",b="Standing out amidst the tauren lodges and rustic orcish tents of Sun Rock Retreat, Braelyn Firehand is a rare sight: a high elf dwelling openly within a remote Horde settlement. The shaman and chieftains of the retreat tolerate her presence, seemingly oblivious to her true loyalties. Braelyn presents herself as an observer fascinated by the flow of regional magic, eager to hire passing Horde mercenaries to handle dangerous field assignments across the crags.",sp=0},{t="A Grudge Against the Grove",b="Braelyn directs her allies against the night elven druids and the sacred offspring of Cenarius stationed high above at Stonetalon Peak. She claims the druids choke the ambient ley lines and stifle the flow of arcane energy throughout the peaks. Her true focus, however, is intensely personal: she harbors bitter memories of Keeper Ordanus, recalling an ancient arrogance where he held himself above even the Highborne. She willingly pays Horde travelers to hunt down Ordanus and return with his head.",sp=1},{t="Ties to Jaedenar",b="Braelyn's resentment is more than idle lingering hatred; her aims align directly with the Shadow Council sect operating out of Jaedenar in Felwood. By encouraging Horde champions to systematically slaughter the night elves and the keepers holding the sacred peaks, she clears the way for darker powers while masking her sinister affiliation under the guise of ordinary frontier skirmishing.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Braelyn Firehand?",a="Braelyn Firehand is an elven mage living at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Though surrounded by the Horde, she pursues her own arcane agenda against the night elves guarding Stonetalon Peak.",al={"who is braelyn","braelyn firehand lore","elf in sun rock retreat"}},{q="Why is an elf staying in Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Sun Rock Retreat serves as a bustling, isolated frontier haven. Braelyn uses the camp's tolerance and its steady stream of Horde warriors to contract out her personal strikes against the night elves without arousing immediate suspicion from the settlement's leadership.",al={"why is she with the horde","why is braelyn in sun rock","blood elf in stonetalon"}},{q="What does she want done at Stonetalon Peak?",a="Braelyn instructs adventurers to infiltrate Stonetalon Peak to kill night elf druids, slay the sons of Cenarius, and decapitate their leader, Keeper Ordanus, ostensibly to reopen the suppressed flows of magic in the mountains.",al={"braelyn quest goals","why kill ordanus","braelyn firehand tasks"}},{q="What is her history with Keeper Ordanus?",a="Braelyn claims to have known Keeper Ordanus personally in the distant past. She resents him bitterly, alleging that he carried immense arrogance and regarded himself as superior even to the ancient Highborne.",al={"braelyn and ordanus","how does she know ordanus","ordanus backstory"}},{q="Who does Braelyn Firehand actually serve?",a="Beneath her claims of restoring arcane balance, Braelyn is an operative working on behalf of the Shadow Council sect rooted in Jaedenar, weaponizing Horde adventurers against the demonic cult's natural enemies.",al={"braelyn true faction","braelyn shadow council","who does she work for"},sp=2},{q="Is Braelyn a mage or a warlock?",a="While affiliated with the demon-worshiping Shadow Council, Braelyn commands arcane fire and frost like a traditional mage rather than drawing upon demonic fel or curses.",al={"braelyn class","is braelyn a warlock","braelyn firehand spells"},sp=2}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Braelyn gladly hires Horde wanderers to strike at the night elves, turning the ongoing territorial clashes in Kalimdor into cover for a deeper, darker agenda.",["class:Mage"]="Braelyn speaks readily of ley energies and mystical blockages, appealing to fellow practitioners who understand the flow of arcane magic through the land.",["class:Druid"]="Her deliberate slaughter of the sons of Cenarius and the desecration of the Barrow Dens stand as an abhorrent crime against the balance of nature."},kw={"braelyn","cenarius","firehand","highborne","ordanus","stonetalon","sun rock retreat"},rel={"subzone:sun-rock-retreat","quest:1088","quest:1087","quest:1089","subzone:stonetalon-peak","topic:shadow-council","subzone:jaedenar","topic:highborne"},src={"Braelyn Firehand"}}
E["npc:darn-talongrip"] = {t="npc",n="Darn Talongrip",z="stonetalon",s="Darn Talongrip is an orc scout stationed along the frontier of the Stonetalon Mountains near Malaka'jin. He monitors local threats in the crags and helps coordinate Horde communication between forward outposts and regional commanders.",h="Darn Talongrip is an orc scout stationed along the frontier of the Stonetalon Mountains near Malaka'jin.",sec={{t="Frontier Scout of Stonetalon",b="Darn Talongrip watches the rugged ascents leading into Stonetalon from the southern Barrens. Perched near the settlement of Malaka'jin and the perilous Webwinder Path, Darn contends with regional dangers such as the aggressive local spiders that choke the ravine paths. His post serves as an early line of contact for travelers winding upward into contested peaks.",sp=0},{t="Eyes for the Command",b="Beyond monitoring venomous beasts in the nearby crags, Darn ensures messages and frontline reports reach key commanders like Kadrak at the Stonetalon border. Outlying encampments in these mountains operate under constant pressure, making Darn's role as a sentry and courier essential to keeping the Horde vanguard informed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Darn Talongrip?",a="Darn Talongrip is an orc scout stationed along Webwinder Path near Malaka'jin in the southern reaches of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who is darn talongrip","darn talongrip identity","who is this orc"}},{q="Where can Darn Talongrip be found?",a="He can be found watching the trails near the troll settlement of Malaka'jin, along Webwinder Path in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"darn talongrip location","where is darn talongrip","darn talongrip coordinates"}},{q="What is his role in Stonetalon?",a="Darn serves as an outpost scout, warning travelers of dangerous predators like local spider broods and passing messages to military liaisons such as Kadrak.",al={"what does darn talongrip do","darn talongrip purpose"}},{q="Who is Kadrak, and why does Darn send travelers to him?",a="Kadrak is a Horde overseer stationed near the border crossing between the Barrens and Stonetalon Mountains. Darn directs travelers to him to keep regional commanders updated on field conditions.",al={"who is kadrak","report to kadrak"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Darn Talongrip keeps early watch along the ascent into Stonetalon, acting as a valuable contact for Horde adventurers fresh from the Barrens.",["race:Orc"]="Like many orc scouts, Darn embraces the harsh conditions of the frontier, standing watch amid jagged rocks and hostile wildlife."},kw={"darn talongrip","kadrak","malakajin","orc scout","stonetalon","webwinder path"},rel={"subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:webwinder-path","npc:kadrak","quest:6541","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Darn Talongrip"}}
E["npc:falfindel-waywarder"] = {t="npc",n="Falfindel Waywarder",z="stonetalon",s="Falfindel Waywarder is a night elf sentinel stationed at Thalanaar, the outpost guarding the border between Feralas and the Thousand Needles. From this frontier watchpost, he works to heal corrupted lands and safeguard the southern wilderness of Kalimdor. Travelers wandering down from Stonetalon or the Barrens often find him seeking aid to restore balance to the wild.",h="Falfindel Waywarder is a night elf sentinel stationed at Thalanaar, the outpost guarding the border between...",sec={{t="Watch at the Southern Border",b="Thalanaar marks the gateway where the lush forests of Feralas descend into the towering mesas and dry salt plains of Thousand Needles. Falfindel Waywarder stands watch at this remote outpost, greeting weary travelers who have ventured far across the continent. Surrounded by natural grandeur and lurking dangers, he serves as a point of contact for the night elves seeking to monitor both local threats and broader environmental calamities across Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Charred Vale",b="Despite his southern post, Falfindel remains deeply concerned with the devastation far to the north in Stonetalon Mountains. The Charred Vale, ruined by dark sorcery and fiery destruction, stands as a painful scar upon Kalimdor's wilderness. When adventurers deliver aid to Falfindel to assist in its recovery, he calls upon the spirits of the forest. Summoning forth swarms of wisps, he directs them to make haste north to Stonetalon to begin mending the scorched earth.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Quillboar and the Wastes",b="In addition to coordinating restoration efforts, Falfindel keeps a close watch on the surrounding region, including the quilboar dens of Razorfen Kraul. By reviewing recovered journals and gathering intelligence on quilboar leadership, Falfindel ensures that the Alliance understands the rising dangers threatening the passes between Feralas and the central deserts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Falfindel Waywarder located?",a="Falfindel is stationed at Thalanaar, the night elf outpost situated on the border between Feralas and Thousand Needles.",al={"falfindel location","where is falfindel","falfindel waywarder map"}},{q="What is Falfindel's role at Thalanaar?",a="He serves as a sentinel and guide at the outpost, monitoring regional threats such as the quilboar in Thousand Needles and coordinating restoration efforts for ruined lands like the Charred Vale.",al={"what does falfindel do","falfindel purpose","falfindel quests"}},{q="How does Falfindel help the Charred Vale?",a="When adventurers assist in efforts to reclaim the Charred Vale, Falfindel channels an incantation to summon forest wisps, dispatching them north to Stonetalon to heal the blighted land.",al={"falfindel stonetalon","falfindel charred vale","reclaiming the charred vale falfindel"}},{q="Why is Falfindel interested in Razorfen Kraul?",a="He studies the threat posed by the quilboar of the Kraul and inspects items like Lonebrow's journal to track the influence of their leaders, such as the Crone of the Kraul.",al={"crone of the kraul falfindel","lonebrow journal falfindel","falfindel quilboar"}},{q="Is Falfindel aligned with the Alliance or neutral?",a="Falfindel is a member of the night elf sentinels and is allied with the Alliance. Horde travelers approaching Thalanaar will find the outpost hostile.",al={"is falfindel alliance","falfindel faction"}},{q="What does Falfindel say to travelers?",a="He warmly greets friendly visitors by acknowledging their long journey, remarking, 'You look as though you have traveled from afar.'",al={"falfindel gossip","falfindel quote"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Falfindel represents your people's vigilance on the frontiers of Kalimdor, striving to mend nature's scars and guard against encroaching wilderness perils.",["class:Druid"]="His efforts to send forest spirits and wisps to heal the scorched soils of Stonetalon reflect the sacred druidic mission of restoration.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers making the long trek south from the Barrens or Stonetalon, Falfindel and the watch at Thalanaar offer a welcoming sanctuary."},kw={"charred vale","falfindel","feralas","stonetalon","thalanaar","thousand needles","waywarder","wisps"},rel={"subzone:thalanaar","quest:1057","quest:1100","quest:1101","zone:feralas","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:charred-vale","topic:night-elf"},src={"Falfindel Waywarder"}}
E["npc:force-commander-valen"] = {t="npc",n="Force Commander Valen",z="stonetalon",s="Force Commander Valen is the commanding officer of the Alliance outpost at the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp in the Stonetalon Mountains. Charged with safeguarding Theramore's territorial push into the region, he coordinates operations against the surrounding Horde forces and hostile Grimtotem tauren.",h="Force Commander Valen is the commanding officer of the Alliance outpost at the Northwatch Expedition Base...",sec={{t="Frontier Commander",b="Positioned at the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp, Force Commander Valen oversees Alliance military strategy in the crags of Stonetalon. His command serves as an arm of the broader Northwatch presence originating from Theramore. Valen must balance multiple conflicts at once: monitoring local Horde maneuvers, clearing out native hazards like the Deep Reaches, and repelling raids led by the aggressive Grimtotem clan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Force Commander Valen?",a="Force Commander Valen is the commanding officer of the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp in the Stonetalon Mountains. He represents the Alliance forces tied to Theramore and directs defensive and offensive strikes across the region.",al={"who is valen","commander valen lore","northwatch commander"}},{q="What threats is Valen facing in Stonetalon?",a="Valen oversees operations against aggressive Horde forces contesting the region and the ruthless Grimtotem tauren led by Grundig Darkcloud. He also directs reconnaissance and containment efforts regarding subterranean threats in the nearby Deep Reaches.",al={"why is northwatch in stonetalon","valen enemies","valen threats"}},{q="Is Valen affiliated with Theramore or Stormwind?",a="Valen commands a Northwatch expedition, meaning his forces are directly linked to Theramore Isle's military infrastructure, operating under the broader banner of the Alliance in central Kalimdor.",al={"valen allegiance","northwatch expedition faction"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions venturing into Stonetalon, Valen serves as the frontline military authority providing missions to secure high ground against both the Horde and the Grimtotem.",["faction:Horde"]="Valen represents the encroachment of Theramore's military might deep into Kalimdor, directly menacing Horde travel routes through the Stonetalon Mountains."},kw={"deep reaches","expedition","force commander valen","grimtotem","northwatch","stonetalon","valen"},rel={"subzone:northwatch-expedition-base-camp","zone:stonetalon","subzone:deep-reaches","topic:horde"},src={"Force Commander Valen"}}
E["npc:gaxim-rustfizzle"] = {t="npc",n="Gaxim Rustfizzle",z="stonetalon",s="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an ambitious gnome scholar and tinker stationed at a small Alliance camp along the Webwinder Path in Stonetalon Mountains. A representative of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, he seeks to prove to skeptical night elves that advanced artifice and alchemy can preserve their woodland realm. His scientific curiosity is matched by a fierce vendetta against the destructive operations of the Venture Company.",h="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an ambitious gnome scholar and tinker stationed at a small Alliance camp along the...",sec={{t="A Scientific Emissary",b="While night elves traditionally rely on ancient druidism and nature magic, Gaxim Rustfizzle arrived in the craggy passes of Stonetalon to demonstrate a radically different perspective. Representing the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, he genuinely believes that calculated mechanisms and chemical solutions can defend and restore Kalimdor's wilderness just as effectively as prayers to Elune. Camped alongside the sentinel Kaela Shadowspear on the Webwinder Path, he works tirelessly to convince his tall, reclusive allies of engineering's ecological merits.",sp=0},{t="Sabotaging the Saws",b="Much of Gaxim's energy is channeled against the Venture Company, whose clear-cutting and industrial greed desecrate nearby Windshear Crag. Believing that crude goblin machinery deserves neither respect nor mercy, Gaxim coordinates covert operations and volatile chemical sabotage against their logging operations. To him, crippling their shredders and stealing their schematics is not merely tactical warfare—it is a practical demonstration that superior gnomish intellect always triumphs over careless corporate plunder.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome scholar and inventor stationed at an Alliance lookout along the Webwinder Path in the Stonetalon Mountains. He serves as an emissary for the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences.",al={"who is gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle lore","gnome in stonetalon"}},{q="What is the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences?",a="It is an academic and scientific society of gnomes dedicated to blending the disciplines of arcane magic, alchemical mixtures, and mechanical engineering. Gaxim represents their ideals abroad in Kalimdor.",al={"enlightened assembly","gaxim faction","gaxim group"}},{q="Why is Gaxim working with the night elves?",a="Gaxim wants to demonstrate to the night elves that gnomish science and alchemy can actively protect and heal natural woodlands, offering a modern Alliance answer to forest conservation alongside traditional druidism.",al={"why is gaxim here","gaxim night elves","gaxim purpose"}},{q="Why does Gaxim hate the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company is ruthlessly clear-cutting Windshear Crag with crude machines and toxic pollution. Gaxim despises their reckless exploitation and relishes turning volatile chemicals and sabotage against their operations.",al={"gaxim venture co","gaxim vs venture company","why fight venture co"}},{q="Who is camped with Gaxim on Webwinder Path?",a="He shares his small outpost with Kaela Shadowspear, a night elf sentinel watching over the trails leading into Windshear Crag.",al={"gaxim companion","who is with gaxim","gaxim and kaela"}},{q="Where can Gaxim Rustfizzle be found?",a="He is located at a modest Alliance camp along the Webwinder Path, just southwest of the industrial logging pits of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"gaxim location","where is gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle map"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim represents gnomish academic pride at its finest, showing Kalimdor's ancient cultures that gears and reagents can save a forest just as well as nature magic.",["race:NightElf"]="Though traditionalists may scoff at his whirring gadgets and bubbling vials, Gaxim is a steadfast ally actively defending Ashenvale and Stonetalon borders from goblin industry.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gaxim puts engineering principles to work in the field, designing covert operations and tactical devices specifically tuned to disrupt crude Venture Company machinery.",["faction:Alliance"]="Perched on the perilous Webwinder Path, Gaxim provides crucial scouting, intelligence, and sabotage missions to check aggressive industrial incursions in Stonetalon."},kw={"assembly","gaxim","gnome","kaela","rustfizzle","stonetalon","venture company","webwinder","windshear"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:webwinder-path","subzone:windshear-crag","npc:kaela-shadowspear","topic:venture-company","quest:1073","quest:1079","quest:1080"},src={"Gaxim Rustfizzle"}}
E["npc:general-grebo"] = {t="npc",n="General Grebo",z="stonetalon",s="General Grebo serves as the second-in-command to Overlord Krom'gar among the Horde forces in the Stonetalon Mountains. Known for his aggressive paranoia, he oversees operations driven by fear of night elf weapons, ruthlessly rooting out perceived threats.",h="General Grebo serves as the second-in-command to Overlord Krom'gar among the Horde forces in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="Second in Command",b="Operating under Overlord Krom'gar, General Grebo is tasked with prosecuting the Horde's harsh campaign across the Stonetalon Mountains. Deeply suspicious and violent, Grebo is consumed by conviction that the night elves within Thal'darah Grove harbor a devastating secret weapon capable of crushing the Horde war effort. Driven by this obsession, he views local attempts at diplomacy and de-escalation as direct acts of treason.",sp=0},{t="Blood and Betrayal",b="When High Chieftain Cliffwalker sent his own son to independently investigate Thal'darah Grove, Grebo intervened with lethal force, murdering the young tauren to keep his militant ambitions unchecked. Carelessly leaving his Krom'gar general's insignia at the crime scene, Grebo was eventually cornered by the grieving chieftain. Rather than face judgment, the unrepentant general turned his blades on Cliffwalker, meeting his death in the ensuing clash.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is General Grebo?",a="General Grebo is an orc commander serving directly beneath Overlord Krom'gar, acting as the second-in-command of the Krom'gar vanguard in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who is grebo","general grebo role","who is this orc"}},{q="What is Grebo's objective in Stonetalon?",a="Grebo is fixated on eliminating the night elf presence in Stonetalon. In particular, he believes the night elves of Thal'darah Grove are concealing a dangerous super-weapon that poses an imminent threat to the Horde.",al={"grebo goal","what does grebo want","thal darah grove weapon"}},{q="Why does High Chieftain Cliffwalker fight General Grebo?",a="Grebo murdered High Chieftain Cliffwalker's son when the youth went to scout Thal'darah Grove. When confronted with the insignia he left behind at the crime, Grebo attacked the chieftain, forcing Cliffwalker to strike him down.",al={"why kill grebo","grebo cliffwalker fight","who killed cliffwalkers son"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Grebo exemplifies the reckless, dishonorable warmongering that threatens tauren autonomy in their ancestral lands, ultimately striking at the heart of the Cliffwalker tribe.",["faction:Horde"]="Serving under Krom'gar, Grebo represents an extreme faction willing to murder allied scouts and slaughter rivals in pursuit of total military dominance."},kw={"cliffwalker","general grebo","grebo","krom'gar","overlord krom'gar","stonetalon","thal'darah grove"},rel={"npc:overlord-krom-gar","npc:high-chieftain-cliffwalker","subzone:cliffwalker-post","subzone:thal-darah-grove","zone:stonetalon","topic:horde","topic:night-elf"},src={"General Grebo"}}
E["npc:grish-longrunner"] = {t="npc",n="Grish Longrunner",z="stonetalon",s="Grish Longrunner is a tauren scout and messenger stationed near the Great Lift, the vital mechanical crossing connecting the southern Barrens with the canyons of Thousand Needles. Serving the interests of the Horde along this bustling boundary, he keeps watch over travelers and coordinates military movement across the frontier.",h="Grish Longrunner is a tauren scout and messenger stationed near the Great Lift, the vital mechanical crossing...",sec={{t="Watcher at the Lift",b="Positioned right beside the towering machinery of the Great Lift, Grish Longrunner stands watch over one of central Kalimdor's most precarious border crossings. The platform elevator is a lifeline connecting the arid wastes of the southern Barrens to the windswept mesas of Thousand Needles below. Between roving quilboar packs and competing territorial threats, travel along this vertical boundary is dangerous, making scouts like Grish essential for keeping the Horde informed and summoning reinforcements where they are sorely needed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grish Longrunner?",a="Grish Longrunner is a tauren scout aligned with the Horde who is stationed at the rim of the Great Lift, which descends from the Barrens down into Thousand Needles.",al={"who is grish","grish longrunner identity","what does grish do"}},{q="Where can I find Grish Longrunner?",a="He is located in the southern reaches of the Barrens, right near the mechanical entrance of the Great Lift leading down to Thousand Needles.",al={"grish longrunner location","where is grish","find grish"}},{q="What role does he play in the area?",a="Grish acts as a point of contact for Horde messengers and travelers, notably assisting in rallying and directing local reinforcements through requests like Calling in the Reserves.",al={"grish purpose","grish quests","calling in the reserves grish"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde couriers and warriors journeying south toward Thousand Needles or returning north into the Barrens, Grish serves as an important lookout and point of contact at the lift.",["race:Tauren"]="Bearing the proud Longrunner name, Grish represents the endurance and vigilance of the shu'halo as they secure vital routes across their ancestral homelands."},kw={"barrens","calling in the reserves","great lift","grish","longrunner","tauren","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:great-lift","quest:5881","zone:barrens","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:quilboar"},src={"Grish Longrunner"}}
E["npc:grunt-logmar"] = {t="npc",n="Grunt Logmar",z="stonetalon",s="Grunt Logmar is an orc warrior of the Horde stationed in the southern Barrens at Camp Taurajo. Dutiful and vigilant, he monitors threats surrounding the camp and coordinates efforts to locate and aid missing Horde scouts in the region.",h="Grunt Logmar is an orc warrior of the Horde stationed in the southern Barrens at Camp Taurajo.",sec={{t="Duty at Camp Taurajo",b="Stationed among the tauren at Camp Taurajo, Grunt Logmar serves as a watchful orc guard on the southern Barrens frontier. The settlement sits close to hostile quilboar grounds and the mountain passes leading into Stonetalon and Mulgore, requiring constant vigilance. Logmar coordinates scouting reports and reaches out to capable Horde travelers when his comrades find themselves ambushed or captured by local hostiles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grunt Logmar?",a="Grunt Logmar is an orc soldier stationed at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, serving the Horde by securing the settlement and overseeing rescue and reconnaissance tasks.",al={"grunt logmar","who is logmar","logmar barrens"}},{q="Where can Grunt Logmar be found?",a="He is located in Camp Taurajo, an outpost situated in the southern plains of the Barrens along the road leading toward the Great Lift and Thousand Needles.",al={"where is logmar","logmar location","find grunt logmar"}},{q="What matters does Logmar oversee?",a="Logmar deals with the safety of missing Horde scouts, notably tasking travelers to investigate the disappearance and captivity of fellow grunt Dogran and secure vital supplies like Ken'zigla's draught.",al={"logmar quests","what does logmar want","dogran rescue"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Logmar represents the frontline military presence supporting the tauren in the Barrens, relying on Horde champions to look after fallen and captured scouts.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc grunt stationed far from Orgrimmar, Logmar demonstrates the Horde's commitment to standing shoulder-to-shoulder with their tauren allies."},kw={"camp taurajo","dogran","grunt logmar","ken'zigla's draught","orc grunt","taurajo","the barrens"},rel={"subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:barrens","quest:1515","quest:1511","zone:stonetalon","topic:alliance"},src={"Grunt Logmar"}}
E["npc:high-chieftain-cliffwalker"] = {t="npc",n="High Chieftain Cliffwalker",z="stonetalon",s="High Chieftain Cliffwalker is the venerable leader of the Cliffwalker tauren residing in the Stonetalon Mountains. Anchored at Cliffwalker Post, he strives to maintain traditional tauren ties to the land and peaceful equilibrium with the region's nature-aligned denizens.",h="High Chieftain Cliffwalker is the venerable leader of the Cliffwalker tauren residing in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Chieftain in the Crags",b="Perched within the rugged heights of the Stonetalon Mountains, High Chieftain Cliffwalker governs Cliffwalker Post, leading his kin in a land fraught with creeping tension between nature's protectors and outside resource extraction. Uniquely carrying the rare title of High Chieftain, he commands deep respect among his tribe. Rather than pursuing aggressive conquest, Cliffwalker favors ancestral tauren traditions, valuing harmony with the land and cautious diplomacy over needless bloodshed in Stonetalon's delicate ecosystem.",sp=0},{t="Defending Stonetalon's Balance",b="The mountains of Stonetalon harbor sacred ancient sites and ancestral groves watched over by both druidic orders and local tauren. Chieftain Cliffwalker works tirelessly to keep his people grounded amidst the volatile frictions of Kalimdor. Maintaining ties and an understanding with nearby druidic caretakers, Cliffwalker acts as a steady voice of moderation, cautioning against reckless escalation and seeking to ensure that the earth and its sacred groves are spared devastation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Chieftain Cliffwalker?",a="He is the leader of the Cliffwalker tauren tribe, dwelling high in the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains at Cliffwalker Post.",al={"cliffwalker lore","who is cliffwalker","high chieftain cliffwalker"}},{q="Why does he hold the title of High Chieftain?",a="While the title of High Chieftain is exceptionally rare among the tauren—traditionally reserved for overall leaders like Cairne Bloodhoof—Cliffwalker holds it as the supreme head of his distinct mountain clan.",al={"why high chieftain","high chieftain title"}},{q="What is his stance on conflicts in the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="High Chieftain Cliffwalker advocates for honor, restraint, and preserving the sanctity of the land, actively opposing senseless slaughter and seeking peaceful coexistence around the region's sacred groves.",al={"cliffwalker alliance","cliffwalker peace"}},{q="Where can High Chieftain Cliffwalker be found?",a="He makes his home at Cliffwalker Post, an elevated settlement located in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"cliffwalker location","where is cliffwalker"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, High Chieftain Cliffwalker represents the enduring wisdom of the Earth Mother, demonstrating that true strength lies in protecting the land rather than seeking blind aggression.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find common ground with Cliffwalker, whose clan values the natural harmony of Stonetalon's groves and respects those who tend to nature."},kw={"cliffwalker","cliffwalker post","high chieftain cliffwalker","stonetalon","tauren","thal'darah grove"},rel={"subzone:cliffwalker-post","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren","topic:druid","subzone:thal-darah-grove","topic:horde"},src={"High Chieftain Cliffwalker"}}
E["npc:kaela-shadowspear"] = {t="npc",n="Kaela Shadowspear",z="stonetalon",s="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf sentinel stationed southwest of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. From her small outpost, she coordinates with fellow sentinels to monitor escalating tensions and regional disruptions in the wilderness. She relies on brave travelers to scout dangerous territory and bring aid to the land's wounded defenders.",h="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf sentinel stationed southwest of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Scout on the Frontier",b="Positioned just southwest of the industrial devastation of Windshear Crag, Kaela Shadowspear keeps a watchful vigil over the surrounding passes. The Stonetalon Mountains are fraught with danger as the Horde encroaches and goblin operations exploit the land's natural bounty. Operating alongside the gnome Gaxim Rustfizzle, Kaela acts as an essential forward liaison for the night elves, tracking threats that push deeper into ancestral territory.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Land",b="The unrest in Stonetalon goes far beyond territorial skirmishes. The violent disruption of nature has agitated the elementals and brought harm to ancient guardians of the forest. Kaela works tirelessly to dispatch adventurers against raging elemental spirits and to tend to the wounded ancients suffering in the crossfire of the region's conflicts, striving to restore peace before the land is irrevocably scarred.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf quest giver stationed in a frontier camp southwest of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. She oversees regional scouting and aids in protecting the local wildlife and spirits.",al={"who is kaela","kaela shadowspear identity","kaela npc"}},{q="Where can Kaela Shadowspear be found?",a="She is located in a small Alliance camp situated southwest of Windshear Crag along the road in the Stonetalon Mountains, sharing the camp with the gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle.",al={"kaela shadowspear location","where is kaela","kaela stonetalon camp"}},{q="Who does Kaela report to?",a="Kaela coordinates closely with Sentinel Thenysil, regularly sending and receiving intelligence updates on enemy movements and local threats across Stonetalon.",al={"kaela reports to who","kaela thenysil","kaela's commander"}},{q="Why is Kaela concerned about the elementals?",a="Intense logging, mining, and military encroachment in Stonetalon have deeply disturbed the natural balance, causing elemental spirits to fly into a rage and attack anyone nearby.",al={"enraged spirits quest","why are spirits angry","kaela elemental spirits"}},{q="What is happening to the ancients near Windshear Crag?",a="The regional conflicts and rapid deforestation have left ancient protectors wounded and suffering. Kaela seeks the aid of travelers to find and heal these fallen protectors of the wild.",al={"wounded ancients quest","kaela ancients","stonetalon wounded ancients"}},{q="Why is a gnome stationed with Kaela?",a="Kaela shares her camp with Gaxim Rustfizzle, an Alliance gnome. While Kaela focuses on the spiritual and tactical balance of the wilderness, Gaxim is concerned with counteracting the hostile goblin machinery and operations nearby.",al={"gaxim rustfizzle kaela","why is gaxim with kaela","gnome and night elf camp"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Kaela Shadowspear serves as a crucial point of contact for Alliance adventurers venturing into the contested reaches of Stonetalon, coordinating intelligence between distant outposts.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, Kaela represents the steadfast defense of sacred ground, laboring to soothe outraged spirits and safeguard the revered ancients of Kalimdor.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find common cause with Kaela's efforts to nurse injured ancients back to health and silence the agony of disturbed nature spirits."},kw={"ancients","kaela","rustfizzle","sentinel","shadowspear","spirits","stonetalon","thenysil","windshear"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","npc:sentinel-thenysil","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","quest:1084","quest:1083","quest:1091","quest:1082","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Kaela Shadowspear"}}
E["npc:keeper-albagorm"] = {t="npc",n="Keeper Albagorm",z="stonetalon",s="Keeper Albagorm is a keeper of the grove stationed at the idyllic sanctuary of Stonetalon Peak. Deeply concerned by the devastation corrupting the southern reaches of the mountains, he enlists travelers to help heal the scorched wilderness of the Charred Vale.",h="Keeper Albagorm is a keeper of the grove stationed at the idyllic sanctuary of Stonetalon Peak.",sec={{t="A Guardian on the Peak",b="Perched within the peaceful boughs of Stonetalon Peak, Keeper Albagorm stands vigil over one of Kalimdor's sacred elven refuges. Like many sons of Cenarius, he feels the pain of the natural world acutely. His attention is drawn southward toward the smoldering ruins of the Charred Vale, where rampant elemental destruction and foul magic have choked out all green life. From his sanctuary, Albagorm works tirelessly to halt the spread of the corruption and restore balance to the wounded forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Albagorm?",a="He is a keeper of the grove—one of the demigod offspring of Cenarius—stationed at Stonetalon Peak in the Stonetalon Mountains. He serves as an ally to the night elves and natural guardians of Kalimdor.",al={"keeper albagorm","who is albagorm","albagorm stonetalon"}},{q="Where can I find Keeper Albagorm?",a="He resides at Stonetalon Peak, an Alliance-aligned druidic refuge nestled high in the northwestern corner of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"keeper albagorm location","where is albagorm","albagorm coords"}},{q="What does Keeper Albagorm want help with?",a="Albagorm seeks to mend the devastation of the Charred Vale. He sends capable adventurers into the ash-choked basin to cleanse the blighted landscape and push back the corrupt forces preventing natural regrowth.",al={"keeper albagorm quests","what does albagorm want","reclaiming the charred vale"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a keeper of the grove, Albagorm shares a direct connection to the Cenarion lineage, making his efforts to cleanse the Charred Vale deeply personal to druids.",["faction:Alliance"]="Albagorm offers shelter and guidance to Alliance forces navigating through the night elven sanctuary at Stonetalon Peak."},kw={"cenarius","charred vale","keeper albagorm","keeper of the grove","stonetalon","stonetalon peak"},rel={"subzone:stonetalon-peak","quest:1057","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Keeper Albagorm"}}
E["npc:lomac-gearstrip"] = {t="npc",n="Lomac Gearstrip",z="stonetalon",s="Lomac Gearstrip is an ambitious gnome inventor based in Tinker Town within Ironforge. Renowned for formulating the devastating NG-5 explosive, he liaises with fellow gnomish researchers operating across Kalimdor.",h="Lomac Gearstrip is an ambitious gnome inventor based in Tinker Town within Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Spark in Tinker Town",b="Amid the clanging gears and hissing pipes of Ironforge's Tinker Town, Lomac Gearstrip pursues the finer points of gnomish ordnance. Like many exiled gnomes who fled the tragedy at Gnomeregan, Lomac has integrated his tinkering operations directly into the dwarven capital. His workshop focuses on volatile chemical mixtures and specialized munitions designed to overcome heavily defended enemy strongholds.",sp=0},{t="The NG-5 Explosive",b="Lomac's proudest contribution to modern combat engineering is the NG-5 explosive. Formulated for maximum destructive yield, the compound demands precise handling and rare chemical reagents. To refine and deploy such hazardous inventions in the field, Lomac maintains contact with old colleagues stationed in distant theaters, exchanging technical orders and dangerous supplies across the Great Sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac Gearstrip resides in Tinker Town, the gnomish quarter located in the eastern portion of the mountain city of Ironforge.",al={"lomac gearstrip location","where is lomac","find lomac gearstrip"}},{q="What is Lomac Gearstrip famous for inventing?",a="Lomac is best known as the creator of the NG-5 explosive, a potent ordnance formula designed to provide devastating firepower for gnomish endeavors.",al={"what did lomac make","lomac invention","ng-5 explosive creator"}},{q="Why does Lomac deal with contacts in Kalimdor?",a="Lomac keeps in touch with former research peers and colleagues working in frontier regions like Stonetalon Mountains, coordinating the procurement of hazardous chemical ingredients and testing his high-yield explosives in active operations.",al={"lomac stonetalon","why stonetalon quest","lomac colleagues"}},{q="What kind of tasks does Lomac offer to adventurers?",a="Lomac tasks trustworthy Alliance couriers with transporting purchase orders and volatile chemical reagents between Ironforge and researchers stationed abroad, often involving his NG-5 explosive experiments.",al={"lomac quests","ineptitude chemicals fun","an old colleague quest"}},{q="What is the Purchase Order Receipt tied to Lomac?",a="Lomac authored the Purchase Order Receipt, a manifest used to organize and document shipments of specialized equipment and dangerous volatile reagents between tinkerers.",al={"purchase order receipt","lomac receipt"}},{q="Is Lomac affiliated with Gnomeregan's refugees?",a="Yes. Like the rest of the residents of Tinker Town, Lomac is part of the displaced Gnomeregan community living under the hospitality of the Ironforge dwarves while continuing his engineering work.",al={"is lomac from gnomeregan","lomac faction"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Lomac's NG-5 explosive represents the cutting edge of gnomish pyrotechnics, serving as inspiration for tinkerers interested in high-yield blasting compounds.",["race:Gnome"]="Lomac embodies the resilient drive of Tinker Town's gnomes, maintaining high-stakes technical research even while living in exile from Gnomeregan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance operatives moving between Ironforge and expedition outposts in Kalimdor often handle sensitive munitions and volatile formulas on Lomac's behalf."},kw={"an old colleague","gnome engineer","ineptitude + chemicals = fun","ironforge","lomac gearstrip","ng-5 explosive","stonetalon","tinker town"},rel={"subzone:tinker-town","zone:ironforge","quest:1072","quest:1073","zone:stonetalon","topic:gnome"},src={"Lomac Gearstrip"}}
E["npc:maggran-earthbinder"] = {t="npc",n="Maggran Earthbinder",z="stonetalon",s="Maggran Earthbinder is a grizzled tauren veteran appointed by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof to lead the Horde encampment at Sun Rock Retreat. Hardened by a lifetime of brutal conflict, he oversees the defense of the craggy valleys of Stonetalon against ravenous beasts and aggressive harpy covens. Though wearied by countless battles, he remains a steadfast guardian of the settlement.",h="Maggran Earthbinder is a grizzled tauren veteran appointed by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof to lead the...",sec={{t="A Veteran's Haven",b="Maggran Earthbinder was sent into the Stonetalon Mountains by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof himself. A veteran of countless skirmishes and bloody campaigns, Maggran admits that age and violence have hardened his heart, stripping away the natural gentleness typical of his people. Sun Rock Retreat was meant to be both an outpost under his steady command and a place of respite, where warm winds and mountain sunshine might soothe his battle-worn spirit.",sp=0},{t="Threats in the Crags",b="Even in Stonetalon, Maggran finds little peace. As overseer of Sun Rock Retreat, he coordinates defense efforts against the Bloodfury harpies nesting in the peaks and marshals fighters to counter predatory perils across the crags. Having once survived an ambush by the giant spider Besseleth himself, Maggran holds no illusions about the deadly wilderness around them and frequently enlists travelers to eliminate deadly regional predators before they overrun the outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Maggran Earthbinder?",a="Maggran Earthbinder is the commanding tauren elder at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Hardened by countless battles, he was stationed here by Cairne Bloodhoof to watch over the settlement and keep its supply roads and borders secure.",al={"maggran","who is maggran","sun rock retreat leader"}},{q="Why was Maggran sent to Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Cairne Bloodhoof appointed him to lead Sun Rock Retreat partly for his seasoned military leadership and partly as a retreat. Maggran's body and soul have been heavily worn by a lifetime of combat, and the quiet mountain sun offers him a measure of healing.",al={"why is maggran here","maggran background","cairne and maggran"}},{q="What threats does Maggran ask adventurers to deal with?",a="Maggran directs defense efforts against the savage Bloodfury harpies infesting the mountains and sends warriors to eliminate the giant spider matriarch Besseleth, a terrifying predator he narrowly escaped earlier in his travels.",al={"maggran quests","what does maggran want","harpies stonetalon"}},{q="What happened between Maggran and Besseleth?",a="Maggran was previously ambushed and ensnared by the colossal spider Besseleth. Though he managed to break free and escape with his life, he sends capable adventurers to slay the beast so no one else falls victim to her web.",al={"maggran besseleth","spider quest maggran","arachnophobia lore"}},{q="Does Maggran have a role in Thunder Bluff?",a="Maggran serves directly at the behest of Thunder Bluff's High Chieftain, Cairne Bloodhoof. While stationed out in the field at Sun Rock Retreat, his authority and orders stem straight from the capital.",al={"maggran thunder bluff","maggran cairne"}},{q="Is Maggran Earthbinder friendly to Alliance players?",a="No. Maggran is a staunch leader of the Horde and remains fully hostile to any Alliance adventurers who stumble into Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"can alliance talk to maggran","maggran hostile"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Maggran embodies the heavy toll warfare takes on the shu'halo spirit, serving as a reminder of how conflict can harden even the most grounded children of the Earth Mother.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers navigating the steep climbs of Stonetalon, Maggran is the primary authority coordinating local Horde patrols and keeping supply routes clear of beasts and harpies."},kw={"besseleth","bloodfury","cairne bloodhoof","earthbinder","harpies","maggran","stonetalon","sun rock retreat"},rel={"subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6284","quest:6282","quest:6283","quest:5881","topic:tauren","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Maggran Earthbinder"}}
E["npc:makaba-flathoof"] = {t="npc",n="Makaba Flathoof",z="stonetalon",s="Makaba Flathoof is a tauren survivor hailing from Camp Aparaje in the Stonetalon Mountains. Having witnessed the devastation of his home and people at the hands of the Grimtotem clan, he seeks brave champions of the Horde to bring vengeance upon the attackers and ensure his family's safety.",h="Makaba Flathoof is a tauren survivor hailing from Camp Aparaje in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Tragedy at Camp Aparaje",b="Makaba Flathoof represents the tragic toll of internal strife among the tauren. His home, Camp Aparaje in the Stonetalon Mountains, fell victim to a ruthless surprise attack by the Grimtotem clan. While many tauren strive for peace and unity under the leadership of Cairne Bloodhoof, the treacherous Grimtotem continually sow discord and violence, leaving survivors like Makaba displaced and grieving.",sp=0},{t="A Plea for Vengeance",b="Unable to retake his fallen settlement alone, Makaba calls upon travelers of the Horde to strike back. He directs fierce retaliation against the Grimtotem renegades who overran his home, demanding justice for the slaughter of his kin. His most urgent concerns center on confronting the warlord responsible, Grundig Darkcloud, and finding word of his missing family member, Kaya.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Makaba Flathoof?",a="Makaba Flathoof is a tauren refugee from Camp Aparaje in the Stonetalon Mountains. His village was overrun and sacked by the Grimtotem clan, driving him to seek help from Horde adventurers.",al={"makaba","who is makaba flathoof","makaba flathoof lore"}},{q="Where did Makaba come from?",a="Makaba hails from Camp Aparaje, a small tauren settlement located in the Stonetalon Mountains that was attacked and devastated by the Grimtotem.",al={"makaba origin","where is makaba from","camp aparaje makaba"}},{q="Who attacked Makaba's village?",a="Camp Aparaje was sacked by the Grimtotem clan, an aggressive and treacherous faction of tauren led locally by figures like Grundig Darkcloud.",al={"who attacked camp aparaje","makaba enemies","who sacked aparaje"}},{q="What does Makaba want Horde adventurers to do?",a="Makaba seeks vengeance for his fallen home, asking capable warriors to cut down the Grimtotem forces at Camp Aparaje, eliminate their leader Grundig Darkcloud, and discover the fate of Kaya Flathoof.",al={"makaba quests","what does makaba ask for","makaba tasks"}},{q="Who is Kaya to Makaba?",a="Kaya Flathoof is a relative of Makaba who went missing during the attack on Camp Aparaje. Makaba desperately hopes to learn if she survived the assault.",al={"kaya flathoof","who is kaya","makaba relative kaya"}},{q="Is Makaba related to Dim Flathoof?",a="Both Makaba and Dim share the Flathoof family surname, indicating they are part of the same tauren lineage, though their specific degree of relation is not deeply detailed.",al={"dim flathoof","makaba and dim","flathoof family"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren heroes, Makaba's plight highlights the bitter treachery of the Grimtotem, serving as a reminder that not all of their kin honor the ways of peace and unity.",["faction:Horde"]="Makaba's calls for aid allow Horde champions to prove their loyalty to their tauren allies by punishing those who butcher peaceful encampments."},kw={"camp aparaje","flathoof","grimtotem","grundig darkcloud","kaya","makaba","stonetalon"},rel={"subzone:camp-aparaje","quest:6548","quest:6629","quest:6523","quest:6401","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren"},src={"Makaba Flathoof"}}
E["npc:master-thal-darah"] = {t="npc",n="Master Thal'darah",z="stonetalon",s="Master Thal'darah is a respected night elf mentor stationed in the heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. Dedicated to instructing and guiding young druids, he watches over the forest haven that bears his name. With growing hostility and encroachment from the Horde threatening the region, he stands vigilant to protect his students and the natural order.",h="Master Thal'darah is a respected night elf mentor stationed in the heights of the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Young",b="Adorned in ceremonial Cenarion robes with leaves woven neatly into his beard, Master Thal'darah serves as a senior instructor for novice druids learning the ways of the wild in Stonetalon. From the vantage of the overlook, he watches the tranquil Thal'darah Grove nestled below. Rather than seeking conflict, his primary responsibility lies in nurturing the next generation of Cenarion practitioners and maintaining harmony across the mountain sanctuary.",sp=0},{t="Under the Shadow of Conflict",b="The mounting friction between the night elves and the Horde throughout Stonetalon places the grove directly in harm's way. Thal'darah harbors a profound distrust and bitterness toward the Horde's expansion, knowing well the vulnerability of the uninitiated apprentices under his charge. As threats draw closer, he depends on traveling Alliance allies to keep watch and defend the sanctuary against encroaching forces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Thal'darah?",a="Master Thal'darah is a senior night elf druid located at Thal'darah Overlook in the Stonetalon Mountains. He acts as an instructor and guardian for young druid novices training in the nearby grove.",al={"who is thaldarah","thaldarah lore","who is master thal'darah"}},{q="What is his connection to Thal'darah Grove?",a="The serene grove nestled below the overlook bears his name, functioning as a tranquil training ground where he mentors uninitiated night elf druids in the mysteries of nature.",al={"why is grove named after him","thal'darah grove","thaldarah grove connection"}},{q="Why does Thal'darah distrust the Horde?",a="Thal'darah views the aggressive logging and territorial expansion of the Horde into the Stonetalon Mountains as a direct threat to the fragile balance of nature and the lives of the young druids under his protection.",al={"why does thaldarah hate horde","thaldarah horde conflict"}},{q="What faction does he belong to?",a="While clad in Cenarion robes and focused on the sacred druidic mission, Master Thal'darah is closely aligned with the Alliance, relying on Alliance travelers to help secure his students and resist enemy incursions.",al={"is thaldarah alliance","cenarion or alliance"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids walking the Cenarion path, Thal'darah embodies the solemn duty of passing the teachings of the wild down to the next generation amidst a turbulent world.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance champions traversing Stonetalon find in Thal'darah an esteemed elder in desperate need of aid to preserve the lives of defenseless Kaldorei novices."},kw={"cenarion","druid","master thal'darah","stonetalon","thal'darah","thal'darah grove","thal'darah overlook"},rel={"subzone:thal-darah-overlook","subzone:thal-darah-grove","zone:stonetalon","topic:druid","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Master Thal'darah"}}
E["npc:mor-rogal"] = {t="npc",n="Mor'rogal",z="stonetalon",s="Mor'rogal is a tauren resident of Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. He serves as an advisor and guide for travelers seeking glory and peril within the rugged subterranean reaches of the crags.",h="Mor'rogal is a tauren resident of Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Watcher in the Crags",b="Perched within the refuge of Sun Rock Retreat, Mor'rogal takes a keen interest in the deep crevices and caverns that cut through the Stonetalon Mountains. Recognizing that the region's twisting subterranean passes offer both great riches and lethal danger, he directs brave Horde wanderers to investigate troubled areas like the Boulderslide Ravine. For Mor'rogal, delving into these treacherous depths is not merely a matter of survival, but a test of spirit for those who follow their heart and soul in search of glory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mor'rogal?",a="Mor'rogal is a tauren quest giver residing in Sun Rock Retreat within the Stonetalon Mountains. He acts as a local guide, urging Horde adventurers to test their mettle in the dangerous caves and ravines scattered across the craggy mountain range.",al={"morrogal","who is mor'rogal","mor rogal lore"}},{q="Where can I find Mor'rogal?",a="He can be found standing in Sun Rock Retreat, the primary Horde outpost situated around the peaceful mountain lake in the central Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"mor'rogal location","where is mor'rogal","morrogal spot"}},{q="What tasks does Mor'rogal offer?",a="Mor'rogal enlists capable champions to venture into Boulderslide Ravine to deal with the hostile elementals and troggs stirring in the rocky defiles.",al={"mor'rogal quests","what does mor'rogal want"}},{q="Why is Mor'rogal focused on caves and ravines?",a="Mor'rogal believes that the perilous subterranean caverns of Stonetalon hold true adventures and tests of spiritual resolve, offering glory and riches to those willing to risk their lives.",al={"why caves","mor'rogal caves"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Mor'rogal embodies the tauren respect for physical and spiritual testing, viewing the deep stone hollows of Kalimdor as sacred ground to prove one's worth.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers reaching the haven of Sun Rock Retreat, Mor'rogal provides crucial intelligence on the threats lurking in the crags beyond the settlement's borders."},kw={"boulderslide ravine","earthen arise","mor'rogal","morrogal","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tauren"},rel={"subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6421","quest:6481","topic:tauren","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Mor'rogal"}}
E["npc:overlord-krom-gar"] = {t="npc",n="Overlord Krom'gar",z="stonetalon",s="Overlord Krom'gar is an aggressive orc commander seeking to claim total control over the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains. Representing hardline Horde expansionism, he advocates for the decisive expulsion of Alliance presence from the region.",h="Overlord Krom'gar is an aggressive orc commander seeking to claim total control over the crags of the...",sec={{t="Horde Expansion in Stonetalon",b="Within the rocky passes of the Stonetalon Mountains, Overlord Krom'gar champions aggressive military action to secure Kalimdor for the Horde. Uncompromising in his ambition, Krom'gar believes that securing the peaks against night elven and Alliance outposts requires overwhelming force and steadfast discipline among the ranks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Overlord Krom'gar?",a="Overlord Krom'gar is an uncompromising orc commander dedicated to securing Horde dominance across the peaks of Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who is kromgar","kromgar lore","overlord kromgar"}},{q="What is his role in Stonetalon?",a="He commands forward Horde forces in the region, focusing on driving out Alliance presence and expanding Horde territory through aggressive military mobilization.",al={"what does kromgar want","kromgar stonetalon goal"}},{q="Who serves alongside him?",a="General Grebo serves as his second-in-command, helping oversee the soldiers under Krom'gar's leadership.",al={"kromgar second in command","general grebo"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde warriors, Krom'gar represents an aggressive vision of territorial expansion that demands unwavering loyalty and ruthlessness against encroaching enemies.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs fighting in Stonetalon encounter in Krom'gar a fierce dedication to martial strength and total dominance over the wilderness."},kw={"grebo","horde","krom'gar","kromgar","orcs","overlord","stonetalon"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","npc:general-grebo","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Overlord Krom'gar"}}
E["npc:piznik"] = {t="npc",n="Piznik",z="stonetalon",s="Piznik is a disgruntled goblin surveyor hiding deep within Windshear Mine in the Stonetalon Mountains. Once a high-ranking overseer in the local Venture Company operations, he was sidelined by the ruthless Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle. Now nurseing a grudge, Piznik secretly gathers intel to undermine his former workplace.",h="Piznik is a disgruntled goblin surveyor hiding deep within Windshear Mine in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Fallen from Grace",b="Before Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle seized supreme authority over Windshear Crag, Piznik held the enviable title of second-in-command across the entire operation. However, corporate restructuring in the Venture Company is unforgiving. Once Gerenzo took full control, Piznik found himself pushed aside and relegated to the murky depths of Windshear Mine. Rather than accepting his demotion quietly, Piznik bides his time underground, keeping a watchful eye on mine movements and quietly plotting revenge against the boss who demoted him.",sp=0},{t="Corporate Espionage",b="Piznik's quiet rebellion took a practical turn through an alliance with Ziz Fizziks, an operative stationed outside who was similarly cast out by Gerenzo. Operating as Ziz's inside man, Piznik collects sensitive corporate correspondence and operational directives. By intercepting Gerenzo's personal orders and passing them along to adventurers, Piznik works to disrupt the Venture Company's deforestation and mining efforts from the shadows, ensuring that Gerenzo's ambitious leadership faces constant, agonizing setbacks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Piznik?",a="Piznik is tucked away inside Windshear Mine, a cavern complex carved into the slopes of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. You will find him deep within the tunnels surrounded by Venture Company workers.",al={"piznik location","where is piznik","find piznik stonetalon"}},{q="What is Piznik's grudge against Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle?",a="Piznik was formerly the second-highest authority in Windshear Crag. When Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle took total command of the logging and mining project, he demoted Piznik, leaving the former supervisor resentful and eager to see Gerenzo ruined.",al={"why does piznik hate gerenzo","piznik gerenzo feud"}},{q="How does Piznik fit into Ziz Fizziks' plans?",a="Ziz Fizziks was fired outright by Gerenzo, whereas Piznik was merely demoted. Piznik uses his remaining access deep inside Windshear Mine to act as an informant, securing Gerenzo's written directives and passing them to Ziz to thwart the Crag's leadership.",al={"piznik and ziz","who does piznik work with"}},{q="Is Piznik still loyal to the Venture Company?",a="Only on paper. While he still wears the mantle of a Venture Company employee to remain within the mine, Piznik's true allegiance is entirely to his own self-interest and his desire to sabotage Gerenzo.",al={"is piznik venture co","piznik faction"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners traversing Windshear Mine will cross paths with Piznik, a living example of how rapidly organizational rank can plummet beneath the weight of corporate greed."},kw={"gerenzo wrenchwhistle","piznik","stonetalon","venture co","windshear crag","windshear mine","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1090","quest:1096","quest:1483","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","topic:goblin"},src={"Piznik"}}
E["npc:sentinel-thenysil"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Thenysil",z="stonetalon",s="Sentinel Tara Thenysil is a night elf sentinel stationed in Astranaar within the ancient forest of Ashenvale. Vigilant over the surrounding wilderness, she keeps close tabs on military operations in the region and coordinates scouts watching neighboring territories. Her attention is particularly focused on allied movements pushing south into the contested Stonetalon Mountains.",h="Sentinel Tara Thenysil is a night elf sentinel stationed in Astranaar within the ancient forest of Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Watching the Borders",b="From her post in the fortified settlement of Astranaar, Sentinel Thenysil helps secure Ashenvale against growing hostility. Night elf holdings throughout the region face relentless encroachment, making communications between distant outposts vital. While much of the local garrison focuses directly on defending the forest road, Thenysil directs Alliance volunteers beyond Ashenvale's borders to ensure distant allies remain supported.",sp=0},{t="Ties to Stonetalon",b="Thenysil maintains a close personal and military friendship with Kaela Shadowspear, an operative deployed south into the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains. Learning that Kaela was dispatched alongside an eccentric gnome mage, Thenysil considered the unorthodox pairing an unmistakable sign of serious trouble brewing in the peaks. Wary of what dangers her comrade might face, she recruits capable adventurers to journey south, deliver support, and report on the unfolding mission.",sp=0},{t="Audience in the Canopy",b="When scouts return from Stonetalon with word of successful strikes against the defiling Venture Company, Thenysil ensures their deeds do not go unnoticed. Recognizing that repelling mechanized exploitation in the mountains protects the sanctity of all neighboring wilds, she grants reliable heroes a formal commendation. Rather than hoarding credit in Astranaar, she directs them up to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus for a personal reception before High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Sentinel Thenysil be found?",a="Sentinel Thenysil is stationed in Astranaar, the primary night elf stronghold located along the central road in Ashenvale.",al={"thenysil location","where is sentinel thenysil","thenysil astranaar"}},{q="Why does Thenysil send travelers to Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Her friend, Kaela Shadowspear, was deployed to Stonetalon alongside a gnome mage. Viewing that unusual assignment as an omen of dangerous trouble, Thenysil sends dependable adventurers to reinforce Kaela's mission.",al={"why stonetalon","thenysil quest stonetalon","on guard in stonetalon why"}},{q="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf scout and a close friend of Sentinel Thenysil. She is stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains investigating threats to the land.",al={"who is kaela","kaela shadowspear relation","thenysil friend"}},{q="What threats are being fought in Stonetalon?",a="Beyond skirmishes with local adversaries, the Venture Company has established invasive, destructive industrial operations in the Stonetalon Mountains, strip-mining and deforesting the landscape.",al={"stonetalon threat","what is happening in stonetalon","venture co stonetalon"}},{q="Why does Thenysil send adventurers to Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="After adventurers successfully assist Kaela Shadowspear in halting the Venture Company's schemes in Stonetalon, Thenysil sends them to Darnassus so that High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind can personally acknowledge their service to the night elves.",al={"reception from tyrande","why see tyrande","thenysil darnassus referral"},sp=1},{q="What is Sentinel Thenysil's role in Astranaar?",a="She serves as a sentinel coordinator in Astranaar, helping organize regional intelligence, monitor borders, and dispatch reliable Alliance recruits to support distant garrisons.",al={"thenysil rank","what does thenysil do","sentinel thenysil duties"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Thenysil represents the diligent watch of the Sentinels, working tirelessly to shield Kalimdor's sacred groves and keep allied operatives safe across border frontiers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Serving as an early bridge between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains, Thenysil provides Alliance adventurers an opportunity to earn direct favor with the leadership in Darnassus.",["race:Gnome"]="Thenysil finds the deployment of an alliance gnome mage to Stonetalon to be an unusual and alarming sign, highlighting how curious night elves still find their diminutive allies."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","kaela shadowspear","sentinels","stonetalon","tara thenysil","thenysil","tyrande whisperwind"},rel={"subzone:astranaar","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:1070","quest:1082","quest:1081","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","npc:tyrande-whisperwind"},src={"Sentinel Thenysil"}}
E["npc:tammra-windfield"] = {t="npc",n="Tammra Windfield",z="stonetalon",s="Tammra Windfield is a tauren resident of Sun Rock Retreat, nestled within the heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. Deeply attuned to the balance of the land, she guides Horde travelers in honoring the natural cycle of renewal and keeping hope alive amid the peaks. Her concerns lie with both the health of the untamed wilderness and the safety of her kin.",h="Tammra Windfield is a tauren resident of Sun Rock Retreat, nestled within the heights of the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Warden of Sun Rock",b="Sun Rock Retreat serves as a vital sanctuary for the Horde within the craggy peaks of Stonetalon, surrounded by hostile harpies, Venture Company loggers, and lurking predators. Tammra Windfield stands among the settlement's caretakers, keeping a watchful eye on both the mountain wilderness and travelers who cross its threshold. Her gentle demeanor belies the resolve necessary to maintain a home in such rugged terrain.",sp=0},{t="Nurturing the Land",b="Like many of her people, Tammra honors the Earth Mother by observing the constant rhythm of growth and decay in nature. Through the tasks she entrusts to travelers—such as tending the cycle of rebirth and bringing forth new life—she works to counter the ravages that conflict and exploitation bring upon Stonetalon. To Tammra, protecting the land requires active healing, ensuring that life flourishes even in scarred mountain soil.",sp=0},{t="Kinship and Vigilance",b="Beyond her spiritual duties to the surrounding wild, Tammra bears deep concern for the companions and kin who brave the treacherous trails of the Stonetalon Mountains. When word spreads that travelers or family have vanished along the crags, she is among the first to seek out reliable aid. For Tammra, the endurance of Sun Rock Retreat depends as much on mutual protection and loyalty as it does on harmony with nature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tammra Windfield?",a="Tammra Windfield is a tauren quest giver residing at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. She is dedicated to the well-being of the settlement, the natural cycle of the mountain landscape, and the survival of her fellow travelers.",al={"who is tammra","tammra windfield","sun rock retreat tammra"}},{q="Where can I find Tammra Windfield?",a="She is located inside Sun Rock Retreat, the Horde encampment tucked away in the western heights of the Stonetalon Mountains, accessed via a mountain trail branching off the main valley road.",al={"tammra windfield location","where is tammra","find tammra windfield"}},{q="What quests does Tammra offer?",a="Tammra is involved in tasks focusing on renewal and the welfare of her kin, including 'Cycle of Rebirth' and 'New Life', and she receives travelers reporting on the survival of kin in 'Kaya's Alive'.",al={"tammra quests","tammra windfield quest list"}},{q="What is Tammra's role in Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Tammra acts as a community anchor and spiritual caretaker, directing adventurers to restore vitality to the surrounding wilderness and tending to the bonds that keep the remote outpost safe.",al={"what does tammra do","tammra role"}},{q="Why does Tammra care about the natural cycle?",a="In tauren culture, maintaining balance requires nurturing the Earth Mother's cycles of death and regeneration. With outside forces and mountain beasts threatening the region, Tammra seeks to cultivate new life to heal the bruised wilderness.",al={"cycle of rebirth lore","why rebirth stonetalon"}},{q="Is Tammra friendly to Alliance players?",a="No. Sun Rock Retreat is a dedicated Horde outpost, and Tammra is aligned with Thunder Bluff and the Horde, making her hostile to Alliance intruders.",al={"is tammra hostile","can alliance talk to tammra"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Tammra exemplifies the tauren commitment to the Earth Mother, demonstrating how spiritual reverence translates into real-world restoration even far from Mulgore.",["class:Druid"]="Her emphasis on the cycle of rebirth and cultivating new life mirrors the central tenets of druidism, making her requests deeply resonant with caretakers of the wild.",["faction:Horde"]="In the contested territory of Stonetalon, Tammra helps maintain Sun Rock Retreat as a secure, enduring foothold for Horde travelers."},kw={"cycle of rebirth","kaya","new life","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tammra","tauren","windfield"},rel={"subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6301","quest:6381","quest:6401","topic:tauren","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Tammra Windfield"}}
E["npc:tyrande-whisperwind"] = {t="npc",n="Tyrande Whisperwind",z="stonetalon",s="Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of Elune and the supreme leader of the night elves. Alongside her beloved, the Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage, she guided her people through the cataclysmic War of the Ancients and ten millennia of the Long Vigil. Now governing from the sacred boughs of Teldrassil, she commands the Sisterhood of Elune and directs the Sentinel army in defense of Kalimdor's sacred wilderness.",h="Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of Elune and the supreme leader of the night elves.",sec={{t="Chosen of the Moon Goddess",b="Born in the ancient city of Suramar, Tyrande grew up alongside the twin brothers Malfurion and Illidan Stormrage. While the brothers followed druidism and sorcery, Tyrande entered the service of Elune as a novice in the sisterhood. When the demonic Burning Legion first invaded Azeroth during the War of the Ancients, the dying High Priestess Dejahna chose Tyrande as her successor. Blessed with direct favor from the Moon Goddess, Tyrande transformed the Sisterhood into a radiant fighting force, wielding both divine restoration and searing lunar wrath to deliver her people from the brink of total annihilation.",sp=0},{t="The Long Vigil and the Sentinels",b="Following the Great Sundering and the sealing of the Well of Eternity, Malfurion and the druids entered the Emerald Dream for deep, prolonged hibernations. Tyrande took upon herself the lonely burden of defending their recovering realm. She organized the Sentinels—an elite cadre of warrior-women who patrolled Kalimdor's forests for ten thousand years. Throughout this Long Vigil, she stood watchful guard over ancient evils and lingering demonic remnants, maintaining unbroken faith in Elune while she waited centuries between brief reunions with Malfurion.",sp=0},{t="The Third War and a New Haven",b="When the Burning Legion returned during the Third War, Tyrande acted decisively to wake the sleeping druids and face the catastrophic threat. Overcoming fierce mistrust toward the newly arrived orcs and humans, she helped forge the desperate coalition at Mount Hyjal, sacrificing the night elves' immortality atop Nordrassil to shatter Archimonde. With Mount Hyjal scarred and Malfurion once again occupied with safeguarding the Emerald Dream, Tyrande governs the kaldorei from the grand Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, watching cautiously over both Horde incursions and the growing Alliance alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of Elune and the supreme spiritual and political leader of the night elves. She has guided her people for over ten thousand years from the War of the Ancients through the Third War, and currently leads the kaldorei from the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"who is tyrande","tyrande whisperwind lore","night elf leader"}},{q="Where does Tyrande reside right now?",a="Tyrande resides in the capital city of Darnassus, situated high in the branches of the world tree Teldrassil. She presides from the upper sanctuary of the Temple of the Moon, surrounded by the Priestesses of Elune and Sentinel guards.",al={"where is tyrande","tyrande location","where to find tyrande"}},{q="What is the relationship between Tyrande and Malfurion?",a="Tyrande and Malfurion Stormrage are lifelong partners who have guided the night elf civilization together for ten millennia. Though both Malfurion and his twin brother Illidan sought her love in their youth, Tyrande chose Malfurion, whose deep devotion to balance and nature mirrored her faith in Elune.",al={"tyrande malfurion","is tyrande married","tyrande and illidan"}},{q="What is the Sisterhood of Elune?",a="The Sisterhood of Elune is the ancient religious order of night elf priestesses dedicated to worshiping the Moon Goddess. Under Tyrande's leadership as High Priestess, the sisters serve not only as healers and spiritual guides, but also as fierce martial commanders and combatants.",al={"sisterhood of elune","priestesses of elune","tyrande priests"}},{q="What role did Tyrande play in the Long Vigil?",a="During the ten thousand years after the Sundering, while Malfurion and the male druids slumbered in the Emerald Dream, Tyrande established and commanded the Sentinels. She patrolled the wilds of Kalimdor, hunted remaining satyrs and demons, and kept her people safe in isolation.",al={"what was the long vigil","tyrande long vigil","sentinel leader"}},{q="Why is Tyrande wary of the Horde?",a="During the Third War, the orcs entered Ashenvale and began clear-cutting sacred forests, slaying the demigod Cenarius under the influence of demon blood. While an uneasy truce was struck at Mount Hyjal, the Horde's ongoing logging operations in Ashenvale ensure Tyrande keeps her Sentinels on high alert.",al={"tyrande horde","why does tyrande hate orcs","night elves vs horde"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Tyrande is your supreme leader and High Priestess. For over ten thousand years, she has kept vigil over your race, championing the light of Elune through every trial.",["class:Priest"]="As the living vessel of Elune's divine favor, Tyrande embodies the pinnacle of kaldorei priesthood, calling down lunar stars and mending wounds through pure faith.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though historically reclusive and fiercely independent, Tyrande leads the night elves within the Alliance to secure mutual defense against Kalimdor's growing perils.",["class:Druid"]="While Malfurion slumbers in the Emerald Dream, Tyrande coordinates closely with the Cenarion Circle to protect sacred groves and nurture Teldrassil.",["faction:Horde"]="To the Horde, Tyrande is a formidable, uncompromising adversary who has commanded the Sentinels to violently resist resource harvesting across Ashenvale."},kw={"darnassus","elune","kaldorei","malfurion","priestess","sentinels","teldrassil","tyrande","whisperwind"},rel={"npc:malfurion-stormrage","npc:shandris-feathermoon","quest:940","topic:night-elf","topic:elune","topic:sentinels","topic:war-of-the-ancients","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Tyrande Whisperwind"}}
E["npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil"] = {t="npc",n="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil",z="stonetalon",s="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is a Darkspear troll mystic dwelling in a cave at Malaka'jin in the southern Stonetalon Mountains. A longtime comrade of Darsok Swiftdagger and the shadow hunter Rokhan, he turns dark voodoo and ritual sorcery against the Horde's local enemies.",h="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is a Darkspear troll mystic dwelling in a cave at Malaka'jin in the southern Stonetalon...",sec={{t="The Hermit of Malaka'jin",b="Secluded inside an eastern cavern above the camp of Malaka'jin, Jin'Zil practices ancient jungle troll arts away from the coastal home of his tribe. Surrounded by bubbling cauldrons and captive prisoners, he gathers exotic reagents from the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains—such as ram horns, resonite crystals, and fierce stormer hearts—to weave potent blessings and curses in defense of the Horde's mountain encampment.",sp=0},{t="A Trusted Veteran",b="Jin'Zil is no ordinary hedge wizard; he shares a storied history with senior Horde scouts, counting both Darsok Swiftdagger and the renowned shadow hunter Rokhan among his old friends. While Darsok coordinates frontline skirmishes against night elves and harpies, Jin'Zil fights the war spiritually and alchemically, using his forest magic and volatile voodoo to undermine threats before they ever reach the camp gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?",a="He resides inside a cave on the eastern side of Malaka'jin, a Horde settlement nestled in the southern pass of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"jin'zil location","where is jinzil","jinzil cave"}},{q="What is Jin'Zil's connection to Rokhan and Darsok Swiftdagger?",a="Jin'Zil is an old, trusted friend to both Darsok Swiftdagger and the shadow hunter Rokhan. Because of these long-standing ties, scouts throughout Stonetalon rely on his magical expertise when dealing with unusual threats.",al={"jin'zil friends","darsok and jinzil","rokhan connection"}},{q="Why does Jin'Zil have prisoners in his cave?",a="Jin'Zil keeps captive enemies caged within his cavern workshop. As a traditional witch doctor, he employs captives and raw reagents to test curses, divine portents, and craft defensive voodoo for the settlement.",al={"prisoners of jinzil","jinzil cages","why does jinzil have captives"}},{q="What kind of tasks does he give to Horde adventurers?",a="He sends travelers across Stonetalon to collect mystical components, including creature organs, ram horns, and resonite crystals, using them to concoct defensive wards and powerful blessings for the war effort.",al={"jinzil quests","what does jinzil want"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Jin'Zil represents traditional Darkspear witch doctor practices transplanted into the rugged wilderness of Kalimdor, maintaining deep ties to prominent figures like Rokhan.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde secures Stonetalon's southern paths, Jin'Zil provides essential occult defense and intelligence support alongside the outpost's scouts."},kw={"darsok","jin'zil","jinzil","malaka'jin","rokhan","stonetalon","voodoo","witch doctor"},rel={"subzone:malaka-jin","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","quest:1058","quest:1060","zone:stonetalon","topic:troll"},src={"Witch Doctor Jin'Zil"}}
E["quest:1057"] = {t="quest",n="Reclaiming the Charred Vale",z="stonetalon",s="Reclaiming the Charred Vale is an Alliance quest offered by Keeper Albagorm atop Stonetalon Peak. It charges adventurers with culling the aggressive Bloodfury harpies who occupy the ruined valley of the Charred Vale, clearing a path so druids and caretakers can begin healing the scorched landscape.",h="Reclaiming the Charred Vale is an Alliance quest offered by Keeper Albagorm atop Stonetalon Peak.",sec={{t="The Wounded Valley",b="To the south of Stonetalon Peak lies the Charred Vale, a once-lush alpine haven reduced to ash and smoldering ruins. The devastation began when a mechanized logging and mining army swept through the sacred crags, stripping trees and fueling uncontrolled blazes. For the guardians stationed around Stonetalon, watching ancient woodland succumb to industrial greed is an intolerable wound upon the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="The Harpy Menace",b="While mechanical fires sparked the ruin, an opportunistic infestation took root in the ashes. The vicious Bloodfury harpies swarmed into the smoking lowlands, establishing nests and aggressively ambushing anyone approaching the valley. Keeper Albagorm and his allies cannot even walk the soil to sow the seeds of renewal, as the Bloodfuries violently refuse passage to all outsiders.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Path to Renewal",b="Before any meaningful restoration can take place, the roosts of the Bloodfury tribe must be broken. Albagorm tasks seasoned Alliance fighters with carving deep into their numbers—slaying hunters, ambushers, and roguefeathers alike. Thinning their predatory flocks is the vital first step toward reclaiming what belongs to nature and giving the forest spirits room to breathe once more.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Charred Vale?",a="The Charred Vale is a valley nestled in the southwestern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. Once a lush, verdant forest, it was consumed by fire and scorched to bedrock during the unchecked exploitation of the land by industrial logging forces.",al={"charred vale lore","what happened to charred vale","why is it burned"}},{q="Who is Keeper Albagorm?",a="Keeper Albagorm is a woodland keeper and caretaker residing at the Alliance settlement on Stonetalon Peak. As a protector of nature and forest spirits, he dedicates himself to curbing desolation in the mountains and driving back encroaching beasts.",al={"keeper albagorm","who gives reclaiming the charred vale","albagorm lore"}},{q="Why are harpies living in the Charred Vale?",a="The Bloodfury harpies are aggressive, opportunistic scavengers who thrive in disrupted and blighted territory. When fire leveled the valley, the flock moved in to dominate the desolate basin, attacking anyone attempting to enter.",al={"bloodfury harpies","why harpies here","bloodfuries in stonetalon"}},{q="Who set fire to the Charred Vale in the first place?",a="Keeper Albagorm identifies the culprits as a greedy mechanized army of industrialists who tore into the hills. Unchecked logging machinery and explosive expansion caused devastating blazes that consumed the woodland.",al={"who burned charred vale","mechanized army industrialists","venture company charred vale"}},{q="What must be done after thinning the harpies?",a="Clearing out the harpies is merely securing the perimeter. Once the Bloodfury numbers are curbed, Keeper Albagorm shifts focus toward planting seeds and channeling restorative magic to coax new life from the scorched soil.",al={"next quest charred vale","reclaiming the charred vale part 2","what happens next"},sp=1},{q="Is this quest available to Horde adventurers?",a="No. Keeper Albagorm operates out of the Alliance-aligned redoubt atop Stonetalon Peak, meaning this specific task to purge the Bloodfury harpies is restricted to Alliance heroes.",al={"can horde do this quest","horde reclaiming charred vale"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Night elves revere the wild forests of Stonetalon; purging the vile harpies from sacred groves defiled by foreign engines is an urgent calling.",["class:Druid"]="As stewards of the Cenarion circle and defenders of natural harmony, druids directly aid the Keepers in clearing out blighted nests to permit magical reforestation.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing the high passes and southern valleys protects the vulnerable night elf settlements and sanctuaries across Stonetalon Peak from predatory threats."},kw={"bloodfury","charred vale","harpies","keeper albagorm","reclaiming the charred vale","stonetalon","stonetalon peak"},rel={"subzone:charred-vale","subzone:stonetalon-peak","npc:keeper-albagorm","topic:harpy","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Keeper Albagorm",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1057},src={"Reclaiming the Charred Vale"}}
E["quest:1058"] = {t="quest",n="Jin'Zil's Forest Magic",z="stonetalon",s="At the small outpost of Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil has captured three night elven scouts in crude iron cages. Rather than executing them outright or holding them for ransom, the eccentric troll tasks Horde adventurers with gathering wilderness reagents from Stonetalon Peak to concoct a gruesome dose of 'forest magic.'",h="At the small outpost of Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil has captured three night elven scouts in crude iron...",sec={{t="A Bitter Brew",b="In the red-rock defile of Malaka'jin, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil conducts his craft under the watchful gaze of the Horde. When three night elf captives fall into his clutches, Jin'Zil decides against ordinary butchery, concocting instead a mocking ritual tailored specifically for his captive woodland foes. He directs travelers north into the untamed peaks to collect an array of indigenous parts: thick tree sap, feline whiskers from predatory twilight runners, a shimmering fey dragon scale, and scores of eyes plucked from the local forest coursers.",sp=0},{t="A Taste of Home",b="Behind Jin'Zil's playful demeanor lies a cruel troll sense of humor. Under the pretense of making the imprisoned elves 'feel right at home' without a forest to frolic in, the mixture of magical fauna and concentrated sap forms a lethal, volatile venom. When released within the cave, the noxious concoction chokes the life from the caged captives on the spot. As their physical bodies perish, the elves' ancestral spirits dissolve into luminous wisps that float out into the mountains, leaving their empty cages behind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is a Darkspear troll stationed at Malaka'jin in the southern Stonetalon Mountains. He serves the Horde war effort against the night elves by practicing traditional troll alchemy, voodoo, and interrogation.",al={"who is jin'zil","witch doctor jin'zil","jinzil lore"}},{q="Why does Jin'Zil want so many courser eyes?",a="Jin'Zil claims that you simply cannot brew fierce forest magic without an abundance of eyes. While troll witch doctors often utilize strange organic components in their potions, the absurd quantity also reflects his eccentric and vindictive personality.",al={"why courser eyes","30 courser eyes","why so many eyes"}},{q="What happens to the caged night elves when the quest finishes?",a="Upon delivering the reagents, Jin'Zil releases the toxic brew throughout his cave. The concoction lethally poisons the three captives, killing them and releasing their spirits as wisps that drift away into the wild.",al={"what happens to the elves","caged elves fate","prisoners of jin'zil"},sp=1},{q="Where are all these reagents found?",a="The courser eyes and Stonetalon sap can be gathered around Mirkfallon Lake and the northern highlands. The twilight whiskers and the rare fey dragon scale are found farther north near Stonetalon Peak, where the mountain's magical beasts roam.",al={"where to find forest magic reagents","stonetalon sap location","fey dragon scale spot"}},{q="Why is the Horde fighting night elves in Stonetalon?",a="The Horde's logging efforts in the region, centered near the lower crags and the borders of Ashenvale, have triggered fierce resistance from the Sentinels and druids guarding the sacred groves of Stonetalon.",al={"why fight night elves in stonetalon","horde night elf conflict stonetalon","stonetalon war"}},{q="Why do the dying elves turn into wisps?",a="Wisps are the spirits of deceased night elves who remain intimately bonded to nature. Upon death, their souls take on this glowing arboreal form rather than lingering as ordinary ghosts or shades.",al={"why do elves become wisps","elven wisps in cave","wisp lore"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Jin'Zil's macabre humor and practical application of voodoo alchemy are classic hallmarks of Darkspear witch doctor craft.",["race:NightElf"]="The agonizing execution of night elven captives through twisted woodland materials stands as one of the crueler Horde acts in Stonetalon.",["class:Druid"]="Seeing sacred fey drakes, majestic coursers, and ancient forest sap harvested to brew a lethal poison is a grim perversion of nature's balance.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Malaka'jin means subduing night elf resistance across the range, even through the unorthodox methods of a recluse witch doctor."},kw={"courser eye","fey dragon","forest magic","jin'zil","malaka'jin","prisoners","stonetalon","twilight runner","witch doctor"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1058},src={"Jin'Zil's Forest Magic"}}
E["quest:1059"] = {t="quest",n="Reclaiming the Charred Vale",z="stonetalon",s="Reclaiming the Charred Vale is a messenger quest tasked by Keeper Albagorm in Stonetalon Peak. Having temporarily suppressed the local harpies, Albagorm sends an Alliance traveler far south to Feralas to recruit the aid of the druid Falfindel Waywarder.",h="Reclaiming the Charred Vale is a messenger quest tasked by Keeper Albagorm in Stonetalon Peak.",sec={{t="The Scars of the Vale",b="The Charred Vale in southern Stonetalon Mountains remains an ash-choked reminder of catastrophic devastation. While Alliance forces under Keeper Albagorm have struck back against the rampant Bloodfury harpies nesting in the ruins, driving them off is merely a holding action. Albagorm recognizes that physical force alone cannot mend the ravaged earth before the harpies rally and reclaim their dominance.",sp=0},{t="A Plea to the South",b="To permanently restore the scorched lands, the grove tenders need mystical intervention beyond their current means. Albagorm dispatches a courier far to the south, skirting past the salt flats and canyons of Thousand Needles to Forest's Edge on the border of Feralas. There waits Falfindel Waywarder, a night elf druid reputed to possess the rare power to call forth primordial forest spirits capable of rejuvenating the dead soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Albagorm?",a="Keeper Albagorm is a night elf keeper stationed at Stonetalon Peak who oversees Alliance efforts to cleanse and restore the blighted Charred Vale.",al={"who is albagorm","keeper albagorm"}},{q="Where is Falfindel Waywarder located?",a="Falfindel Waywarder is stationed at the Forest's Edge, positioned on the western border where Thousand Needles transitions into the lush wilderness of Feralas.",al={"where is falfindel","falfindel waywarder location","find waywarder"}},{q="Why send for a druid all the way in Feralas?",a="Keeper Albagorm considers Falfindel uniquely capable of summoning powerful ancient forest spirits that can reverse the deep ecological devastation of the Charred Vale.",al={"why go to feralas","why falfindel"}},{q="What threat resides in the Charred Vale?",a="The valley is overrun by hostile Bloodfury harpies alongside fire elementals and wild beasts that thrived in the wake of the land's burning.",al={"charred vale enemies","what is attacking the vale"}},{q="Does this quest require combat?",a="No. The second part of Reclaiming the Charred Vale is purely an overland travel quest requiring you to deliver Albagorm's message across central and southern Kalimdor.",al={"is this quest hard","combat in charred vale quest"}},{q="How do you reach Thousand Needles from Stonetalon?",a="Travelers must journey east out of Stonetalon Mountains into the Barrens, head south along the Great Divide, descend the Great Lift into Thousand Needles, and continue west toward Feralas.",al={"how to get to thousand needles","travel route to feralas"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This mission highlights the Cenarion duty to reach beyond local garrisons and summon primal nature spirits to heal lands scarred by unnatural ruin.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance's foothold at Stonetalon Peak relies on connecting frontier outposts across vast, contested stretches of Kalimdor."},kw={"bloodfuries","charred vale","falfindel waywarder","feralas","forest's edge","keeper albagorm","stonetalon peak","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:1057","npc:keeper-albagorm","npc:falfindel-waywarder","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:forest-s-edge","zone:stonetalon","zone:feralas","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Keeper Albagorm",["end"]="Falfindel Waywarder",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1059},src={"Reclaiming the Charred Vale (2)"}}
E["quest:1060"] = {t="quest",n="Letter to Jin'Zil",z="stonetalon",s="Letter to Jin'Zil is a Horde delivery quest entrusted to adventurers who have slain Serena Bloodfeather in the northern Barrens. Orc rogue Darsok Swiftdagger sends you across the border into the rugged crags of Stonetalon Mountains to deliver word of the harpy matriarch's demise to his old friend, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil.",h="Letter to Jin'Zil is a Horde delivery quest entrusted to adventurers who have slain Serena Bloodfeather in...",sec={{t="A Message into the Mountains",b="After the harpy threat around the northern Barrens is systematically dismantled, Darsok Swiftdagger reveals that the winged raiders were never native to the scrublands. The Witchwing and Bloodfeather broods descended from the rugged ridges of the Stonetalon Mountains to the northwest. Impressed by your prowess in dispatching Serena Bloodfeather, Darsok sends you into those dangerous peaks to carry news of her death to an old acquaintance, Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, residing at the troll settlement of Malaka'jin.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Bloodfury Claws",b="Reaching Jin'Zil in his shaded cave reveals an older chapter of Horde history. Upon hearing that Serena Bloodfeather has fallen, the troll witch doctor recalls the earlier campaign when the scout Rokhan and the wandering Beastmaster Rexxar slew Serena's elder sister, Bloodfury. The eradication of Serena brings a sense of finality to the longstanding feud between the Horde's frontier outposts and the bloodthirsty harpies of Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Letter to Jin'Zil?",a="Darsok Swiftdagger gives the quest at the Far Watch Post in the northern Barrens. He offers it only after you complete the hunt for Serena Bloodfeather.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest","who starts letter to jin'zil"}},{q="Where can I find Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?",a="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil resides inside a cave at Malaka'jin, a Darkspear troll encampment located just off the main path entering the Stonetalon Mountains from the Barrens.",al={"where is jin'zil","jin'zil location","malaka'jin location"}},{q="Why does Darsok send you to Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Darsok wants to inform his old friend Jin'Zil that the harpy threat has been broken with Serena Bloodfeather's death, while also steering a capable adventurer toward the wider challenges awaiting the Horde in the Stonetalon peaks.",al={"why go to stonetalon","why darsok sends letter"}},{q="What previous sister of Serena is Jin'Zil referring to?",a="Jin'Zil mentions Bloodfury, an elder harpy who terrorized Kalimdor years earlier. She was slain by the Shadow Hunter Rokhan and the Mok'Nathal warrior Rexxar during their travels alongside the founding Horde.",al={"serena older sister","rokhan and rexxar harpy","bloodfury"}},{q="Is this quest part of a larger chain?",a="Yes. It serves as the conclusion to the northern Barrens harpy hunting chain, following Harpy Raiders, Harpy Lieutenants, and Serena Bloodfeather, while acting as a breadcrumb into the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"quest chain","prerequisites","what leads to this"}},{q="What faction can undertake this task?",a="This is strictly a Horde quest, as both Darsok Swiftdagger and Witch Doctor Jin'Zil serve the interests of the Horde frontier.",al={"is this horde only","can alliance do this quest"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Delivering this letter transitions Horde warriors from pacifying the internal trade routes of the Barrens into establishing footholds in the contentious Stonetalon Mountains.",["race:Troll"]="Jin'Zil's cave at Malaka'jin serves as a key spiritual and tactical outpost for Darkspear trolls seeking to secure the mountain approaches."},kw={"bloodfury","darsok swiftdagger","harpies","letter to jin'zil","malaka'jin","serena bloodfeather","stonetalon mountains","witch doctor jin'zil"},rel={"quest:876","npc:witch-doctor-jin-zil","npc:darsok-swiftdagger","subzone:malaka-jin","zone:stonetalon","quest:875","quest:867","zone:barrens"},m={start="Darsok Swiftdagger",["end"]="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1060},src={"Letter to Jin'Zil (quest)"}}
E["quest:1062"] = {t="quest",n="Goblin Invaders",z="stonetalon",s="Goblin Invaders is a Horde quest tasked by Seereth Stonebreak at the border between the Barrens and the Stonetalon Mountains. It directs warriors of the Horde into Windshear Crag to strike directly at the Venture Company loggers despoiling the region's ancient woodlands.",h="Goblin Invaders is a Horde quest tasked by Seereth Stonebreak at the border between the Barrens and the...",sec={{t="A Forest in Agony",b="The Venture Company has pushed deep into the Stonetalon Mountains, carving wide swaths of destruction through the crags and valleys. Their logging operations strip the hillsides of timber and set fire to underbrush, leaving behind smoldering scars. To the tauren and their allies, this is not merely an unsightly mining and lumber operation; the primal spirits bound to Stonetalon are howling in torment. Seereth Stonebreak, stationed along the mountain border, observes that these spirits have grown blind with agony and fury under the goblins' relentless assault.",sp=0},{t="The Language of Force",b="Appeals to reason or diplomacy mean nothing to the cutthroat executives and hirelings of the Venture Company, whose sole concern is raw profit. Recognizing this, Seereth orders travelers to venture past Greatwood Vale and directly into Windshear Crag to cull fifteen loggers. By meeting corporate greed with armed force, the Horde aims to halt the deforestation in its tracks and buy time for tauren elders to soothe the agitated spirits of the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Seereth Stonebreak?",a="Seereth Stonebreak is a tauren scout and warden stationed near the southern boundary between the Barrens and the Stonetalon Mountains. He monitors the encroachment of hostile factions and works to protect the spiritual balance of the region.",al={"seereth stonebreak","quest giver","who gives goblin invaders"}},{q="Why are the goblins deforesting Stonetalon Mountains?",a="The Venture Company is an unscrupulous, profit-driven enterprise. They see Stonetalon's dense ancient forests and mineral-rich hills purely as raw materials to be harvested, processed, and sold to the highest bidder, completely indifferent to the natural and spiritual devastation left behind.",al={"why venture co logging","venture company motivation stonetalon","why cut trees"}},{q="Where is Windshear Crag located?",a="Windshear Crag lies in the central portion of the Stonetalon Mountains. To reach it from the Barrens border, travel northwest up the mountain road through Greatwood Vale until the vibrant green forest gives way to the mechanical logging camps and clear-cut hills of the Venture Company.",al={"windshear crag location","where are loggers","where to find venture co loggers"}},{q="How do the spirits react to the Venture Company's presence?",a="According to Seereth Stonebreak, the land spirits are driven near madness with rage and pain from the rampant logging and burning of the woodlands. Their suffering disrupts the natural balance, posing a spiritual threat to the entire region.",al={"stonetalon spirits angry","spirits of stonetalon reaction"}},{q="What happens after culling the Venture Company loggers?",a="Eliminating the loggers is only the initial blow against the operation. Seereth next turns the Horde's attention toward dismantling the company's mechanized infrastructure, while also recommending that the champion seek the guidance of tauren elders to help soothe the wounded spirits.",al={"after goblin invaders","next quest after loggers"},sp=1},{q="Why does the Horde care about logging in Stonetalon?",a="The Stonetalon Mountains hold deep cultural and spiritual significance for the tauren, while the Horde as a whole views the unbridled aggression and resource theft of the Venture Company as a threat to their territorial influence and spiritual harmony.",al={"horde interest stonetalon","why horde fight venture co"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The desecration of Stonetalon's forests and the agony of its earth spirits make confronting the Venture Company an urgent duty for every tauren who honors the Earth Mother.",["class:Druid"]="The mindless destruction of living groves and slaughter of ancient trees in Windshear Crag represent a direct violation of the natural order that druids are sworn to defend.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman can acutely feel the cries of the local elementals and nature spirits, who have been driven blind with fury by the smoke and devastation of goblin machinery.",["faction:Horde"]="Halting the Venture Company secures the borderlands between the Barrens and the higher passes, ensuring hostile commercial syndicates do not fortify central Kalimdor."},kw={"goblin","greatwood vale","logger","seereth stonebreak","spirits","stonetalon mountains","venture company","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:seereth-stonebreak","subzone:windshear-crag","quest:1061","subzone:greatwood-vale","zone:stonetalon","topic:venture-company","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},m={start="Seereth Stonebreak",level="19",faction="Horde",id=1062},src={"Goblin Invaders"}}
E["quest:1068"] = {t="quest",n="Shredding Machines",z="stonetalon",s="Shredding Machines is a Horde quest tasking adventurers with hunting down two specialized Venture Company logging mechs in Windshear Crag. Directed by the shaman Seereth Stonebreak, players strike against the mechanical deforestation that torments Stonetalon's native spirits.",h="Shredding Machines is a Horde quest tasking adventurers with hunting down two specialized Venture Company...",sec={{t="A Vision of Deforestation",b="Stationed along the dusty border between the Barrens and the Stonetalon Mountains, the tauren shaman Seereth Stonebreak listens closely to the unseen realm. While much of Stonetalon's spiritual voice is drowned out by chaos, one vision came to him with harrowing clarity: man-shaped contraptions tearing through ancient woods with unnatural haste. Marked with the mechanical designations XT:4 and XT:9, these goblin-engineered shredders butcher the timberlands of Windshear Crag, sending waves of distress through the surrounding nature spirits.",sp=0},{t="Silencing the Saws",b="To stem the devastation, Horde champions venture deep into Windshear Crag, northwest of Greatwood Vale, where the Venture Company operates. Tracking down and wrecking these specific logging constructs deals a sharp blow to the commercial deforestation of the mountains. Though bringing down XT:4 and XT:9 calms the immediate cries of the wounded tree spirits, Seereth warns that unless the Venture Company abandons Stonetalon entirely, far darker atrocities await the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Seereth Stonebreak?",a="Seereth Stonebreak is a tauren shaman posted at the southern border of the Stonetalon Mountains near the Barrens. Attuned to the elemental and spiritual forces of the land, he acts as a conduit for the anguished forest spirits protesting the rapid expansion of the Venture Company.",al={"who is seereth","quest giver seereth","seereth stonebreak lore"}},{q="What are XT:4 and XT:9?",a="XT:4 and XT:9 are specialized, designated logging shredders operated by the Venture Company in Windshear Crag. Powered by steam engines and piloted by goblin operators, these mechanized walkers cut down ancient timber far faster than manual laborers ever could.",al={"what are the shredders","xt4 and xt9","shredder targets"}},{q="Where is Windshear Crag?",a="Windshear Crag lies in the northern reaches of the Stonetalon Mountains, situated northwest of Greatwood Vale. It has been transformed into a massive industrial logging basin by the Venture Company.",al={"windshear crag location","where do i find the shredders","where are the machines"}},{q="Why does a shaman care about trees and druidic magic?",a="As Seereth explains, shamanistic communion with spirits shares close ties with druidic nature magic. The trauma inflicted upon living forests echoes into the spiritual realm, enabling perceptive shaman to hear the wails of slaughtered tree spirits alongside elemental unrest.",al={"why do shaman care about trees","shaman druid connection","nature spirits shaman"}},{q="Who owns and operates these shredders?",a="The shredders belong to the Venture Company, an unscrupulous goblin-run commercial conglomerate infamous across Azeroth for ruthlessly stripping valuable natural resources with no regard for the local ecosystem or ancestral inhabitants.",al={"who made xt4","who runs the shredders","venture company shredders"}},{q="Does destroying XT:4 and XT:9 drive the Venture Company away?",a="No. While destroying these flagship machines calms the weeping tree spirits and sets back local logging efforts, the Venture Company maintains an extensive industrial foothold across Windshear Crag, requiring ongoing resistance from defenders of the wild.",al={"does the venture company leave","after shredding machines","quest outcome"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Seereth highlights the profound resonance between spiritual magic and nature, reminding shaman that elemental balance relies on defending the spirits inhabiting the land.",["race:Tauren"]="The desecration of Stonetalon's ancient forests by soulless goblin machinery directly violates the tauren devotion to the Earth Mother.",["profession:Engineering"]="The XT-series logging mechs showcase advanced goblin shredder design, balancing mechanical hydraulic saws with raw steam locomotion.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde establishes footholds across Kalimdor, checking the unregulated greed of the Venture Company is critical to preserving the land and securing safe transit through Stonetalon."},kw={"logging","seereth stonebreak","shredder","shredding machines","stonetalon mountains","venture company","windshear crag","xt:4","xt:9"},rel={"npc:seereth-stonebreak","subzone:windshear-crag","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","quest:1061","subzone:greatwood-vale","topic:druid","zone:barrens"},m={start="Seereth Stonebreak",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1068},src={"Shredding Machines"}}
E["quest:1070"] = {t="quest",n="On Guard in Stonetalon",z="stonetalon",s="On Guard in Stonetalon is an Alliance breadcrumb quest directing adventurers south from Ashenvale into the rugged Stonetalon Mountains. Sentinel Thenysil dispatches travelers to check on her scout friend, Kaela Shadowspear, who was sent into the crags alongside a gnome mage to monitor industrial incursions by the Venture Company.",h="On Guard in Stonetalon is an Alliance breadcrumb quest directing adventurers south from Ashenvale into the...",sec={{t="A Scout Sent South",b="Stationed along the southern reaches of Ashenvale, Sentinel Thenysil keeps a close watch on threats pressing toward the ancient forest. Deeply concerned for her friend Kaela Shadowspear, Thenysil asks passing Alliance champions to track her down. Kaela was dispatched into the Stonetalon Mountains by Sentinel Wolfrunner to survey rising turmoil in the heights, but communication has fallen silent, leaving Thenysil anxious for her safety.",sp=0},{t="Uneasy Partnerships in the Crags",b="Thenysil's concern is heightened by Kaela's assigned companion: a gnome mage deployed alongside her by the Alliance leadership. While the night elves have joined the Grand Alliance out of strategic necessity, many Sentinels remain deeply skeptical of arcane practitioners and tinkering gnomes operating in pristine wilderness. Finding Kaela perched on the bluffs above Windshear Crag reveals an outpost keeping vigil over widespread environmental devastation wrought by the Venture Company.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="The quest is offered by Sentinel Thenysil, a night elf sentinel stationed along the borders of southern Ashenvale near the path into the mountains.",al={"quest giver","where to start","who starts on guard in stonetalon"}},{q="Where can I find Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is encamped high on a rocky ridge overlooking the valley entrance into Windshear Crag within the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"kaela location","find kaela","kaela shadowspear spot"}},{q="Why is Sentinel Thenysil worried about Kaela?",a="Kaela was sent to investigate dangerous hostile incursions in Stonetalon and has not sent word back. Furthermore, Thenysil is wary because the Alliance paired Kaela with a gnome mage, a pairing she considers an omen of trouble.",al={"why worry","thenysil concern"}},{q="What threats are active in the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="The mountains suffer heavily from the Venture Company, an unscrupulous goblin mining and logging cartel tearing up the wilderness, alongside aggressive native beasts and rival Horde forces encroaching from the south.",al={"stonetalon enemies","who is in stonetalon"}},{q="Who is Tara?",a="Tara is Sentinel Thenysil's first name. When you meet Kaela, she fondly refers to her old friend as Tara and expresses pride that she is coordinating scouts and adventurers.",al={"who is tara","tara mentioned"}},{q="What happens after finding Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Reaching Kaela completes the journey and leads into further tasks assisting her and her gnome partner with keeping watch over the encroaching threats in Windshear Crag.",al={"next quest","what comes next"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This task marks the southward expansion of Alliance frontier security, linking defense outposts in Ashenvale to isolated scouting perches in the Stonetalon Mountains.",["race:NightElf"]="The mission illustrates the friction between traditional night elf Sentinels and the arcane, mechanical practices of their Eastern Kingdom allies, particularly gnomes.",["race:Gnome"]="Sentinels view gnomish magic and contraptions with deep skepticism, seeing the inclusion of a gnome mage as an odd, unpredictable variable in Kalimdor's wilderness."},kw={"ashenvale","kaela shadowspear","on guard in stonetalon","sentinel thenysil","stonetalon mountains","venture co","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:sentinel-thenysil","npc:kaela-shadowspear","zone:stonetalon","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels","topic:gnome","quest:764"},m={start="Sentinel Thenysil",["end"]="Kaela Shadowspear",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1070},src={"On Guard in Stonetalon"}}
E["quest:1071"] = {t="quest",n="A Gnome's Respite",z="stonetalon",s="A Gnome's Respite is an Alliance quest offered by the eccentric tinkerer Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains. Overwhelmed by the Venture Company's rapid industrial push into Windshear Crag, Gaxim hires adventurers to cull their loggers and deforesters so he can buy enough breathing room to invent new deterrents.",h="A Gnome's Respite is an Alliance quest offered by the eccentric tinkerer Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Clashing Alliance",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle represents the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences. Stationed among the ancient groves of Stonetalon, his stated duty is proving to the nature-worshipping night elves that modern gnomish invention—blending magic, chemical brews, and mechanics—can actively protect their threatened lands. However, the relentless pace of the Venture Company has left him with barely any time to prototype his defensive devices.",sp=0},{t="Buying Time in Windshear Crag",b="To stem the tide, Gaxim sends adventurers directly into the smoking operations at Windshear Crag. By targeting the frontline Venture Co. Loggers and Deforesters, travelers give Gaxim the respite he needs to organize his workshop and devise his next line of defense: strategic, controlled high explosives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an Alliance gnome engineer located in the Stonetalon Mountains. He serves as an operative of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, attempting to aid the night elves against industrial invaders.",al={"gaxim","who is gaxim rustfizzle","quest giver gaxim"}},{q="Why is a gnome trying to protect night elf forests?",a="Gaxim believes it is his duty to prove to the skeptical night elves that advanced gnomish sciences—specifically arcanology, alchemy, and engineering—can coexist with nature and actively help defend their wilderness from unchecked industrial exploitation.",al={"why gnome in stonetalon","why help night elves","gnome ecology"}},{q="Who are the Venture Company in Windshear Crag?",a="The Venture Company is a ruthless goblin-run merchant syndicate strip-mining and clear-cutting Windshear Crag. Driven purely by profit, they have overrun the valley with loggers, deforesters, and heavy logging machinery.",al={"venture co stonetalon","who are venture co","windshear crag goblins"}},{q="Where can the loggers and deforesters be found?",a="They operate throughout Windshear Crag, the heavily industrialized basin located directly east of Gaxim's position along the main road in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where are loggers","where to find deforesters","windshear crag location"}},{q="What does Gaxim plan to do once he gets time to think?",a="With the goblin workers driven back, Gaxim intends to replenish his stock of high explosives, using targeted mountain detonations to herd and frighten the Venture Company away from the groves.",al={"gaxim plan","gnome respite continuation","explosives plan"}},{q="What is the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences?",a="It is a gnomish academic society that explores the integration of arcane spellcraft, chemical mixtures, and mechanical engineering to solve practical problems across Azeroth.",al={"gnomish assembly","arcanology assembly","what is enlightened assembly"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim's mission represents classic gnomish ambition: solving ancient, philosophical conflicts between nature and civilization through superior ingenuity and a bit of high explosives.",["race:NightElf"]="While Kaldorei sentinels typically view gnomish machinery with deep suspicion, the relentless advance of the Venture Company makes any effective deterrent welcome in Stonetalon.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will appreciate Gaxim's philosophy that mechanisms and chemistry can solve environmental crises, as well as his fondness for high explosives."},kw={"deforester","explosives","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome","logger","stonetalon","venture co","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","topic:goblin","quest:1070"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1071},src={"A Gnome's Respite"}}
E["quest:1072"] = {t="quest",n="An Old Colleague",z="stonetalon",s="An Old Colleague is an Alliance quest given by the gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains. Looking to construct an extraordinarily potent device, Gaxim sends an adventurer all the way across the sea to Ironforge to track down an old acquaintance capable of synthesizing a hazardous explosive concoction. Completing this errand opens the door to procuring the volatile chemical compound known as Nitromirglyceronium.",h="An Old Colleague is an Alliance quest given by the gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Volatile Recipe",b="While stationed among the peaks of Stonetalon, Gaxim Rustfizzle conceives of his most ambitious engineering endeavor yet. Creating a mechanism of that scale requires specialized fuel far beyond typical gunpowder or crude oil. Specifically, Gaxim requires Nitromirglyceronium, also designated as NG-5, an explosive mix potent enough to guarantee destructive results should everything go according to plan.",sp=0},{t="Tinker Town Connection",b="Formulating NG-5 is no simple task, and Gaxim knows of only one mind skilled enough to refine it: an old acquaintance named Lomac Gearstrip. Lomac resides far to the east in the gnome quarter of Tinker Town, tucked deep within the mountain stronghold of Ironforge. Entrusted with the long journey, the courier arrives only to be greeted by Lomac's immediate suspicion and paranoid questioning.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest An Old Colleague?",a="The quest is provided by Gaxim Rustfizzle, a gnome engineer stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"quest giver","who starts an old colleague","gaxim quest"}},{q="Where can I find Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac Gearstrip can be found within Tinker Town, the gnomish quarter located in the eastern portion of the dwarven city of Ironforge.",al={"where is lomac","lomac gearstrip location","ironforge lomac"}},{q="What is Nitromirglyceronium?",a="Nitromirglyceronium, also known as NG-5, is an extremely volatile chemical explosive engineered by Lomac Gearstrip and coveted by Gaxim Rustfizzle for his high-powered devices.",al={"what is ng-5","nitromirglyceronium","ng 5"}},{q="Why does Gaxim send me all the way to Ironforge?",a="Gaxim claims that Lomac Gearstrip is the only person capable of synthesizing the specialized NG-5 compound necessary to power his experimental device.",al={"why travel to ironforge","why lomac","why go to tinker town"}},{q="What happens after finding Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Once you confirm Gaxim's request with the suspicious Lomac, he presents you with the quest Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun to gather the hazardous reagents required to mix the batch.",al={"next quest","what comes after an old colleague","followup quest"}},{q="Which faction can undertake this task?",a="This is strictly an Alliance quest, as it originates from an Alliance-aligned gnome in Stonetalon and concludes inside the Alliance capital of Ironforge.",al={"is this alliance only","horde version","can horde do this"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This task sends Alliance adventurers on a continent-spanning journey from the embattled crags of Kalimdor back to the safety of Ironforge.",["race:Gnome"]="A quintessential gnomish endeavor involving long-distance academic network ties, eccentric rivalries, and dangerously unstable explosive compounds.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will appreciate Gaxim and Lomac's relentless pursuit of maximum firepower regardless of the hazardous logistics involved."},kw={"explosives","gaxim rustfizzle","ironforge","lomac gearstrip","ng-5","nitromirglyceronium","stonetalon","tinker town"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:lomac-gearstrip","quest:1073","subzone:tinker-town","zone:ironforge","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",["end"]="Lomac Gearstrip",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1072},src={"An Old Colleague"}}
E["quest:1073"] = {t="quest",n="Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun",z="stonetalon",s="Seeking an explosive countermeasure against the Venture Company's logging machines in the Stonetalon Mountains, Alliance adventurers are sent across the sea to Ironforge. There, the eccentric gnome Lomac Gearstrip agrees to brew his volatile invention, Nitromirglyceronium, provided you fetch the necessary alchemical reagents.",h="Seeking an explosive countermeasure against the Venture Company's logging machines in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Volatile Solution",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle, stationed high in the craggy passes of the Stonetalon Mountains, found himself completely stymied by the sheer bulk and armor of goblin shredders. Rather than relying on simple steel or standard siege tactics, he turned to an eccentric former colleague living in Ironforge: Lomac Gearstrip. Lomac is the creator of Nitromirglyceronium, a substance so inherently unstable and destructive that he finds the prospect of anyone using it hilarious, regardless of who gets blown apart in the process.",sp=0},{t="Potions for Pyrotechnics",b="Despite Lomac's eagerness to see goblin machinery—and possibly the adventurer—blown into pieces, his workshop in Ironforge is entirely out of the finished compound. Before he will brew a fresh batch of Nitromirglyceronium, Lomac demands common alchemical draughts: Minor Mana Potions and Elixirs of Minor Fortitude. In his eyes, forcing an adventurer to gather these ingredients serves a dual purpose, ensuring he has the raw reagents needed for the reaction while proving they possess at least a shred of respect for the craft of alchemy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac Gearstrip is an eccentric gnomish alchemist and tinkerer located in the dwarven capital of Ironforge. He is an old colleague of Gaxim Rustfizzle and the inventor of Nitromirglyceronium, an extraordinarily volatile explosive compound.",al={"lomac gearstrip","who is lomac","ironforge gnome"}},{q="Why does Lomac want potions instead of standard engineering parts?",a="Lomac utilizes alchemy alongside his mechanical know-how to produce high-grade volatile reactions. The magical energy of Minor Mana Potions and the stabilizing bodily humors enhanced by Elixirs of Minor Fortitude serve as base reagents for his specialized Nitromirglyceronium mixture.",al={"why potions","alchemical ingredients","why mana potions"}},{q="Why send an adventurer all the way to Ironforge for this?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is isolated in the wilds of Stonetalon without access to heavy industrial or chemical workshops. Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge is the only associate he trusts—or fears enough—to possess an explosive potent enough to crack Venture Company machinery.",al={"why ironforge","why travel so far","gaxim to ironforge"}},{q="What is Nitromirglyceronium?",a="Nitromirglyceronium is Lomac Gearstrip's proprietary explosive chemical brew. It is notoriously volatile, formulated specifically to generate enough concussive blast force to tear apart heavily fortified mechanical equipment.",al={"nitromirglyceronium","what is the explosive","gnome bomb juice"}},{q="Is Lomac worried about the Venture Company or the forest?",a="Not in the slightest. Lomac openly laughs at the idea of using high explosives to save trees. His sole interest in handing over the compound is the chaotic prospect of watching either the goblins or the courier get blasted to pieces.",al={"does lomac care about nature","lomac motives"}},{q="Do you need to be an alchemist to complete this task?",a="No. While Lomac talks about testing your alchemical mettle, he accepts reagents acquired through trade, merchants, or other crafters just the same, so long as he gets the draughts required for his recipe.",al={"need alchemy","alchemy required"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Lomac represents the unrestrained, madcap fringe of gnomish ingenuity, prioritizing sheer chemical yield and theoretical application over safety or diplomatic caution.",["faction:Alliance"]="The long trek from Stonetalon to Ironforge highlights the logistical strain of supporting remote Alliance outposts scattered throughout hostile Kalimdor.",["profession:Engineering"]="Where standard blasting powder fails against Venture Company steel, combining esoteric alchemy with engineering principles produces far more catastrophic results."},kw={"elixir of minor fortitude","gaxim rustfizzle","ironforge","lomac gearstrip","mana potion","nitromirglyceronium","stonetalon","venture company"},rel={"npc:lomac-gearstrip","quest:1072","zone:stonetalon","zone:ironforge","topic:goblin"},m={start="Lomac Gearstrip",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1073},src={"Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun"}}
E["quest:1074"] = {t="quest",n="Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun",z="stonetalon",s="This errand delivers a canister of volatile NG-5 from the tinker Lomac Gearstrip to Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains. Gaxim requires this unstable chemical to create a potent igniter for several wagons packed with dynamite. The resulting blast forms a critical distraction for Alliance operations in the disputed crags.",h="This errand delivers a canister of volatile NG-5 from the tinker Lomac Gearstrip to Gaxim Rustfizzle in the...",sec={{t="A Volatile Delivery",b="Gnomish engineering often balances brilliance on the razor edge of catastrophe, and Nitromirglyceronium—or NG-5—is no exception. Lomac Gearstrip hands over the unstable compound with a stern warning: handle it with extreme care, or risk blowing yourself to pieces on the road back to Gaxim Rustfizzle.",sp=0},{t="A Recipe for Distraction",b="Upon receiving the canister intact, Gaxim Rustfizzle reveals the true scope of his handiwork. NG-5 is the essential catalyst needed to detonate entire wagons full of dynamite. By staging a colossal explosion, Gaxim hopes to sow chaos and misdirect enemies in Stonetalon while the Alliance pursues its regional goals.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is NG-5?",a="NG-5, short for Nitromirglyceronium, is a highly volatile chemical compound concocted by Lomac Gearstrip. It serves as an unequivocal ignition catalyst for heavy ordnance.",al={"what is nitromirglyceronium","ng-5","what did lomac give me"}},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome operative and engineer stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains, orchestrating Alliance demolition efforts and tactical distractions against regional threats.",al={"gaxim","who is gaxim rustfizzle"}},{q="Who is Lomac Gearstrip?",a="Lomac Gearstrip is an engineer and associate of Gaxim Rustfizzle who prepares the dangerous NG-5 compound and entrusts it to reliable couriers.",al={"lomac","who is lomac gearstrip"}},{q="Why does Gaxim need so much explosive power?",a="Gaxim has arranged multiple wagons loaded with dynamite. The NG-5 provides the reliable, massive spark required to detonate them all at once, creating an overwhelming diversion.",al={"why wagons of dynamite","gaxim plan","why the explosion"}},{q="Is the chemical dangerous to transport?",a="Lomac explicitly warns that NG-5 is unstable and prone to catastrophic accidental detonation if mishandled, though a steady courier can deliver it safely to Gaxim.",al={"does ng5 explode","is ng-5 safe"}},{q="Where does this delivery take place?",a="The delivery concludes at Gaxim Rustfizzle's post within the rugged passes of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where is gaxim","stonetalon location"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Only gnomish ambition would consider wagons of high explosives ignited by Nitromirglyceronium a reasonable distraction.",["profession:Engineering"]="Handling NG-5 requires an appreciation for volatile chemistry and a steady pair of hands to avoid early detonation.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stonetalon is a contested frontier; a massive explosion gives Alliance operatives the breathing room they desperately need."},kw={"dynamite","engineering","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome","lomac gearstrip","ng-5","nitromirglyceronium","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:1073","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:lomac-gearstrip","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Lomac Gearstrip",["end"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1074},src={"Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun (2)"}}
E["quest:1077"] = {t="quest",n="Special Delivery for Gaxim",z="stonetalon",s="Special Delivery for Gaxim represents the return leg of an Alliance courier mission between Stormwind City and the wilds of Kalimdor. Collin Mauren provides a specialized Scroll of Messaging to take back to the gnome tinkerer Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains. The scroll contains the arcane component needed to construct a remote explosive against local deforestation efforts.",h="Special Delivery for Gaxim represents the return leg of an Alliance courier mission between Stormwind City...",sec={{t="Arcane Deliveries",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle's efforts to sabotage the destructive operations of the Venture Company require unconventional solutions. Having concocted an explosive compound called NG-5, the tinkerer found himself lacking a reliable means of remote detonation. Rather than turning to crude fuses, Gaxim enlisted help across the Great Sea, reaching out to Collin Mauren in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind to acquire an enchanted Scroll of Messaging.",sp=0},{t="A Remote Distraction",b="Upon receiving the scroll, Gaxim reveals the full scope of his eccentric engineering plan. The enchanted parchment does not serve merely to pass words across long distances; instead, its communicative magic can be tethered directly to the unstable NG-5 mixture. By triggering the detonation magically from afar, Gaxim intends to produce a devastating distraction that allows operatives to slip into the Venture Company compound undetected.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Scroll of Messaging used for?",a="While originally designed as an arcane tool for conveying messages, Gaxim Rustfizzle combines the scroll with his volatile NG-5 compound. The messaging magic acts as a remote trigger, allowing him to detonate explosives safely from a distance.",al={"why scroll of messaging","what does the scroll do","scroll of messaging purpose"}},{q="Who is Collin Mauren?",a="Collin Mauren is an Alliance wizard based in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City. He assists adventurers with arcane matters and crafts the enchanted scroll needed for Gaxim's plan in Stonetalon.",al={"collin mauren lore","who is collin"}},{q="Why is Gaxim Rustfizzle sabotaging the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company is ruthlessly clear-cutting the pristine forests of the Stonetalon Mountains. Gaxim aims to slow down their deforestation by causing chaos, destroying their operations, and stealing their proprietary engineering plans and correspondence.",al={"why attack venture co","gaxim motivation","venture co stonetalon"}},{q="Where does this delivery take the adventurer?",a="The delivery takes the courier from Stormwind City across the sea back to the Alliance camp in the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains on Kalimdor.",al={"delivery destination","where is gaxim","stonetalon location"}},{q="What happens after the scroll is delivered?",a="With both the scroll and NG-5 in hand, Gaxim prepares a remote explosive distraction, clearing the way for an operative to infiltrate the Windshear Crag operations to recover logging letters and schematics.",al={"next quest","what after delivery","venture co distraction"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Gaxim's scheme highlights the quirky intersection of gnomish engineering and wizardry, pairing volatile NG-5 explosives with arcane triggers.",["class:Mage"]="Collin Mauren's craft demonstrates how simple parchment enchantments can be repurposed into functional arcane relays by clever tinkerers.",["faction:Alliance"]="This task demonstrates the logistical links connecting the human capital of Stormwind to remote Alliance outposts struggling against industrial exploitation in Kalimdor."},kw={"collin mauren","gaxim rustfizzle","ng-5","remote explosive","scroll of messaging","stonetalon","venture co"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:collin-mauren","zone:stonetalon","quest:764"},m={start="Collin Mauren",["end"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1077},src={"Special Delivery for Gaxim"}}
E["quest:1078"] = {t="quest",n="Retrieval for Mauren",z="stonetalon",s="Retrieval for Mauren is a quest given by Collin Mauren in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind. Hearing tales of travelers venturing deep into Kalimdor, the wizard contracts Alliance adventurers to gather crystallised scales from basilisks dwelling in Stonetalon's Charred Vale. Mauren seeks these rare specimens to grind into dust as reagents for his personal spellcraft.",h="Retrieval for Mauren is a quest given by Collin Mauren in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Mage's Curious Reagents",b="Collin Mauren, a wizard residing in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City, keeps an ear close to the chatter of wandering adventurers. Word has reached him that the distant Stonetalon Mountains in Kalimdor have become a burgeoning hotspot for travelers seeking wild wyverns, unruly elementals, or lucrative deals and clashes with the Venture Company. Rather than seeking riches or glory, Mauren's interest lies in the rare natural wonders reported from the region's harshest corners.",sp=0},{t="The Glassy Beasts of the Vale",b="Deep within Stonetalon lies the Charred Vale, an ash-choked expanse left scarred by magical devastation. According to Mauren's studies, the basin was once known to house a peculiar breed of basilisk. When harvested and crushed into a fine powder, their scales form a potent catalyst for specialized arcane spells he has developed. Unsure whether the creatures managed to survive the harsh transformation of the Vale, Mauren relies on intrepid explorers to harvest a fresh batch of crystallised scales and confirm whether the breed endures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Collin Mauren?",a="Collin Mauren is an arcane practitioner found in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind. He studies esoteric spellcraft and frequently relies on adventurous travelers to procure rare magical reagents from distant lands.",al={"collin mauren","who gives retrieval for mauren","mauren stormwind"}},{q="Why does Collin Mauren need basilisk scales?",a="Mauren grinds the crystallized scales into fine dust, utilizing their unique mineral composition as a catalyst reagent for original spells he has devised.",al={"why scales","what are scales for","crystallized scales use"}},{q="Where is the Charred Vale located?",a="The Charred Vale is a ruined, soot-covered basin located in the southwestern reaches of the Stonetalon Mountains on the continent of Kalimdor.",al={"where charred vale","find charred vale","charred vale location"}},{q="Why is the Charred Vale charred?",a="The Charred Vale was devastated during the Third War by intense magical warfare and lingering elemental corruption, leaving the ground blackened, smoldering, and populated by hardy, twisted beasts.",al={"what happened to charred vale","charred vale fire","charred vale destruction"}},{q="What creatures drop the scales needed for this task?",a="The scales are gathered from the various basilisks prowling the smoldering wastes of the Charred Vale in Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"which basilisks","who drops crystallized scales","scale mobs"}},{q="Why send an adventurer all the way across the sea for this?",a="The specific crystalline properties Mauren requires are only found on the basilisks indigenous to the Charred Vale. Because crossing the Great Sea is perilous, Mauren enlists seasoned travelers already setting out for Kalimdor.",al={"why kalimdor","why stonetalon for scales"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Procuring esoteric reagents for fellow wizards is a hallmark of arcane research, illustrating how exotic magical wildlife fuels the development of new incantations.",["faction:Alliance"]="This task demonstrates how the Alliance's presence in Stormwind maintains active interests and supply lines reaching deep into the wild territories of Kalimdor."},kw={"basilisk scales","charred vale","collin mauren","crystallized scales","mage quarter","retrieval for mauren","stonetalon mountains","stormwind"},rel={"npc:collin-mauren","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:764"},m={start="Collin Mauren",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=1078},src={"Retrieval for Mauren"}}
E["quest:1079"] = {t="quest",n="Covert Ops - Alpha",z="stonetalon",s="Covert Ops - Alpha is an Alliance infiltration mission directed by the gnome tinker Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains. While operating out of the peaks, operatives are tasked with penetrating the Venture Company's lumber mill in Windshear Crag to recover proprietary engineering schematics. Securing these blueprints allows the Alliance to decipher the mechanical vulnerabilities of goblin machinery while co-opting their logging technology.",h="Covert Ops - Alpha is an Alliance infiltration mission directed by the gnome tinker Gaxim Rustfizzle in the...",sec={{t="Sabotage and Espionage",b="Operating from Windshear Crag, Gaxim Rustfizzle conducts a persistent covert campaign to disrupt the aggressive logging operations of the Venture Company. While goblin deforesters fell the primeval timber south of Cragpool Lake, Gaxim recognizes that wanton destruction alone cannot halt the enterprise. Instead of merely detonating industrial hardware, Plan Alpha prioritizes intelligence gathering, requiring agents to slip past goblin loggers and overseers to seize their core technical schematics directly from the lumber mill.",sp=0},{t="Reverse Engineering",b="Gnomish interest in the Venture Company extends beyond ecological sympathy for the night elves. The recovered schematics detail the inner workings of heavy-duty goblin loggers, mechanical cutters, and mechanized transports. By studying these blueprints, Alliance engineers can expose critical structural flaws to dismantle future operations—while simultaneously borrowing refined goblin designs to enhance their own mechanical projects back in Ironforge and Gnomeregan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the primary goal of Covert Ops - Alpha?",a="The primary objective is the recovery of the Venture Company's engineering plans from their lumber mill in Windshear Crag, located south of Cragpool Lake. While explosive devices are involved in the overall covert effort, securing these blueprints is the sole measure of the mission's success.",al={"what is covert ops alpha","alpha mission goal","what does gaxim want"}},{q="Who gives the quest Covert Ops - Alpha?",a="The mission is assigned by Gaxim Rustfizzle, an Alliance gnome tinker stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains overseeing covert sabotage operations against goblin industrial efforts.",al={"who starts covert ops alpha","gaxim rustfizzle quest","covert ops quest giver"}},{q="Where are the engineering plans located?",a="The Venture Company Engineering Plans are kept inside the operational lumber mill in Windshear Crag, situated just south of Cragpool Lake amidst heavy goblin logging defenses.",al={"where are the venture co plans","engineering plans location","windshear crag lumber mill plans"}},{q="Why does Gaxim Rustfizzle want the Venture Co. blueprints?",a="Gaxim seeks the plans to study the structural vulnerabilities of goblin logging machines. Discovering their mechanical flaws allows the Alliance to sabotage future machinery more effectively, while also adopting practical goblin engineering designs for Alliance devices.",al={"why steal venture co plans","what will gaxim do with plans","reason for covert ops alpha"}},{q="Is sheer destruction the point of the mission?",a="No. Gaxim explicitly reminds operatives that mission success does not depend on the amount of destruction inflicted, but rather on successfully extracting the schematics intact from the mill.",al={"do i blow up the mill","should i destroy machines","mission destruction focus"}},{q="Why is the Alliance fighting the Venture Company here?",a="The Venture Company is pillaging the natural resources of Stonetalon through unchecked deforestation and industrial pollution. Alliance operatives intervene to undermine their industrial footprint and preserve strategic territory in Kalimdor.",al={"why fight venture company in stonetalon","alliance venture co conflict","stonetalon logging war"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For a gnome tinker, analyzing goblin blueprints is the ultimate prize: it offers the rare chance to mock goblin design oversights while stealing their most lucrative mechanical tricks.",["profession:Engineering"]="The recovered schematics expose the gritty, high-combustion mechanisms favored by the Venture Company, providing valuable technical insights into industrial motor works.",["race:NightElf"]="The Venture Company's deforestation in Windshear Crag wounds Stonetalon's ancient forests, making any sabotage of their logging infrastructure an urgent priority for the kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing footholds and curbing industrial extraction across Kalimdor ensures the Alliance maintains tactical parity against rival powers encroaching on contested wilderness."},kw={"alpha","covert ops","cragpool lake","engineering plans","gaxim rustfizzle","lumber mill","stonetalon","venture co","windshear crag"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:cragpool-lake","zone:stonetalon","quest:764"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1079},src={"Covert Ops - Alpha"}}
E["quest:1080"] = {t="quest",n="Covert Ops - Beta",z="stonetalon",s="Covert Ops - Beta is an Alliance mission organized by the gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon Mountains. Building upon previous sabotage against the encroaching Venture Company, this operation sends an agent deep into Windshear Mine to trigger explosive diversions and extract vital operational letters. The retrieved intelligence serves both gnome curiosity and the territorial defense of the regional night elf Sentinels.",h="Covert Ops - Beta is an Alliance mission organized by the gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="Sabotage in the Depths",b="Following initial strikes against the Venture Company's clear-cutting operations across Windshear Crag, Gaxim Rustfizzle devises a follow-up operation aimed directly at their logistical heart. Plan Beta follows the same fundamental logic as its predecessor: creating an explosive, chaotic diversion to scatter the goblin operators and mercenaries while an operative slips through the confusion to search the mines for written correspondence.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on Windshear Mine",b="Windshear Mine sits at the far eastern reaches of the crag, serving as the company's regional subterranean base. Digging through rock and harvesting timber, the goblins maintain strict ledgers and communications detailing their supply lines and executive directives. By sneaking inside, setting Gaxim's specialized explosive packs, and seizing the Venture Co. Letters, operatives dismantle the company's security while uncovering their wider ambitions in Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Pragmatic Partnership",b="While Gaxim approaches the mission with typical gnomish delight for pyrotechnics and clever gadgetry, the mission has serious strategic implications for the night elves. The Sentinels guarding Stonetalon Peak, led by commanders like Kaela Nightstrider, are hard-pressed battling both the Horde and ruthless industrial exploiters. The intelligence recovered from the mine directly assists the Sentinels in predicting and thwarting the defilement of their sacred woodlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of Covert Ops - Beta?",a="The objective is to infiltrate Windshear Mine in eastern Windshear Crag, detonate explosive diversions using Gaxim Rustfizzle's pack, and steal the Venture Co. Letters outlining their regional operations.",al={"covert ops beta objective","what do i do in covert ops beta","plan beta goal"}},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome engineer stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains. He uses his mechanical expertise and explosive inventions to assist the night elf Sentinels in combating the logging and mining ventures encroaching on the mountain.",al={"gaxim rustfizzle","who gives covert ops beta"}},{q="Where is Windshear Mine located?",a="Windshear Mine is carved into the mountains at the eastern end of Windshear Crag, nestled deep inside the Venture Company's sprawling clear-cut deforestation zone.",al={"windshear mine location","where is the mine"}},{q="Why does Gaxim want the Venture Co. Letters?",a="The letters contain vital intelligence on the Venture Company's supply routes, leadership directives, and operational plans. Recovering them helps the Alliance and the Sentinels anticipate the company's next moves and disrupt their exploitation of the forest.",al={"why steal letters","what are the venture co letters"}},{q="How does this mission benefit the night elves?",a="The night elf Sentinels lack the numbers to police every corner of Stonetalon against industrial desecration. Gaxim's explosive sabotage delays the logging efforts, while the recovered correspondence gives Sentinel commanders like Kaela actionable intelligence on their enemies.",al={"why do night elves care","sentinels covert ops"}},{q="What was Plan Alpha?",a="Plan Alpha was Gaxim's preceding covert operation, establishing the tactic of planting engineering charges across Venture Company logging equipment in Windshear Crag to sow chaos and weaken their perimeter.",al={"plan alpha","covert ops alpha","previous mission"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle's blend of high-yield explosives, meticulous planning, and covert intrusion represents quintessential gnomish ingenuity put to practical military use.",["race:NightElf"]="The Venture Company is stripping the ancient woods bare; supporting Gaxim's covert operations ensures that Sentinel commanders receive the intelligence needed to protect the mountain.",["profession:Engineering"]="The mission centers around Gaxim's specialized Covert Ops Pack, showing how clever pyrotechnic diversions can accomplish objectives that brute force alone cannot.",["faction:Alliance"]="Coordinating gnomish technology with night elf territorial defense strengthens the Alliance's fragile presence across central Kalimdor."},kw={"covert ops - beta","gaxim rustfizzle","sentinels","stonetalon mountains","venture co.","venture co. letters","windshear crag","windshear mine"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","subzone:windshear-crag","quest:764","topic:sentinels","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1080},src={"Covert Ops - Beta"}}
E["quest:1081"] = {t="quest",n="Reception from Tyrande",z="stonetalon",s="Reception from Tyrande is an Alliance quest that sends adventurers from the embattled slopes of the Stonetalon Mountains directly to the night elf capital of Darnassus. After aiding Sentinel Thenysil in securing their precarious foothold against Horde encroachment, you are summoned to receive formal recognition from High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind herself in the Temple of the Moon.",h="Reception from Tyrande is an Alliance quest that sends adventurers from the embattled slopes of the...",sec={{t="A Foothold in Stonetalon",b="The night elven outposts scattered throughout the Stonetalon Mountains face intense pressure, particularly from Horde expansionists and hostile wildlife. Sentinel Thenysil coordinates defensive efforts on the ground, but sustaining these remote bases requires immense resilience. Securing supply lines and intelligence is vital to maintaining an Alliance presence in Kalimdor's interior, making outside aid profoundly impactful to the Sentinels stationed there.",sp=0},{t="Audience with the High Priestess",b="Recognizing that your assistance has actively bolstered the Sentinels' grip on the region, Sentinel Thenysil directs you to travel back to Teldrassil. At the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind grants you a personal audience. Tyrande acknowledges your rising deeds across Kalimdor, welcoming you not merely as a wandering mercenary, but as an allied champion fighting alongside the kaldorei.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this quest start?",a="The quest begins with Sentinel Thenysil in the Stonetalon Mountains, immediately following the completion of 'Update for Sentinel Thenysil'.",al={"where do i get reception from tyrande","quest giver","sentinel thenysil location"}},{q="Where can I find Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="Tyrande Whisperwind resides within the Temple of the Moon, located in the central district of the night elf capital city of Darnassus on Teldrassil.",al={"where is tyrande","find tyrande","temple of the moon location"}},{q="Why does Tyrande want to see me?",a="Your efforts in Stonetalon have helped preserve the Kaldorei foothold in contested mountain territory. Sentinel Thenysil feels your contributions to the night elves warrant a personal token of appreciation from their spiritual and military leader.",al={"why tyrande wants to talk","purpose of audience"}},{q="What is the strategic value of the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Stonetalon forms a rugged buffer between Ashenvale and the southern plains of Kalimdor. With Horde forces pushing out from the Barrens, holding outposts here is crucial for the night elves to monitor enemy movements and safeguard sacred lands.",al={"why care about stonetalon","stonetalon lore"}},{q="Do other Alliance races get recognized here?",a="Yes. Any Alliance adventurer who assists Sentinel Thenysil can undertake this journey to Darnassus, symbolizing the growing mutual defense between the night elves and the broader Alliance.",al={"can non night elves do this","is this for humans"}},{q="Is there a follow-up quest after meeting Tyrande?",a="This audience marks the culmination of the Stonetalon courier and support tasks for Sentinel Thenysil, serving as a formal conclusion and offering an opportunity to seek further orders in Darnassus.",al={"what comes next","next quest in chain"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="An audience with Tyrande Whisperwind serves as a meaningful bridge between Kalimdor's night elves and the broader Alliance, turning wilderness skirmishes into recognized service to Darnassus.",["race:NightElf"]="Reporting to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind inside the Temple of the Moon is a proud homecoming, proving your devotion to the defense of ancient ancestral grounds."},kw={"darnassus","kaldorei","reception from tyrande","sentinel thenysil","stonetalon mountains","teldrassil","temple of the moon","tyrande whisperwind"},rel={"npc:tyrande-whisperwind","npc:sentinel-thenysil","quest:1082","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","zone:stonetalon","quest:2519"},m={start="Sentinel Thenysil",["end"]="Tyrande Whisperwind",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1081},src={"Reception from Tyrande"}}
E["quest:1082"] = {t="quest",n="Update for Sentinel Thenysil",z="stonetalon",s="This errand carries word of relief from the crags of Stonetalon back to the night elf outpost of Astranaar. Having aided Kaela Shadowspear and Gaxim Rustfizzle against the encroaching Venture Company, you are tasked with reassuring Sentinel Tara Thenysil that their outpost holds firm.",h="This errand carries word of relief from the crags of Stonetalon back to the night elf outpost of Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Dispatch from the Peaks",b="Stonetalon's jagged passes are an isolated and vulnerable frontier for the night elves. With goblin deforestation operations eating away at the crags and polluting the waterways, the outpost manned by Kaela Shadowspear and the gnome tinkerer Gaxim Rustfizzle operates under constant threat. Once the immediate dangers posed by the Venture Company are blunted, keeping the command hierarchy informed is essential. Kaela sends you northeast across the border back into Ashenvale to confirm their survival.",sp=0},{t="Relief in Astranaar",b="In the forested sanctuary of Astranaar, Sentinel Tara Thenysil maintains watch over Ashenvale's interior roads while worrying over scouts deployed into harsher territories. Receiving confirmation that both Kaela and her eccentric engineering partner are alive and actively healing the land offers a rare moment of good news. It proves that despite dwindling forces and multiple hostile fronts, cooperation with Alliance allies can stem the tide of ecological destruction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Thenysil?",a="Tara Thenysil is an officer of the night elf Sentinels stationed in Astranaar, the primary Alliance hub in Ashenvale. She monitors the status of scouts and patrols sent into the surrounding wilds and adjacent regions.",al={"sentinel thenysil","tara thenysil","thenysil astranaar"}},{q="Why is Kaela Shadowspear in Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Kaela Shadowspear was deployed to Stonetalon to monitor and combat the destructive environmental exploitation carried out by the Venture Company, working alongside the gnome Gaxim Rustfizzle to sabotage goblin machinery and restore the land.",al={"kaela shadowspear","kaela mission","why is kaela in stonetalon"}},{q="Who is Gaxim?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an Alliance gnome engineer stationed alongside Kaela Shadowspear in Stonetalon. Though his noisy trade contrasts with traditional elven sensibilities, his technical expertise is crucial for disrupting goblin logging machinery.",al={"gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle","the gnome with kaela"}},{q="Where do I find Sentinel Thenysil?",a="Sentinel Thenysil is stationed in Astranaar, situated along the central road in Ashenvale, northeast of the path leading down from the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where is thenysil","thenysil location","where is astranaar"}},{q="What happens after reporting back to Sentinel Thenysil?",a="Reporting the success in Stonetalon to Sentinel Thenysil opens further opportunities within the night elf military and leads toward higher-level communications with Darnassus leadership.",al={"next quest after thenysil","where do i go next","reception from tyrande"}},{q="Why is the Venture Company a threat in Stonetalon?",a="The Venture Company is ruthlessly clear-cutting sacred groves, operating massive logging machinery, and poisoning the waterways in Stonetalon, posing a direct threat to the natural balance the night elves guard.",al={"venture co stonetalon","why fight venture co"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Delivering news of Kaela's survival reassures the Sentinels that their hold over Kalimdor's borderlands has not broken under industrial encroachment.",["race:Gnome"]="Even Sentinel Thenysil grudgingly acknowledges relief that Gaxim Rustfizzle is safe, demonstrating that gnomish ingenuity can earn respect even among traditionalist elves.",["faction:Alliance"]="Maintaining communication between the frontier posts of Stonetalon and the strongholds of Ashenvale helps secure the Alliance's presence in central Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","gaxim rustfizzle","kaela shadowspear","sentinel thenysil","stonetalon","update for sentinel thenysil","venture co"},rel={"npc:sentinel-thenysil","npc:kaela-shadowspear","subzone:astranaar","quest:1081","quest:764","zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Kaela Shadowspear",["end"]="Sentinel Thenysil",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1082},src={"Update for Sentinel Thenysil"}}
E["quest:1083"] = {t="quest",n="Enraged Spirits",z="stonetalon",s="Enraged Spirits is an Alliance quest given by Kaela Shadowspear in the Stonetalon Mountains. After the Venture Company laid waste to the Charred Vale with fire and heavy machinery, furious fire elementals broke free and overran the blighted basin. Alliance champions are asked to quell these roaming spirits of flame and stone so the wounded land might one day heal under Elune's grace.",h="Enraged Spirits is an Alliance quest given by Kaela Shadowspear in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Scorched Tragedy",b="The Charred Vale was once a lush haven within Stonetalon, but the reckless greed of the Venture Company transformed it into an ashen wasteland. In their drive to log and strip the land of resources, the goblins deployed incendiary devices and heavy machinery that set the entire canopy ablaze. Their destructive meddling did not merely destroy trees; it shattered the fragile elemental balance beneath the earth.",sp=0},{t="Unleashed Fury",b="The venture did not go as planned for the goblins. The conflagration and deep excavation stirred ancient, dormant spirits of fire, stone, and fury from the depths. These enraged elementals swiftly turned on the trespassers, driving the Venture Company back and claiming the smoldering crater as their own. Kaela Shadowspear laments that until these chaotic elementals are culled, nature can never begin to recover.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Enraged Spirits?",a="Kaela Shadowspear, a night elf sentinel stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains, gives this quest to Alliance adventurers seeking to aid the land.",al={"quest giver","where to get enraged spirits","who starts enraged spirits"}},{q="Why are the fire elementals rampaging in the Charred Vale?",a="The Venture Company clear-cut and torched the forest using destructive machinery. Their invasive industrial methods disrupted the earth and unleashed dormant spirits of flame, stone, and rage that quickly overran the area.",al={"why are there elementals here","what caused the fire elementals","charred vale fire spirits"}},{q="What happened to the Venture Company in the Charred Vale?",a="The goblins ignited the forest, but their carelessness unleashed elementals far more dangerous than anticipated. The furious fiery beings overwhelmed their operations, leaving behind ruined camps and blazing wreckage.",al={"venture co fate","did goblins die in charred vale","venture co charred vale"}},{q="What are Smoldering Embers?",a="Smoldering Embers are the burning remnants collected from destroyed fire elementals in the Charred Vale, brought back to Kaela Shadowspear as physical proof that their chaotic numbers have been culled.",al={"smoldering embers lore","what are embers for","embers of enraged spirits"}},{q="Can the Charred Vale ever recover?",a="Kaela Shadowspear believes the land has no chance of feeling Elune's blessing or recovering while hostile elementals wander the ashes. Removing these rampaging spirits is the first step toward any eventual healing.",al={"will charred vale heal","healing the charred vale","can the vale be saved"}},{q="Where is the Charred Vale located?",a="The Charred Vale lies in the southwestern region of the Stonetalon Mountains, marked by blackened earth, burned timber, and roaming elemental spirits.",al={"charred vale location","how to find charred vale","where are the elementals"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the devastation of the Charred Vale is a heartbreaking wound inflicted on Kalimdor's sacred wildlands by unchecked industrial avarice.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view the rampaging fire elementals as a catastrophic disruption of nature's equilibrium, requiring active intervention before life can return to the soil.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman understand that the elementals' wrath is a direct, agonizing reaction to the reckless exploitation of the earth by mortal miners and loggers.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance works through night elf sentinels in Stonetalon to contain the chaos caused by goblin cartels and restore safety to the mountain passes."},kw={"charred vale","elune","enraged spirits","fire elementals","kaela shadowspear","smoldering embers","stonetalon mountains","venture co"},rel={"subzone:charred-vale","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:764","zone:stonetalon","topic:elune"},m={start="Kaela Shadowspear",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=1083},src={"Enraged Spirits"}}
E["quest:1084"] = {t="quest",n="Wounded Ancients",z="stonetalon",s="Wounded Ancients is an Alliance task given by Kaela Shadowspear in the Stonetalon Mountains. Suspecting that goblin munitions drove the local forest guardians mad, Kaela sends adventurers to recover shrapnel lodged in the corrupted treants so the gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle can analyze the taint.",h="Wounded Ancients is an Alliance task given by Kaela Shadowspear in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Blighted Protectors",b="The forested groves of Stonetalon were long watched over by towering treants, gentle yet ferocious guardians bound to the health of the land. When the Venture Company moved in with buzzsaws, explosives, and strip-mining operations, nature fought back. The treants successfully repelled the invaders from parts of the vale, but victory came at an insidious cost. The defenders did not return to peaceful guardianship; instead, they devolved into hostile, maddened husks.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Investigation",b="Kaela Shadowspear, an Alliance scout stationed in the mountains, believes the treants' decline is no natural sickness. The gnome engineer Gaxim Rustfizzle suspects the culprit lies in the chemical and mechanical arsenal used by the goblins during their chaotic retreat. By prying corroded shrapnel from the wounded wood-beasts, Gaxim hopes to determine whether Venture Company ordnance is actively poisoning Stonetalon's ancient protectors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Wounded Ancients?",a="Kaela Shadowspear gives the quest. She is an Alliance operative monitoring the escalating strife and ecological damage within the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"wounded ancients questgiver","who gives wounded ancients","kaela shadowspear quest"}},{q="Why are the treants corrupted?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle suspects that toxic munitions and weaponry fired by the Venture Company during their chaotic retreat lodged in the treants, steadily poisoning and maddening the forest guardians.",al={"why are treants mad","stonetalon treants corrupted","treant corruption source"}},{q="What item must be retrieved for this task?",a="You need to retrieve a piece of Corroded Shrapnel, embedded within the bark and flesh of the wounded treants wandering the area.",al={"wounded ancients item","corroded shrapnel quest"}},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim is an Alliance-aligned gnome engineer assisting Kaela Shadowspear. He uses his mechanical expertise to inspect Venture Company technology and determine how their weapons corrupt natural life.",al={"gaxim","gnome in stonetalon","gaxim rustfizzle role"}},{q="What is the Venture Company's presence in Stonetalon?",a="The Venture Company is a ruthless goblin logging and mining syndicate that invaded Stonetalon to clearcut sacred woodlands and plunder mineral deposits without regard for local balance.",al={"venture co stonetalon","why are goblins in stonetalon"}},{q="Does collecting the shrapnel heal the treants?",a="No. The retrieved shrapnel is purely an analytical sample intended for Gaxim to examine the nature and origin of the toxin rather than an immediate cure for the corrupted guardians.",al={"can you cure treants","do treants recover"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Watching ancient woodland defenders rot and twist under goblin industry is an outrage to any Kaldorei dedicated to safeguarding Kalimdor's wilderness.",["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle's analytical eye demonstrates that mechanical craft can be wielded to understand and diagnose environmental crimes committed by irresponsible engineers.",["class:Druid"]="Treants represent the living pulse of nature; extracting the foreign metal poisoning their flesh is a grim necessity in confronting Venture Company destruction.",["profession:Engineering"]="The corroded metal recovered from the treants highlights the destructive, slapdash nature of Venture Company munitions compared to refined gnomish craftsmanship."},kw={"corroded shrapnel","corruption","gaxim rustfizzle","kaela shadowspear","stonetalon","treants","venture co","wounded ancients"},rel={"npc:kaela-shadowspear","zone:stonetalon","quest:764","topic:gnome","topic:goblin"},m={start="Kaela Shadowspear",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1084},src={"Wounded Ancients"}}
E["quest:1085"] = {t="quest",n="On Guard in Stonetalon",z="stonetalon",s="On Guard in Stonetalon directs Alliance travelers from Kaela Shadowspear to Gaxim Rustfizzle at Stonetalon Peak. Facing rampant despoilment by the Venture Company, an otherwise unlikely pair—a cautious night elf sentinel and an eccentric gnome tinkerer—join forces to safeguard the mountain pass.",h="On Guard in Stonetalon directs Alliance travelers from Kaela Shadowspear to Gaxim Rustfizzle at Stonetalon...",sec={{t="An Unlikely Alliance",b="Night elves and gnomes rarely share common ground, especially when it comes to technology and the natural world. In the crags of Stonetalon Mountains, however, necessity bridges the cultural gulf. With the rapacious Venture Company carving out the wilderness and felling ancient trees, the sentinel Kaela Shadowspear has recognized that pure martial prowess alone cannot overcome industrialized pillaging. Welcoming gnome ingenuity into sacred Kaldorei territory demonstrates just how precarious the situation has become.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Philosophy",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle represents the eccentric pragmatism of the Alliance's smaller allies. While night elf society famously turned its back on arcane excess millennia ago, Gaxim believes that abstaining from magic and technical innovation leaves them vulnerable. By pairing alchemy and engineering with a touch of arcane discipline, Gaxim aims to convince his Kaldorei hosts that practical science can defend nature just as effectively as bow and glaive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are a night elf and a gnome working together here?",a="The Venture Company's destructive deforestation and resource extraction in Stonetalon are so severe that Kaela Shadowspear accepted outside aid. Gaxim brings engineering and alchemical expertise that the night elves typically lack, providing technical support to counter modern industrial machinery.",al={"why is gaxim with kaela","kaela and gaxim","gnome night elf alliance"}},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim is an adventurous gnome engineer and tinkerer stationed at Stonetalon Peak. He believes strongly that the night elves' strict aversion to arcane magic leaves them disadvantaged, seeking to prove that combining engineering, alchemy, and controlled magic can solve even the direst threats.",al={"gaxim rustfizzle lore","who is gaxim","gnome at stonetalon peak"}},{q="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is a night elf sentinel tasked with maintaining watch and defense over the Stonetalon Mountains. She serves as a regional commander coordinating resistance against the Venture Company.",al={"kaela shadowspear","who is kaela"}},{q="What threat is the Venture Company posing in Stonetalon?",a="The Venture Company is an unscrupulous mercantile syndicate cutting down sacred forests, operating destructive drilling rigs, and polluting pristine lands across Stonetalon for rapid commercial profit.",al={"venture co stonetalon","why fight venture co"}},{q="Who is Tara, mentioned by Kaela?",a="Tara is a night elf contact and quest giver stationed at Astranaar in Ashenvale, who originally dispatched Alliance messengers and scouts into Stonetalon to assess the situation.",al={"tara stonetalon","send you back to tara"}},{q="Where does this task lead next?",a="After speaking with Gaxim Rustfizzle, he offers 'A Gnome's Respite,' enlisting your aid to secure local supplies and further test his technical solutions against the hazards of the region.",al={"quest after on guard in stonetalon","next quest after gaxim"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle proudly represents gnomish ingenuity in Kalimdor, using his presence to demonstrate that science, engineering, and magic can overcome challenges where ancient traditions falter.",["race:NightElf"]="For Kaldorei sentinels, trusting a gnome tinkerer who advocates combining engineering with magic requires swallowing considerable pride, reflecting just how devastating the Venture Company's logging operations have become.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gaxim's mission underscores the practical utility of engineering in frontline reconnaissance and ecosystem defense, proving that cogwheels can serve conservation when turned against unchecked exploitation.",["faction:Alliance"]="This partnership showcases the broader Alliance ethos in action, as Eastern Kingdoms expertise blends with Kalimdor sentinels to stem shared threats across the frontier."},kw={"engineering","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome","kaela shadowspear","night elf","stonetalon","stonetalon peak","venture co"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:1071","quest:1070","quest:764","zone:stonetalon","topic:gnome","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Kaela Shadowspear",["end"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1085},src={"On Guard in Stonetalon (2)"}}
E["quest:1086"] = {t="quest",n="The Flying Machine Airport",z="stonetalon",s="Tasked by Apothecary Zamah from Thunder Bluff, Horde adventurers hunt down a hidden Venture Company landing pad nestled above Stonetalon Mountains. Carrying an alchemical Toxic Fogger, operatives must slip into the heart of the goblin logging operations to gas their air transit hub. The mission strikes directly at the cartel's communications while underscoring the ruthless methods of the Royal Apothecary Society.",h="Tasked by Apothecary Zamah from Thunder Bluff, Horde adventurers hunt down a hidden Venture Company landing...",sec={{t="A Silent Delivery",b="While the tauren seek to protect Stonetalon from deforestation and ravaging machinery, the Forsaken bring an entirely different philosophy to the front. Apothecary Zamah crafts a lethal compound designed to disrupt the Venture Company's logistics. Rather than attacking foot soldiers or loggers directly, she targets the cartel's link to the outside world: a rumored copter pad used to ferry light cargo and messages between Stonetalon and distant corporate offices.",sp=0},{t="Cragpool's Sky Port",b="Hidden high in the Cragpool Lake area south of the great waterwheel sits the Venture Company's copter pad, perched above the soot and chopped timber. It is small, meant for lightweight flying machines rather than massive zeppelins. Setting off the Toxic Fogger directly upon the pad ensures that any pilot, courier, or mechanic operating the machinery is smothered in deadly vapor before they can alert their commanders.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Pragmatism",b="Upon receiving news of the bombing, Apothecary Zamah makes no apology for utilizing chemical warfare against the goblins. In her eyes, the Venture Company deserves far worse for what they do to the land. More importantly, she offers the Horde a fundamental lesson from Undercity doctrine: never shy from dark paths if they lead toward ultimate victory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the flying machine airport located?",a="The Venture Company copter pad is located in the Cragpool Lake region of the Stonetalon Mountains. You will find the elevated wooden structure south of the massive industrial waterwheel, overlooking the lake's southern bend.",al={"where is the airport","copter pad location","where is sky port","venture co landing pad"}},{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah want this site poisoned?",a="Zamah wants to sever the Venture Company's communications and light supply lines between Stonetalon and their remote headquarters. By contaminating the copter pad, she hopes the toxin will cripple goblin flight crews and potentially hitch a ride back to their corporate leaders.",al={"why bomb the airport","why toxic fogger","zamah motive"}},{q="Who is Apothecary Zamah?",a="Apothecary Zamah is an emissary of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff. She studies Kalimdor's flora and fauna while developing alchemical weapons on behalf of the Forsaken and the Horde.",al={"zamah identity","who is zamah","undead in thunder bluff"}},{q="Why is the Horde using chemical weapons here?",a="The Forsaken fight with pragmatic ruthlessness. Although their tauren allies prefer spiritual healing and direct defense of the earth, Zamah believes the Venture Company's destructive greed warrants merciless tactics, teaching that victory matters above sentimental restraint.",al={"horde using plague","why poison goblins","is this plague"}},{q="What kind of aircraft does the Venture Company use here?",a="The platform is sized for small goblin flying machines and gyro-copters rather than full-sized zeppelins. These agile craft allow the cartel to quickly bypass Stonetalon's rugged mountain passes to haul high-priority messages and cargo.",al={"venture co copters","what flying machine","goblin aircraft stonetalon"}},{q="What happens after the fogger is deployed?",a="Once you release the fogger at the top of the pad, you flee before the vapors overtake you. Zamah considers the deployment a success and anticipates that the poison will severely disrupt goblin logistics.",al={"fogger outcome","after placing fogger"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, deploying the Toxic Fogger in Stonetalon is business as usual, demonstrating to Kalimdor that Undercity's alchemical genius can solve problems brute force cannot.",["race:Tauren"]="While your people abhor the Venture Company's destruction of Stonetalon, utilizing chemical toxins under the advice of a Forsaken apothecary tests the balance between earth-mother reverence and harsh battlefield pragmatism.",["profession:Engineering"]="The goblin copter pad displays the crude, utilitarian engineering that powers the Venture Company's rapid transit across rugged mountain ranges.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Stonetalon requires cutting off the Venture Company from external aid, and striking their air transit is a critical logistical blow."},kw={"airport","apothecary zamah","copter pad","cragpool lake","flying machine","stonetalon","thunder bluff","toxic fogger","venture co"},rel={"quest:1067","quest:853","subzone:cragpool-lake","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","zone:thunderbluff","topic:forsaken","topic:goblin"},m={start="Apothecary Zamah",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1086},src={"The Flying Machine Airport"}}
E["quest:1087"] = {t="quest",n="Cenarius' Legacy",z="stonetalon",s="Cenarius' Legacy is a Horde task handed out by Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Frustrated by the natural wards maintained by the night elves and the children of Cenarius, the Forsaken mage seeks to cull their numbers at Stonetalon Peak to restore the raw flow of magic. For the Horde, striking at the Cenarion defenders also weakens the regional Alliance presence.",h="Cenarius' Legacy is a Horde task handed out by Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="Stifled Currents",b="Braelyn Firehand resides in the hills near Sun Rock Retreat, festering with frustration at Stonetalon's natural environment. According to her, the druids of the Cenarion Circle and the demigod Cenarius's offspring actively suppress and choke the arcane currents of the land. Describing the process of channeling power here as drawing water with a perforated bucket, she hungers to strip away their natural defenses so raw magical energy can surge unimpeded once again.",sp=0},{t="A Strike at Stonetalon Peak",b="To weaken this verdant stranglehold, Braelyn enlists Horde champions to venture north to Stonetalon Peak. There, around the ancient kaldorei groves and temple grounds, patrol the Cenarion Botanists alongside the proud Sons and Daughters of Cenarius. Striking down these wardens serves a dual purpose: it dismantles the wards muffling Braelyn's spellcraft and deals a bloody blow to the night elf enclave threatening the Horde's foothold in the mountains.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Shadow Council",b="While Braelyn presents her grievance as an issue of magical convenience, her true loyalties lie in darker corners. She longs to return to Jaedenar, the corrupted stronghold of the Shadow Council concealed in Felwood to the north, but notes that her unseen master forbids her return until her work in Stonetalon is complete. The Horde aids her out of territorial expediency, often unaware of the sinister cult pulling her strings.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Braelyn Firehand?",a="Braelyn Firehand is a Forsaken spellcaster camped in the crags near Sun Rock Retreat. Though she accepts assistance from the Horde to clear out the night elf presence in Stonetalon, she serves a hidden master based out of Jaedenar in Felwood.",al={"braelyn firehand lore","who is the quest giver","braelyn"},sp=1},{q="Why does Braelyn want the children of Cenarius dead?",a="She claims that the druidic magic practiced by the kaldorei botanists and Cenarius's offspring actively suppresses the flow of raw arcane power across the mountains. Eliminating them weakens the grove's wards and allows magic to flow freely into her grasp.",al={"why kill sons of cenarius","why hate cenarion botanists","why does braelyn hate them"}},{q="Where are the targets located?",a="The Sons of Cenarius, Daughters of Cenarius, and Cenarion Botanists are concentrated far to the north at Stonetalon Peak, guarding the ancestral ruins, groves, and moonwells maintained by the night elves.",al={"where are sons of cenarius","stonetalon peak mob locations","where to find cenarion botanists"}},{q="What is Jaedenar, which Braelyn mentions?",a="Jaedenar is a deep canyon and cave complex located in Felwood, heavily corrupted by the Burning Legion and currently serving as the central base of operations for the Shadow Council in Kalimdor.",al={"what is jaedenar","braelyn master jaedenar","jaedenar connection"}},{q="Why is the Horde willing to help Braelyn attack Cenarion defenders?",a="The night elves at Stonetalon Peak are directly aligned with the Alliance and contest the Horde's expansion throughout the Stonetalon Mountains. Weakening their grove secures the region for the Horde, regardless of Braelyn's personal motives.",al={"why does horde kill cenarion circle","horde conflict stonetalon peak"}},{q="What happens after completing Cenarius' Legacy?",a="Once the initial wardens fall, Braelyn sends you back to Stonetalon Peak to assassinate Keeper Ordanus, the powerful keeper of the grove overseeing the sanctuary.",al={"quest after cenarius legacy","what is next in the chain","ordanus questline"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Tauren druids, butchering Cenarius's offspring and Cenarion Circle botanists is an uncomfortable and deeply divisive act, underscoring the tragic friction between faction loyalty and the sacred ways of nature.",["class:Mage"]="Braelyn's complaints strike a chord with arcane practitioners who recognize the friction between ancient kaldorei warding and free-flowing ley energies, even if her reckless zeal verges on obsession.",["faction:Horde"]="Stonetalon Peak represents the largest bastion of Alliance and kaldorei strength in the mountain chain; clearing out its defenders is vital for safeguarding Sun Rock Retreat and the Greatwood Vale."},kw={"braelyn firehand","cenarion botanist","cenarius' legacy","daughter of cenarius","jaedenar","ordanus","son of cenarius","stonetalon peak","sun rock retreat"},rel={"npc:braelyn-firehand","quest:1088","quest:1089","subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:jaedenar","topic:cenarius","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Braelyn Firehand",level="25",faction="Horde",id=1087},src={"Cenarius' Legacy"}}
E["quest:1088"] = {t="quest",n="Ordanus",z="stonetalon",s="Braelyn Firehand at Sunrock Retreat uses her arcane sight to track down Keeper Ordanus, an elder son of Cenarius who fled Stonetalon Peak. Believing his people desecrated ancient Highborne ruins, she sends Horde champions across the border into Ashenvale to take his head.",h="Braelyn Firehand at Sunrock Retreat uses her arcane sight to track down Keeper Ordanus, an elder son of...",sec={{t="A Hunt Driven by Ancient Grudges",b="Braelyn Firehand arrived in Stonetalon Mountains on orders from her master to reclaim the sacred ruins of Azshara's ancient temples. She found the night elves already occupying the peak, treating the relics of her Highborne forebears as wilderness to be contained. Her chief target, Keeper Ordanus, fled before she could corner him, slipping across the border into Ashenvale. Using her arcane vision, Braelyn scried his hiding place high in a wooden refuge at Raynewood Retreat and enlisted the Horde to finish the hunt.",sp=0},{t="The Scion of the Forest God",b="Ordanus is counted among the eldest sons of Cenarius, possessing deep ties to the wild magics of Kalimdor. Night elf guardians moved him from Stonetalon Peak to Raynewood Retreat, seeking to protect him from the arcane forces encroaching upon sacred groves. Defended by loyal Cenarion Vindicators and summoned woodland treants, the keeper represents both the ancient authority of the forest demigod and a living obstacle to Braelyn's vengeance.",sp=0},{t="Highborne Vengeance",b="For Braelyn Firehand, claiming Ordanus's head is deeply personal rather than merely tactical. She openly recalls knowing him centuries ago, remembering the arrogance with which Cenarius's offspring looked down upon the Highborne and their mastery of the arcane. Severing his head serves to avenge ancient slights and clear the path for her master's deeper designs in Kalimdor's wilderness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Ordanus?",a="Ordanus is a keeper of the grove and one of the eldest sons of the demigod Cenarius. He was initially stationed near Stonetalon Peak before fleeing into Ashenvale to escape Highborne vengeance.",al={"ordanus lore","who is ordanus","who is keeper ordanus"}},{q="Where can Keeper Ordanus be found?",a="Ordanus resides at the top of a massive hollow tree structure in Raynewood Retreat, located along the road through central Ashenvale.",al={"ordanus location","where is ordanus","raynewood retreat tree"}},{q="Why does Braelyn Firehand want Ordanus dead?",a="Braelyn views night elf presence in Stonetalon as a desecration of ancient Highborne temple ruins. She also holds a long-standing personal hatred toward Ordanus, remembering him as arrogant and dismissive of her people in ages past.",al={"why kill ordanus","braelyn grudge","why does braelyn want ordanus"}},{q="Who is Braelyn Firehand's master?",a="Braelyn speaks of serving a master who directed her to the peak of Stonetalon to reclaim the ancient temple ruins of Azshara, though she keeps the master's exact identity guarded.",al={"braelyn master","who sent braelyn","braelyns master"}},{q="How does this conflict fit into the Horde's presence in Stonetalon?",a="Horde forces stationed at Sunrock Retreat frequently clash with night elf sentinels and Cenarion protectors for territory and resources across Stonetalon and Ashenvale, making Braelyn's strike against a Cenarion leader mutually beneficial.",al={"why does horde help braelyn","stonetalon horde motives"}},{q="What happens after Ordanus is slain?",a="Once Ordanus is dead, Braelyn rewards the champion and directs them toward The Den, delving further into the surrounding threats across the Stonetalon peaks.",al={"what next after ordanus","quest after ordanus","the den next"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Striking down an elder son of Cenarius weakens night elf authority across the Ashenvale-Stonetalon border, aiding Horde expansion into contested timberlands.",["class:Mage"]="Braelyn Firehand represents the unyielding arcane pride of the Highborne, asserting arcane supremacy over Cenarion natural philosophy.",["class:Druid"]="Horde druids face a grim dilemma in this task, taking the life of a direct son of Cenarius to fulfill a blood elf's ancient feud."},kw={"ashenvale","braelyn firehand","cenarius","highborne","ordanus","raynewood retreat","stonetalon","sunrock retreat"},rel={"npc:braelyn-firehand","quest:1087","quest:1089","subzone:raynewood-retreat","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","topic:cenarius","topic:highborne"},m={start="Braelyn Firehand",level="29",faction="Horde",id=1088},src={"Ordanus (quest)"}}
E["quest:1089"] = {t="quest",n="The Den",z="stonetalon",s="The Den is the culmination of a Horde infiltration campaign against night elf druids entrenched on Stonetalon Peak. Directed by the blood elf operative Braelyn Firehand, champions delve into the Talon Den's subterranean barrow chambers to crack a layered security system and plunder the druids' hidden relics.",h="The Den is the culmination of a Horde infiltration campaign against night elf druids entrenched on Stonetalon...",sec={{t="Subterranean Secrets",b="Perched upon the highest reaches of the Stonetalon Mountains, the Talon Den serves as an underground redoubt for night elf druids. Carved deep into living stone, these barrow halls are designed to shield meditating guardians and shelter sacred treasures away from prying eyes. Knowing the strategic and arcane value of what rests within, Braelyn Firehand interrogates a captured druid to pry loose the secrets of their defenses.",sp=0},{t="The Layered Locks",b="To safeguard their most potent relics, the druids devised an intricate mechanism rather than trusting a single door. At the threshold of the barrow chambers, hidden inside a humble lantern, lies the Gatekeeper's Key. This initial key unlocks three dispersed caches deeper in the complex—yielding the Sleepers' Key, the Claw Key, and the Barrow Key. Only when all three carved stones are turned in the central hoard do the druidic seals dissolve, surrendering their ancient items to Horde hands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Talon Den?",a="The Talon Den is a subterranean night elf barrow complex carved into the heights of Stonetalon Peak. It serves as both a meditation sanctuary for resting druids and a secure repository for their sacred relics.",al={"where is talon den","what is the den","stonetalon barrow den"}},{q="Who orders the infiltration of the Talon Den?",a="Braelyn Firehand, a Sin'dorei operative working alongside the Horde in the Stonetalon Mountains, orchestrates the raid. Having extracted crucial intel from an unfortunate druid captive, she directs Horde agents to bypass the sanctuary's wards and loot its hoard.",al={"who gives the den quest","braelyn firehand purpose","who sent me to the den"}},{q="How do the keys inside the Den work?",a="A primary Gatekeeper's Key is stashed inside a lantern near the entrance. That key opens three scattered caches inside the barrow, yielding the Sleepers' Key, Claw Key, and Barrow Key. When inserted together into the carved stone hoard, the wards dispel.",al={"how to open talon den hoard","gatekeepers key use","three keys stonetalon"}},{q="Why are the druids on Stonetalon Peak being targeted?",a="The Horde's expansion into Stonetalon has caused fierce territorial conflict with the native night elves. Infiltrating the peak neutralizes their druidic leadership, such as Ordanus, while stripping them of valuable arcane and natural artifacts.",al={"why attack stonetalon druids","horde reason for killing ordanus","why loot the den"}},{q="What is inside the Talon Den Hoard?",a="The hoard contains powerful relics and treasures gathered by the night elf druids. Sealed beneath layered wards, these items were kept safe from foreign intrusion until their security sequence was coerced by Braelyn.",al={"talon den hoard loot lore","what is in the hoard","what did the druids hide"}},{q="What happened right before this quest?",a="Before breaking into the Den, Horde adventurers are tasked with investigating the night elf presence in Cenarius' Legacy and assassinating the keeper Ordanus to fracture the defenders' command.",al={"den quest chain","what leads to the den","prerequisites for the den"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Raiding the Talon Den breaks the night elves' defensive spine atop Stonetalon Peak, securing the mountain approaches and seizing potent magical relics for the Horde.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of the Talon Den marks a grim violation of sacred barrow sanctuaries, seeing the ancient sleep of Cenarion guardians disrupted and their ward-locked relics plundered.",["class:Druid"]="Tauren druids of the Horde face a bitter irony here, turning keys designed around traditional barrow architecture—named for Sleepers, Claws, and Barrows—against fellow Cenarion keepers.",["class:Rogue"]="Navigating the shadowy halls of the barrow to lift keys from hidden lanterns and torch brackets calls on keen infiltration and subterfuge."},kw={"barrow key","braelyn firehand","cenarius' legacy","claw key","gatekeeper's key","ordanus","sleepers' key","stonetalon peak","talon den","talon den hoard"},rel={"quest:1088","quest:1087","npc:braelyn-firehand","subzone:stonetalon-peak","zone:stonetalon","topic:druid","topic:cenarius"},m={start="Braelyn Firehand",["end"]="Talon Den Hoard",level="29",faction="Horde",id=1089},src={"The Den (quest)"}}
E["quest:1090"] = {t="quest",n="Gerenzo's Orders",z="stonetalon",s="At the Venture Company dig site in Stonetalon Mountains, an ousted goblin named Piznik schemes to expose his new boss, Gerenzo. By defending Piznik from camp patrols while he extracts a strange gold-green ore, adventurers help uncover the lucrative secrets behind the company's aggressive excavation.",h="At the Venture Company dig site in Stonetalon Mountains, an ousted goblin named Piznik schemes to expose his...",sec={{t="Corporate Betrayal in the Crag",b="The Venture Company's massive operations within Stonetalon rely on cutthroat competition, where promotions are won through ruthlessness rather than loyalty. Piznik once enjoyed the status of being second-in-command at the excavation until Gerenzo seized power, ousted supervisor Ziz Fizziks, and demoted Piznik to swinging a pick in the dirt. Rather than walking away, Piznik stayed on as an informant under Ziz's instructions, watching Gerenzo's every move and biding his time to strike back at his treacherous new supervisor.",sp=0},{t="Unearthing the Gold-Green Vein",b="Gerenzo's sudden takeover is driven by an obsession with a mysterious gold-green ore running through the Stonetalon rocks. Believing the mineral holds extraordinary commercial value, Gerenzo ordered miners to rip massive quantities out of the earth. Suspecting that Ziz Fizziks's mysterious new employer will pay handsomely for information on the venture, Piznik risks discovery to dig up a pristine sample while reliant on an ally to fend off aggressive diggers, vermin, and overseers who police the operation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Piznik?",a="Piznik is a goblin laborer at the Windshear Crag operation in the Stonetalon Mountains. He was once the second most important manager at the dig site under Ziz Fizziks, but after Gerenzo seized control, Piznik was demoted to working the mines as simple labor.",al={"piznik","who is the goblin miner","piznik stonetalon"}},{q="Why is Piznik mining this ore secretly?",a="Piznik is secretly gathering a sample of a strange gold-green mineral that Gerenzo has ordered harvested in huge quantities. His former boss, Ziz Fizziks, promised that his new employer will pay generously for intelligence on whatever valuable operation Gerenzo is running.",al={"why mine ore","mysterious ore","gold green ore"}},{q="Who is Gerenzo?",a="Gerenzo is the ruthless Venture Company supervisor who took control of the Stonetalon excavation by firing Ziz Fizziks. He immediately redirected company resources toward aggressively excavating an unfamiliar, valuable gold-green ore found throughout the crag.",al={"gerenzo","who is gerenzo","gerenzo venture co"}},{q="Who does Ziz Fizziks work for now?",a="After getting fired by Gerenzo, Ziz Fizziks allied with new backers interested in monitoring Venture Company activities in the region. He pays operatives and informants like Piznik to sabotage Gerenzo and uncover what the Venture Company is unearthing.",al={"ziz new boss","who hired ziz","ziz employer"}},{q="What attacks Piznik while he digs?",a="The noise and illicit activity quickly attract local cave vermin, Windshear diggers, geomancers, and company overseers who patrol the dig site to prevent theft and keep laborers under tight control.",al={"piznik ambush","who attacks piznik","windshear patrols"}},{q="What happens once the sample is mined?",a="Once Piznik successfully extracts the ore sample, he gives it to his protector to deliver directly to Ziz Fizziks, hoping it provides the leverage needed to thwart Gerenzo's ambitious plans.",al={"where to take ore","what to do with the sample"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The strange gold-green ore discovered by Venture Company miners in Stonetalon does not match conventional iron or tin veins, piquing the curiosity of any prospector interested in rare minerals.",["faction:Horde"]="The Venture Company's reckless, invasive mining despoils Stonetalon's natural landscape, making any effort to monitor, disrupt, or exploit their operations useful to Horde forces nearby."},kw={"gerenzo","gold-green ore","mysterious ore","piznik","stonetalon mountains","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"npc:piznik","quest:1483","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Piznik",level="22",id=1090},src={"Gerenzo's Orders"}}
E["quest:1091"] = {t="quest",n="Kaela's Update",z="stonetalon",s="Kaela's Update is an Alliance dispatch in the Stonetalon Mountains, carrying captured correspondence between frontline operatives. The gnome mage Gaxim Rustfizzle sends the adventurer back to Kaela Shadowspear with intercepted Venture Company letters. The intelligence helps the night elf Sentinels track the goblin cartel's destructive expansion across sacred lands.",h="Kaela's Update is an Alliance dispatch in the Stonetalon Mountains, carrying captured correspondence between...",sec={{t="A Messenger in the Mountains",b="After assisting the gnome mage Gaxim Rustfizzle in uncovering the movements of the Venture Company, he compiles recovered letters detailing the cartel's operations. Not one to pass up credit, Gaxim sends the player directly back to Kaela Shadowspear, the night elf Sentinel coordinator stationed in Stonetalon Peak. He makes sure to remind the courier to mention how his magical prowess made the investigation a success.",sp=0},{t="Eyes of the Sentinels",b="The Sentinels stationed in Stonetalon watch the crags with growing concern. While Horde forces contest the lower trails, the Venture Company's clear-cutting and mining apparatus pose an immediate ecological and tactical threat. The letters recovered by Gaxim grant Kaela valuable insights into the cartel's internal communications, bolstering the Alliance's defensive planning along the ridges.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaela Shadowspear?",a="Kaela Shadowspear is an Alliance-aligned night elf Sentinel officer stationed at Stonetalon Peak. She oversees scouting and defensive efforts against both the encroaching Horde and the destructive ventures of goblin mining companies in the mountains.",al={"kaela shadowspear","who is kaela","kaela stonetalon"}},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an energetic gnome mage based in the Stonetalon Mountains. He uses his arcane skills to investigate and disrupt Venture Company operations, cooperating closely with the local night elf Sentinels.",al={"gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle","gnome mage stonetalon"}},{q="What is in the Venture Company letters?",a="The letters contain internal Venture Company communications intercepted during operations against their camps. They provide Kaela Shadowspear and the Sentinels with crucial intelligence on the cartel's local logistics, excavations, and resource stripping.",al={"venture co letters","what are the letters","letters for kaela"}},{q="Why are the Sentinels concerned about the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company clear-cuts sacred forests and scars the earth with reckless mining machinery. To the Sentinels, this relentless industrialization is an affront to nature and a direct threat to the sanctity of Stonetalon.",al={"why care about goblins","sentinels venture co","venture company stonetalon"}},{q="Where does this quest start and end?",a="The quest begins with Gaxim Rustfizzle along the mountain pathways and finishes with Kaela Shadowspear at the Alliance outpost of Stonetalon Peak.",al={"quest location","turn in kaela update","where is kaela"}},{q="Does this quest lead to further investigations?",a="Delivering the letters keeps the Sentinels informed of the cartel's activities, allowing Kaela to plan further military responses and reconnaissance throughout the Stonetalon range.",al={"next quest","what comes after kaela update","follow up quest"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Delivering intercepted Venture Company correspondence bolsters the fragile Alliance foothold at Stonetalon Peak against corporate pillaging.",["race:NightElf"]="Every scrap of intelligence gathered against the Venture Company helps the Sentinels protect Kalimdor's scarred wilderness from industrial defilement.",["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle proudly represents gnomish arcane ingenuity, making certain his night elf allies recognize the indispensable value of gnome magic."},kw={"gaxim rustfizzle","kaela shadowspear","kaela's update","letters","sentinels","stonetalon peak","venture co"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:764","topic:sentinels","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",["end"]="Kaela Shadowspear",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1091},src={"Kaela's Update"}}
E["quest:1092"] = {t="quest",n="Gerenzo's Orders",z="stonetalon",s="Having eliminated Chief Engineer Gerenzo and secured a sample of strange ore, Piznik dispatches adventurers to take the specimen to his contact, Ziz Fizziks. The delivery wraps up a risky act of corporate espionage deep in the Venture Company operations of Windshear Crag.",h="Having eliminated Chief Engineer Gerenzo and secured a sample of strange ore, Piznik dispatches adventurers...",sec={{t="A Ticket Out",b="With Chief Engineer Gerenzo dead, Piznik knows his time among the Venture Company crew at Windshear Crag has expired. Corporate management in Undermine does not take kindly to internal sabotage and murder, prompting the nervous goblin to orchestrate his escape. Before slipping away to seek a new employer, he entrusts the Unidentified Ore secured from Gerenzo to an outsider, ensuring the prized specimen gets delivered safely without drawing suspicion to himself.",sp=0},{t="Corporate Curiosities",b="The ore's destination is Ziz Fizziks, who has established a secretive outpost on the western rim of Windshear Crag. Ziz recognizes the strategic value of the mineral, intending to send it south to Undermine engineers while quietly skimming a valuable fraction off the top for personal profit. Such self-serving pragmatism highlights the cutthroat nature of trade and engineering disputes simmering beneath the peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Piznik need to flee Windshear Crag?",a="Piznik orchestrated the assassination of his superior, Chief Engineer Gerenzo. He knows that once the Venture Company's higher-ups catch wind of the incident, retribution will be swift, so he must sneak away and secure new employment.",al={"why is piznik leaving","piznik runaway","why piznik scared"}},{q="Who is Ziz Fizziks?",a="Ziz Fizziks is a goblin operator camped on the western ridge of Windshear Crag. He planted Piznik inside the Venture Company to steal corporate intelligence and rare mineral samples.",al={"who is ziz","ziz fizziks role","where is ziz"}},{q="What is the Unidentified Ore?",a="It is a rare geological sample obtained from Chief Engineer Gerenzo. Ziz Fizziks intends to send it to researchers and engineers in Undermine to analyze its industrial applications.",al={"unidentified ore lore","what is the ore","gerenzo ore"}},{q="Where can Ziz Fizziks be found?",a="Ziz Fizziks hides at a small encampment perched along the western edge overlooking Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"ziz fizziks location","find ziz","where to turn in gerenzo orders"}},{q="What happens to the ore once Ziz receives it?",a="Ziz plans to forward the bulk of the ore sample to Undermine engineers for profit and reputation, while pocketing a small shard for himself without his employers' knowledge.",al={"what does ziz do with the ore","ziz keep the ore"}},{q="Is Piznik loyal to the Venture Company?",a="Piznik worked under the Venture Company only long enough to serve Ziz's interests. He shows no loyalty to the syndicate and actively fears retribution from its leadership.",al={"piznik faction","is piznik venture co","who does piznik work for"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The Unidentified Ore extracted from Gerenzo reveals that the Venture Company's deforesting operations in Windshear Crag are equally focused on scouring the mountains for unknown subterranean wealth.",["profession:Engineering"]="Goblin engineers in Undermine pay handsomely for unrefined, exotic ores capable of powering volatile new mechanisms and prototypes."},kw={"gerenzo's orders","piznik","stonetalon","undermine","unidentified ore","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1090","quest:1483","npc:piznik","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Piznik",["end"]="Ziz Fizziks",level="22",faction="Neutral",id=1092},src={"Gerenzo's Orders (2)"}}
E["quest:1093"] = {t="quest",n="Super Reaper 6000",z="stonetalon",s="Super Reaper 6000 is a quest offered by the disgruntled goblin tinkerer Ziz Fizziks in the Windshear Crag of the Stonetalon Mountains. Looking to curry favor with his new boss Sputtervalve, Ziz hires adventurers to infiltrate the local Venture Company logging operation and steal the schematic blueprints for a colossal woodcutting machine designed by his rival, the gnome Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle.",h="Super Reaper 6000 is a quest offered by the disgruntled goblin tinkerer Ziz Fizziks in the Windshear Crag of...",sec={{t="Industrial Espionage in Windshear Crag",b="The Venture Trading Company has carved an industrial scar straight into the heart of the Stonetalon Mountains, ruthlessly deforesting Windshear Crag. Yet beneath the smog and spinning blades lies petty corporate rivalry. Ziz Fizziks, a goblin engineer recently cast out of the Venture Company's ranks, has found employment with Sputtervalve. Eager to cement his position and show off his value, Ziz seeks to procure the Venture Company's most prized mechanical asset: the blueprints for their massive automated lumber engine, the Super Reaper 6000.",sp=0},{t="Goblins vs. Gnomish Engineering",b="Part of Ziz's burning resentment stems from pride. The Venture Company, nominally a goblin-dominated syndicate, broke tradition by putting a gnome, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, in charge of local engineering efforts. After the schematics are pried from the hands of the Venture Company machine operators, Ziz finds himself exasperated: the overly convoluted, perfectionist design philosophy of gnomish drafting is almost entirely incomprehensible to a goblin engineer used to brute force, cheap parts, and volatile combustion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ziz Fizziks?",a="Ziz Fizziks is a goblin engineer dwelling in the Stonetalon Mountains. Recently fired by the Venture Company, he was quickly recruited by Sputtervalve, an influential associate in the area, and now seeks payback against his former employers.",al={"ziz fizziks","who is the quest giver","ziz"}},{q="What is the Super Reaper 6000?",a="The Super Reaper 6000 is an enormous, mechanical woodcutting machine designed by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle for the Venture Company's logging operations in Windshear Crag.",al={"super reaper 6000","what is the super reaper","what machine is this"}},{q="Who designed the Super Reaper 6000?",a="It was designed by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a gnome tinkerer hired by the Venture Company, a fact that deeply offends the goblin engineers who used to run the site.",al={"who made the super reaper","who built the machine","gerenzo wrenchwhistle"}},{q="Why does Sputtervalve want the blueprints?",a="Sputtervalve wants access to the cutting-edge heavy logging technology developed by the Venture Company, and Ziz Fizziks is eager to provide them to prove his usefulness to his new employer.",al={"why steal the plans","sputtervalve blueprints"}},{q="Where are the blueprints found?",a="The schematics are carried by the Venture Company machine operators supervising the harvesting machinery in Windshear Crag.",al={"where do i find the plans","who drops the blueprints"}},{q="Why does Ziz struggle to read the blueprints once retrieved?",a="Goblin and gnomish engineering philosophies are notoriously incompatible. Ziz finds the meticulous, intricate diagrams of Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle overly confusing and impossible to decipher at a glance.",al={"why cant ziz read the plans","gnome blueprints goblin"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="This quest highlights the eternal rivalry between goblin pragmatism—explosive, fast, and rough—and gnomish design, which prizes over-engineered complexity and precision.",["race:Gnome"]="Ziz expresses utter disbelief that a goblin syndicate would trust a gnome to build their flagship machinery, only to find himself thoroughly baffled by the gnome's technical genius.",["race:NightElf"]="The Super Reaper 6000 represents the pinnacle of mortal disregard for nature, clear-cutting ancient trees in Stonetalon to feed the maw of industrial profit."},kw={"blueprints","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","sputtervalve","stonetalon mountains","super reaper 6000","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","quest:1483","quest:1094","topic:venture-company","topic:goblin","topic:gnome","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Ziz Fizziks",level="21",id=1093},src={"Super Reaper 6000 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1094"] = {t="quest",n="Further Instructions",z="stonetalon",s="Further Instructions is a delivery task connecting the chaotic logging operations of the Stonetalon Mountains to the trade hub of Ratchet. The disgruntled tinkerer Ziz Fizziks sends a courier with stolen blueprints and internal documents to his counterpart, Sputtervalve, aiming to turn corporate espionage into personal advantage.",h="Further Instructions is a delivery task connecting the chaotic logging operations of the Stonetalon Mountains...",sec={{t="Corporate Espionage",b="When Ziz Fizziks was booted out of the Venture Company's logging operations in the Windshear Crag, he did not leave empty-handed. Bitter over his dismissal, Fizziks snatched up an assortment of sensitive documents, internal manuals, and technical schematics, culminating in the prized blueprints for the experimental Super Reaper 6000. Desperate to find a buyer or ally willing to exploit the data, he sealed the gathered secrets into an envelope marked for Ratchet.",sp=0},{t="The Ratchet Connection",b="The recipient of the stolen documents is Sputtervalve, an engineer stationed within the neutral port of Ratchet in the Barrens. While Sputtervalve harbors little personal affection or trust for Fizziks, the rivalry with the Venture Company makes the offering impossible to refuse. The Steamwheedle-aligned goblins are constantly looking for ways to diminish their ruthless competitor's footprint while happily reverse-engineering any superior mechanical innovations they stumble across.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Sealed Envelope?",a="The envelope contains internal Venture Company documents, technical manuals, and blueprints for the Super Reaper 6000 that Ziz Fizziks stole when he was ousted from their logging operation.",al={"envelope contents","what is fizziks sending","stolen documents"}},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin engineer residing in Ratchet in the Barrens. Though he does not fully trust Ziz Fizziks, he is eager to weaken the Venture Company and examine their mechanical advancements.",al={"sputtervalve identity","who is the recipient","ratchet engineer"}},{q="Why is Ziz Fizziks working against the Venture Company?",a="Fizziks was unceremoniously kicked out of the Venture Company's ranks in Stonetalon. Spiteful and out for revenge, he began leaking their trade secrets to rivals.",al={"why fizziks betrayed venture co","fizziks motive"}},{q="Where can Sputtervalve be found?",a="Sputtervalve is stationed in the neutral port town of Ratchet, located along the eastern coast of the Barrens.",al={"where is sputtervalve","sputtervalve location","find sputtervalve"}},{q="Does Sputtervalve trust Ziz Fizziks?",a="No, Sputtervalve openly admits he does not trust Fizziks, but the value of the technical manuals and blueprints outweighs his wariness of the messenger.",al={"does sputtervalve trust fizziks","fizziks and sputtervalve relationship"}},{q="What is the Super Reaper 6000?",a="It is an advanced industrial shredder developed by the Venture Company to clear forests and process lumber at high speed, making its blueprints highly coveted.",al={"super reaper 6000","what is the machine","venture co reaper"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The envelope represents classic goblin industry at work: ruthless corporate espionage, patent theft, and reverse-engineering complex lumber harvesters.",["faction:Horde"]="Running stolen Venture Company plans to Ratchet helps fuel the simmering trade wars that undermine dangerous industrial encroachment near Horde territories."},kw={"barrens","further instructions","ratchet","sputtervalve","stonetalon","super reaper 6000","venture company","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1093","npc:sputtervalve","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","quest:1483"},m={start="Ziz Fizziks",["end"]="Sputtervalve",level="21",id=1094},src={"Further Instructions"}}
E["quest:1095"] = {t="quest",n="Further Instructions",z="stonetalon",s="Further Instructions marks an escalation in goblin corporate politics, ordering the assassination of a rogue gnome engineer hired by Mogul Razdunk. Sputtervalve delivers directives originating from high within Undermine, commanding Ziz Fizziks to eliminate Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle in the Stonetalon Mountains.",h="Further Instructions marks an escalation in goblin corporate politics, ordering the assassination of a rogue...",sec={{t="Corporate Disapproval",b="The Venture Company operates under ruthless profit motives, but hiring outsider talent can spark fierce internal friction. When Mogul Razdunk brought the gnome engineer Gerenzo into the fold, word reached Undermine and ruffled feathers among the ruling Trade Princes. Director Riddlevox instructed Sputtervalve to intervene and handle the situation quietly. Sputtervalve, deducing that the order stems from the highest trade authorities, passes down the dirty work to the operative closest to the scene: Ziz Fizziks.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of Dun Morogh",b="Upon receiving the assassination order, Ziz Fizziks eagerly embraces the mission. Goblin engineers harbor natural disdain for gnome rivals, but Gerenzo's personal history makes him an especially volatile figure. Before joining the Venture Company, Gerenzo was a head engineer in Gnomeregan involved in a top-secret endeavor that Undermine spies failed to fully uncover. That project reportedly ended in catastrophe, an explosive failure that sent Gerenzo fleeing across the sea to sell his dangerous expertise in Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin operative working under Director Riddlevox. Acting on directives from Undermine, he coordinates field operations and passes contracts down to ground agents like Ziz Fizziks.",al={"sputtervalve","who gives quest","quest giver sputtervalve"}},{q="Why do the Trade Princes care about Gerenzo?",a="The Trade Princes of Undermine strongly disapprove of Mogul Razdunk consorting with outside gnome engineers. Hiring high-profile non-goblins threatens internal goblin industrial dominance and invites unwelcome scrutiny.",al={"why do trade princes care","undermine anger","gerenzo trade princes"}},{q="What secret project did Gerenzo work on?",a="Gerenzo was a lead engineer in Gnomeregan working on a classified project that goblin spies could never penetrate. Whatever he built reportedly ended in catastrophic disaster, literally exploding in the faces of the engineers involved.",al={"gerenzo secret project","gnomeregan explosion","gerenzo past"}},{q="Where is Ziz Fizziks located?",a="Ziz Fizziks is stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains, keeping watch over local Venture Company logging and mining efforts while carrying out corporate contracts.",al={"ziz fizziks location","where is ziz","where to deliver orders"}},{q="Why is Ziz Fizziks eager to kill Gerenzo?",a="Beyond goblin professional hatred for gnomes, Fizziks recognizes Gerenzo as a hazardous rival whose botched experiments in Dun Morogh make him dangerous to everyone around him.",al={"why ziz hate gerenzo","fizziks reaction","why kill gerenzo"}},{q="Who is Mogul Razdunk?",a="Mogul Razdunk is the chief executive of the Venture Company. His decision to hire Gerenzo directly defied conventional trade etiquette in Undermine, triggering the Trade Princes to push for Gerenzo's elimination.",al={"mogul razdunk","who is razdunk","venture company boss"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The goblin operatives mention Gerenzo's past as a senior engineer in Gnomeregan whose secret experiment detonated catastrophically, hinting at the lingering fallout that contributed to the tinker city's downfall.",["profession:Engineering"]="The cutthroat rivalry between gnome and goblin engineering takes a literal turn here, shifting from design patent debates into outright corporate assassination."},kw={"further instructions","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","gnomeregan","razdunk","riddlevox","sputtervalve","stonetalon","undermine","venture company","ziz fizziks"},rel={"quest:1483","quest:1094","npc:sputtervalve","zone:stonetalon","topic:venture-company","zone:gnomeregan","zone:dunmorogh","topic:gnome"},m={start="Sputtervalve",["end"]="Ziz Fizziks",level="27",id=1095},src={"Further Instructions (2)"}}
E["quest:1096"] = {t="quest",n="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle",z="stonetalon",s="This bounty tasks Horde adventurers with eliminating Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a rogue gnome overseer perched high above Cragpool Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains. Gerenzo has heavily augmented his decaying flesh with gears, clockwork machinery, and artificial limbs. The goblin engineer Ziz Fizziks seeks his mechanical arm as indisputable proof of his demise to earn a coveted promotion from his superiors.",h="This bounty tasks Horde adventurers with eliminating Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a rogue gnome overseer perched...",sec={{t="A Monstrous Hybrid",b="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle is infamous even among veteran tinkerers for his gruesome physical transformations. By the account of those who have seen him, his natural flesh appears to be rotting away, patched over by grafted gears, iron plating, and whirring clockwork prosthetics. Perched near the massive water wheel perched high above Cragpool Lake, the gnome watches over operations with mechanical precision and an unsettling disregard for his own mortal biology.",sp=0},{t="Goblin Ambitions",b="Ziz Fizziks, a goblin operating on behalf of Sputtervalve, sees Gerenzo's downfall as his golden ticket out of Stonetalon's backwaters. Lacking the physical prowess to fight up the cliffs or defeat the augmented overseer himself, Ziz enlists an adventurer to take Gerenzo down and recover his mechanical arm. Armed with this trophy, Ziz hopes to demonstrate his worth and secure a transfer to the prestigious Tinkers' Union workshops in Gadgetzan or Undermine.",sp=0},{t="Clashing Philosophies",b="The recovery of Gerenzo's mechanical arm highlights the profound ideological divide between goblin and gnome engineering traditions. While Gerenzo took the extreme gnomish step of amputating failing flesh to integrate complex prosthetics, goblins find the sacrifice baffling. As Ziz points out, true goblin ingenuity wouldn't discard a biological limb—it would simply mount an explosive third arm alongside the other two.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle?",a="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle is a renegade gnome overseer in the Stonetalon Mountains. He is infamous for replacing portions of his decaying flesh and limbs with mechanical prosthetics and gears, maintaining watch over industrial operations high above Cragpool Lake.",al={"gerenzo","who is gerenzo","gerenzo lore"}},{q="Where can Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle be found?",a="Gerenzo is located northeast of Ziz Fizziks' position, elevated high above the waters of Cragpool Lake near a large industrial water wheel.",al={"gerenzo location","find gerenzo","where is gerenzo"}},{q="Why does Ziz Fizziks want Gerenzo dead?",a="Ziz Fizziks is acting under orders from Sputtervalve. Eliminating Gerenzo proves Ziz's competence, which he hopes will earn him a transfer to a major Tinkers' Union workshop in Gadgetzan or Undermine.",al={"why kill gerenzo","ziz motive","ziz fizziks goal"}},{q="What proof does Ziz require?",a="Ziz requires Gerenzo's grafted mechanical arm as tangible, undeniable proof that the cyborg overseer has been permanently decommissioned.",al={"what proof","gerenzo proof","quest objective item"}},{q="Why is Gerenzo partly mechanical?",a="Gerenzo's organic flesh appeared to be rotting away, prompting him to graft gears, iron plates, and mechanical limbs directly onto his body to sustain and augment himself.",al={"why is gerenzo a cyborg","gerenzo robot","gerenzo body"}},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a prominent goblin supervisor who oversees operations and directs underlings like Ziz Fizziks from elsewhere in Kalimdor.",al={"sputtervalve","who is sputtervalve"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The gruesome construction of Gerenzo's mechanical arm serves as an unsettling extreme of gnomish bionic engineering, contrasting sharply with goblin practical design.",["race:Gnome"]="Gerenzo represents an eccentric and macabre departure from standard gnomish ingenuity, adopting radical self-augmentation to preserve his failing body.",["faction:Horde"]="Assisting goblin contractors in Stonetalon helps secure valuable resources and territory while disrupting dangerous rogue engineers in the crags."},kw={"cragpool lake","cyborg","gerenzo","mechanical arm","sputtervalve","stonetalon","wrenchwhistle","ziz fizziks"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","quest:1483","quest:1094","subzone:cragpool-lake","zone:stonetalon","topic:gnome","subzone:gadgetzan"},m={start="Ziz Fizziks",level="27",id=1096},src={"Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle (quest)"}}
E["quest:1483"] = {t="quest",n="Ziz Fizziks",z="stonetalon",s="This quest sends Horde travelers to check on Ziz Fizziks, a disgruntled goblin engineer stationed on the western ridge of Windshear Crag. Offended when the Venture Company hired a gnome engineer over him, Ziz defected to the Tinkers' Union under Sputtervalve's demanding direction.",h="This quest sends Horde travelers to check on Ziz Fizziks, a disgruntled goblin engineer stationed on the...",sec={{t="A Matter of Professional Pride",b="The Venture Company relies on ruthless exploitation and mechanical innovation, but it crossed a line for Ziz Fizziks when it brought on a gnome engineer named Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle. Deeply insulted by having to work alongside a gnomish rival, Ziz immediately sought a way out. He reached out to Sputtervalve, a contact representing the Tinkers' Union, begging for a transfer away from Gerenzo's oversight.",sp=0},{t="Out of the Frying Pan",b="Securing a new position with the Tinkers' Union did not grant Ziz the easy life he anticipated. Stationed on the western edge of Windshear Crag, he quickly discovered that Sputtervalve is just as much of a slave driver as any Venture Company foreman. Even so, Ziz considers heavy labor under a demanding goblin superior far preferable to sharing an engineering workshop with a gnome.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ziz Fizziks?",a="Ziz Fizziks is a goblin engineer formerly employed by the Venture Company in Stonetalon Mountains. He defected to join the Tinkers' Union after his former employers hired a gnomish engineer.",al={"who is ziz","ziz fizziks npc","about ziz fizziks"}},{q="Why did Ziz Fizziks leave the Venture Company?",a="He walked out in protest after the Venture Company hired a gnome engineer, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle. Refusing to work alongside a gnomish rival, Ziz begged Sputtervalve for new employment.",al={"why did ziz quit","why leave venture co","ziz venture co"}},{q="Where can Ziz Fizziks be found?",a="He is located along the western edge of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains, overlooking the Venture Company logging and excavation operations.",al={"ziz fizziks location","where is ziz","find ziz fizziks"}},{q="Who is Sputtervalve?",a="Sputtervalve is a goblin operative affiliated with the Tinkers' Union who poaches skilled engineers away from the Venture Company, putting them to work on competitive projects.",al={"who is sputtervalve","sputtervalve role"}},{q="Who is Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle?",a="Gerenzo is a gnome engineer brought into Windshear Crag by the Venture Company, an appointment that outraged Ziz and spurred fierce professional rivalry.",al={"gerenzo wrenchwhistle","who is the gnome engineer"}},{q="What is the Tinkers' Union?",a="The Tinkers' Union is an established goblin engineering trade association. They actively compete with rivals like the Venture Company and recruit or reclaim top talent whenever possible.",al={"tinkers union","goblin tinkers union"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The fierce feud between Ziz and Gerenzo perfectly reflects the long-standing, volatile rivalry between goblin and gnomish engineering philosophies.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers operating in Stonetalon Mountains often assist Tinkers' Union operatives like Sputtervalve and Ziz to disrupt Venture Company dominance in Windshear Crag."},kw={"gerenzo wrenchwhistle","sputtervalve","stonetalon","tinkers union","venture company","windshear crag","ziz fizziks"},rel={"npc:sputtervalve","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","quest:1096","topic:venture-company","topic:goblin","topic:gnome"},m={start="Sputtervalve",["end"]="Ziz Fizziks",level="21",id=1483},src={"Ziz Fizziks (quest)"}}
E["quest:1510"] = {t="quest",n="News of Dogran",z="stonetalon",s="This quest sends Horde adventurers deep into the foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains to contact the Darkspear troll Ken'zigla at Malaka'jin. An injured grunt from Camp Taurajo named Dogran lies wounded, and the first runner sent to fetch a lifesaving herbal draught never returned.",h="This quest sends Horde adventurers deep into the foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains to contact the...",sec={{t="A Plea Across the Frontier",b="Dogran, a Horde grunt stationed at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, was grievously wounded during a skirmish against entrenched quilboar. His fellow grunts managed to hold him in place, but festering injuries meant any rough transport back across the plains would kill him. Desperate for a potent remedy, Taurajo sent word north toward Stonetalon, hoping to procure a traditional healing draught prepared by the jungle trolls of Malaka'jin.",sp=0},{t="Bloodshed at Malaka'jin",b="When travelers arrive at the crags of Malaka'jin, they discover that the relief mission collapsed almost immediately. The first courier sent to collect the medicine was ambushed and killed by local Venture Company goblins before ever securing the draught. Ken'zigla still possesses the remedy Dogran needs, but securing it requires dealing with the volatile frontier dangers bordering the Stonetalon passes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dogran and why is he hurt?",a="Dogran is an orc grunt stationed at Camp Taurajo. While leading a squad to clear out aggressive quilboar encampments in the southern Barrens, he suffered brutal, festering wounds that made it impossible to transport him without immediate medical treatment.",al={"who is dogran","why is dogran hurt","dogran story"}},{q="Where is Malaka'jin located?",a="Malaka'jin is a small Darkspear troll outpost nestled in the rocky base of the Stonetalon Mountains, just past the northwestern border of the Barrens.",al={"malakajin location","where is malakajin","find ken'zigla"}},{q="What happened to the first messenger sent for the draught?",a="The initial courier dispatched from Taurajo to retrieve Ken'zigla's draught was ambushed and slain by Venture Company goblins operating along the road near the Stonetalon foothills.",al={"first runner","what happened to the messenger","dead courier"}},{q="Why do warlock trainers care about Dogran's fate?",a="Warlock initiates are directed toward Dogran's plight under the guise of an errand for Blind Cazul and Gazrog, but the ordeal ultimately leads them to an artifact steeped in love and heartbreak required to summon and bind a succubus.",al={"warlock quest connection","succubus dogran","why warlocks do this"},sp=1},{q="Who is Ken'zigla?",a="Ken'zigla is a Darkspear troll alchemist and herbalist residing at the Malaka'jin settlement in Stonetalon, knowledgeable in brewing potent wilderness draughts.",al={"who is kenzigla","kenzigla stonetalon","ken'zigla"}},{q="Why could Dogran not be moved directly to a city?",a="Dogran's wounds became severely festered following the fight with the quilboar. His fellow soldiers feared that hauling him across the rough roads of the Barrens to a major healer would kill him before he arrived.",al={"why not move dogran","dogran wounds","why camp taurajo left him"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="What appears to be a standard military mercy mission is actually a pivotal trial set by Cazul and the Shadow Council in Orgrimmar, steering you toward the emotional resonance required to bind a succubus.",["faction:Horde"]="This leg of the journey illustrates the thin, fragile supply chains connecting remote outposts like Camp Taurajo to isolated camps such as Malaka'jin in the face of quillboar and goblin hostility."},kw={"camp taurajo","dogran","gazrog","ken'zigla","malaka'jin","quilboar","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:1509","quest:1511","npc:gazrog","subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:stonetalon","npc:cazul","quest:1471"},m={start="Gazrog",["end"]="Ken'zigla",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1510},src={"News of Dogran (2)"}}
E["quest:1511"] = {t="quest",n="Ken'zigla's Draught",z="stonetalon",s="Ken'zigla's Draught is an urgent courier task in the Horde warlock chain to summon a succubus. Entrusted with a potent medicinal concoction from Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, the warlock must rush across Kalimdor to Camp Taurajo to save an operative named Dogran.",h="Ken'zigla's Draught is an urgent courier task in the Horde warlock chain to summon a succubus.",sec={{t="A Life-Saving Brew",b="In the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains, the troll apothecary Ken'zigla anticipated trouble. Knowing that an earlier emissary sent to secure medicine for the missing scout Dogran never made it back, Ken'zigla prepared a second dose of his potent restorative draught. The concoction is volatile and powerful: half a dose grants a mortally wounded soldier the vigor to move without causing his injuries to hemorrhage, while the rest must be withheld until the next day to complete recovery.",sp=0},{t="Rendezvous at Camp Taurajo",b="Carrying the draught out of the mountains and into the southern Barrens, the warlock is directed to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo. Logmar holds vital intelligence on Dogran's whereabouts, but his garrison is stripped bare by foraging expeditions. With Dogran trapped and bleeding in hostile territory, delivery of the draught to Taurajo marks the final preparations before staging a rescue operation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Ken'zigla's Draught meant to do?",a="It is a potent medicinal brew crafted by Ken'zigla to revive the injured orc operative Dogran. Given in split doses, the first half grants a wounded fighter enough strength to move without reopening mortal wounds, while the second completes the healing process.",al={"what is the draught","kenziglas draught purpose","why make draught"}},{q="Who is Ken'zigla?",a="Ken'zigla is a troll apothecary situated in the Stonetalon Mountains. He provides specialized alchemical mixtures and concoctions to Horde agents operating in the region.",al={"kenzigla lore","who is kenzigla"}},{q="Why is Grunt Logmar waiting at Camp Taurajo?",a="Grunt Logmar is stationed at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. He monitors local scout movements and holds the last known intelligence on where Dogran disappeared, but lacks the grunts to mount a rescue on his own.",al={"who is grunt logmar","logmar taurajo","grunt logmar role"}},{q="How does this quest connect to summoning a succubus?",a="To summon and bind a succubus, Horde warlocks in Orgrimmar require Dogran's pendant, an artifact suffused with passion and devotion. Securing the pendant requires finding Dogran and saving his life with Ken'zigla's draught.",al={"why succubus quest draught","succubus chain dogran"}},{q="Why didn't the first courier bring the draught?",a="The original messenger dispatched to Stonetalon never completed the mission, prompting Ken'zigla to prepare a backup dose for the next adventurer tracking Dogran down.",al={"what happened to first messenger","previous courier"}},{q="Where does the trail go after Camp Taurajo?",a="Upon receiving the draught, Grunt Logmar points the warlock toward Dogran's captors in the southern Barrens, where the dying scout is held hostage.",al={"where is dogran","next step after logmar"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This leg of your journey is a test of patience and resourcefulness; to command a creature of raw desire and seduction, you must first mend the broken mortal who holds the token of binding.",["faction:Horde"]="Shows the logistical stretch of the young Horde across central Kalimdor, where isolated outposts in Stonetalon and the Barrens rely on travelers to bridge critical communications and medical aid."},kw={"barrens","dogran","draught","ken'zigla","logmar","stonetalon","succubus","taurajo"},rel={"npc:grunt-logmar","quest:1509","quest:1515","quest:1512","quest:1471","quest:1472","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Ken'zigla",["end"]="Grunt Logmar",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1511},src={"Ken'zigla's Draught (quest)"}}
E["quest:5881"] = {t="quest",n="Calling in the Reserves",z="stonetalon",s="\"Calling in the Reserves\" is a Horde courier task entrusted to adventurers resting at Sun Rock Retreat. Maggran Earthbinder sends you south to the edge of the Barrens with orders to relieve an exhausted sentry watching the Great Lift.",h="\"Calling in the Reserves\" is a Horde courier task entrusted to adventurers resting at Sun Rock Retreat.",sec={{t="A Long-Awaited Relief",b="Even in an era of relative prosperity following the Third War, maintaining garrisons across central Kalimdor tests the Horde's resources. At Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains, Maggran Earthbinder oversees logistics and troop welfare. Recognizing that seasoned soldiers wear thin under endless watch duty, Maggran dispatches a letter of reassignment south to the Great Lift, where a young sentry named Grish Longrunner has been standing guard far from home.",sp=0},{t="Watching the Lift",b="The Great Lift serves as the singular engineering artery linking the high plateaus of the Southern Barrens down into the wind-carved canyons of Thousand Needles. Handing the letter over to Grish relieves him of an isolated and monotonous watch over the lift mechanisms, clearing the way for him to finally return to his family and allowing fresh reserves to step in.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Maggran Earthbinder gives the quest at Sun Rock Retreat, nestled high within the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"quest giver","where to get calling in the reserves","maggran earthbinder location"}},{q="Where do I deliver Maggran's letter?",a="You must take Maggran's Reserve Letter south through the Barrens all the way to the Great Lift, the massive wooden elevator structure perched on the border overlooking Thousand Needles.",al={"grish longrunner location","where is grish","where is the great lift"}},{q="Why does Grish Longrunner need relief?",a="Grish has spent extended duty stationed alone guarding the lift mechanisms. He submitted a formal request some time ago to be relieved so he could travel home and visit his family.",al={"grish backstory","why grish leaves","great lift sentry duty"}},{q="Is there any combat required for this quest?",a="No combat is required. It is purely a messenger task intended to steer travelers south toward Thousand Needles.",al={"do i have to fight","peaceful quest","courier task"}},{q="Which faction gains reputation from completing this?",a="Delivering the letter to Grish grants reputation with Thunder Bluff, reflecting the tauren presence and administration over the route.",al={"rep reward","what rep does this give","thunder bluff rep"}},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="The delivery brings you right to the top of the Great Lift, positioning you to ride the elevators down into the canyons of Thousand Needles to explore further Horde outposts.",al={"next quest","where to go after","thousand needles breadcrumb"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The mission illustrates how Horde commanders manage their forces across the Kalimdor frontier, rotating sentries to keep morale and watchposts steady.",["race:Tauren"]="Helping rotate sentries at the Great Lift supports the vital passage connecting the southern reaches of Kalimdor toward Thunder Bluff's broader territories."},kw={"calling in the reserves","great lift","grish longrunner","maggran earthbinder","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","the barrens","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:maggran-earthbinder","npc:grish-longrunner","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:great-lift","zone:stonetalon","zone:barrens","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},m={start="Maggran Earthbinder",["end"]="Grish Longrunner",level="28",faction="Horde",id=5881},src={"Calling in the Reserves"}}
E["quest:6282"] = {t="quest",n="Harpies Threaten",z="stonetalon",s="Harpies Threaten is a Horde quest offered by Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Fulfilling the tauren calling as stewards of the land, adventurers are directed south into the devastated Charred Vale to cull the surging ranks of the Bloodfury harpy coven.",h="Harpies Threaten is a Horde quest offered by Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="Protectors of the Land",b="The tauren of Sun Rock Retreat hold a profound duty to safeguard Stonetalon, maintaining natural balance and shielding peaceful travelers from the region's hazards. Maggran Earthbinder, an elder shaman watching over the retreat, observes with growing alarm the relentless rise of the local harpy population. The Bloodfury coven has spread across the scorched wastes of the Charred Vale, harassing passing beasts and choking off travel routes. Left unchecked, their predatory flocks threaten to isolate Sun Rock Retreat entirely.",sp=0},{t="Scouring the Charred Vale",b="South of Sun Rock Retreat lies the Charred Vale, a desolate wasteland of ash, scorched earth, and smoldering trees left behind after catastrophic fires. Here, nesting high in the charred remnants of ancient woods, the Bloodfuries have established a stronghold. Maggran tasks Horde warriors with venturing into this hostile caldera to cull dozens of harpy ambushers, slayers, and roguefeathers. Thinning the flock shatters the immediate grip the coven holds over the vale and clears the path to confront their matriarchal lineage directly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Harpies Threaten?",a="The quest is given by Maggran Earthbinder, a tauren located near the central pool of water in Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"quest giver harpies threaten","where to pick up harpies threaten","maggran earthbinder quest"}},{q="Where are the Bloodfury harpies located?",a="The Bloodfury harpies dwell throughout the Charred Vale, a burnt expanse located directly south of Sun Rock Retreat. A mountain path behind Sun Rock leads straight down into the vale.",al={"where are bloodfury harpies","bloodfury harpy location","charred vale harpies"}},{q="Why do the tauren want the harpies culled?",a="The tauren consider themselves guardians of Stonetalon's natural balance. Maggran Earthbinder fears the Bloodfuries are expanding aggressively across Kalimdor, attacking innocents and preventing living creatures from freely traveling through the land.",al={"why kill harpies","tauren harpy conflict","why maggran hates harpies"}},{q="What comes after completing Harpies Threaten?",a="Completing Harpies Threaten unlocks the follow-up quest, Bloodfury Bloodline, in which Maggran Earthbinder sends you to eliminate the ruling leadership of the Bloodfury coven.",al={"next quest harpies threaten","harpies threaten follow up","what after harpies threaten"}},{q="Is this quest Horde only?",a="Yes. The quest is offered exclusively to the Horde from the settlement of Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"can alliance do harpies threaten","harpies threaten horde only","alliance harpies threaten"}},{q="What kinds of harpies must be slain?",a="You must slay seven Bloodfury Harpies, seven Bloodfury Ambushers, seven Bloodfury Slayers, and seven Bloodfury Roguefeathers across the Charred Vale.",al={"which harpies to kill","harpy types charred vale","harpies threaten objectives"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren characters, culling the encroaching Bloodfuries is an honorable duty to fulfill their ancestral promise as protectors of Kalimdor's wilderness.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the skies of the Charred Vale strengthens the Horde's foothold at Sun Rock Retreat against dangerous wild factions inhabiting Stonetalon.",["class:Druid"]="The twisted presence of the Bloodfury coven desecrates the already fragile, fire-ravaged ecology of the Charred Vale.",["class:Shaman"]="Working at the behest of Maggran Earthbinder, shaman answer the call to purge aggressive defilers who upset the natural elemental balance."},kw={"ambushers","bloodfury","charred vale","coven","harpies threaten","maggran earthbinder","roguefeathers","slayers","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat"},rel={"quest:6283","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","npc:maggran-earthbinder","topic:harpy","topic:tauren","zone:stonetalon","quest:6301"},m={start="Maggran Earthbinder",level="26",faction="Horde",id=6282},src={"Harpies Threaten"}}
E["quest:6283"] = {t="quest",n="Bloodfury Bloodline",z="stonetalon",s="Bloodfury Bloodline is a Horde task issued by Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat to strike down the leader of the Bloodfury harpies. Culminating Maggran's efforts to cleanse the Charred Vale, the hunt aims to break the flock's ferocious hold over the scarred wilderness.",h="Bloodfury Bloodline is a Horde task issued by Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat to strike down the...",sec={{t="Striking the Matron",b="Culling lesser harpies along the edge of the Charred Vale provides only temporary relief for Sun Rock Retreat. Maggran Earthbinder believes that the only lasting way to curb their aggression is to eliminate their matriarch, Bloodfury Ripper. Revering her as something akin to a queen, the flock draws its ruthless coordination and boldness directly from her leadership along the craggy western ridge.",sp=0},{t="Peace in the Earth",b="Once Bloodfury Ripper falls and her remains are presented as proof, the immediate threat to the retreat subsides. With their brood queen destroyed, the disorganized harpies become far easier to keep at bay. The victory also lifts a spiritual burden from Maggran himself, freeing his thoughts from bitter vigilance so he can return to the customary tauren pursuit of harmony and balance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Bloodfury Bloodline?",a="The quest is provided by Maggran Earthbinder, a tauren shaman located near the pool of water inside Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"quest giver bloodfury bloodline","who starts bloodfury bloodline","maggran earthbinder quest"}},{q="What prerequisite must be finished before this hunt unlocks?",a="You must complete 'Harpies Threaten', where Maggran first sends you into the Charred Vale to thin the general ranks of the Bloodfury harpies.",al={"bloodfury bloodline prequest","prereq for bloodfury bloodline","harpies threaten follow up"}},{q="Where is Bloodfury Ripper located?",a="She stalks the rocky hills along the northwestern edge of the Charred Vale. She can be distinguished from her flock by her distinct blue coloration.",al={"where is bloodfury ripper","find bloodfury ripper","bloodfury ripper spawn"}},{q="Why does Maggran want Bloodfury Ripper dead?",a="Maggran recognizes Bloodfury Ripper as the guiding queen behind the flock's ferocious territorial expansion. Slaying her splinters their leadership and permanently weakens their grip on the vale.",al={"why kill bloodfury ripper","harpy leader charred vale lore","maggran earthbinder motive"}},{q="How does Bloodfury Ripper's death affect the tauren of Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Her death brings Maggran peace of mind, freeing him from the lingering anger and constant dread of an impending attack so he can redirect his focus toward healing the land.",al={"stonetalon harpy threat lore","what happens when bloodfury ripper dies","maggran reaction"},sp=1},{q="What is the quickest path to reach the Charred Vale from Sun Rock Retreat?",a="A mountain trail leads directly out the back of Sun Rock Retreat, bypassing the winding main roads of Stonetalon and descending straight into the Charred Vale.",al={"how to get to charred vale from sun rock","sun rock retreat back way","charred vale shortcut"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Stonetalon's scarred landscape pains the tauren, and removing the violent harpy queen allows local shamans like Maggran to turn their minds back to harmony and healing.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the perimeter around Sun Rock Retreat safeguards the Horde's solitary haven nestled deep within the contested Stonetalon Mountains."},kw={"bloodfury bloodline","bloodfury ripper","charred vale","harpies","maggran earthbinder","stonetalon","sun rock retreat"},rel={"quest:6282","npc:maggran-earthbinder","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren"},m={start="Maggran Earthbinder",level="26",faction="Horde",id=6283},src={"Bloodfury Bloodline"}}
E["quest:6284"] = {t="quest",n="Arachnophobia",z="stonetalon",s="Arachnophobia is a Horde bounty quest targeting Besseleth, an ancient and colossal predator haunting southern Stonetalon Mountains. Posted on a roadside notice near Windshear Crag, the bounty directs adventurers into Sishir Canyon to claim the spider matriarch's fang for Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat. Putting an end to her reign makes the mountain roads safer for night travelers.",h="Arachnophobia is a Horde bounty quest targeting Besseleth, an ancient and colossal predator haunting southern...",sec={{t="The Roadside Warning",b="Travelers along the main thoroughfare south of Windshear Crag will spot a weathered wanted poster warning of the dangers to the west. Sishir Canyon and Webwinder Path have been completely overrun by eight-legged predators. At the heart of this webbed menace sits Besseleth, an unusually large, orange-hued spider who commands her brood and ambushes anyone daring to stray off the path after sunset.",sp=0},{t="The Earthbinder's Grievance",b="The bounty on Besseleth is offered by Maggran Earthbinder, a tauren resident of Sun Rock Retreat. Maggran has a personal score to settle with the matriarch: during a previous encounter, he was nearly killed when struck by Besseleth's massive two-foot fang. Though he managed to fight her off and limp to safety, the lingering wound serves as a constant reminder of the danger lurking in the canyon shadows. By having an adventurer claim Besseleth's Fang, Maggran hopes to secure the passes so trade and travel to Sun Rock Retreat can flourish without fear.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the quest Arachnophobia begin?",a="The quest is started by inspecting a wanted poster posted along the west side of the main road in the Stonetalon Mountains, just south of the entrance to Windshear Crag.",al={"where to get arachnophobia","wanted poster besseleth location","how to start arachnophobia"}},{q="Where can Besseleth be found?",a="Besseleth lairs inside Sishir Canyon, located just west of the roadside wanted poster. She roams among her spider offspring across the canyon's web-choked ground.",al={"besseleth location","where is besseleth","find besseleth spider"}},{q="Who is Maggran Earthbinder?",a="Maggran Earthbinder is a tauren situated at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. He personally survived a venomous strike from Besseleth and posted the bounty to rid the canyon of her menace.",al={"who is maggran","maggran earthbinder role","who turned in arachnophobia"}},{q="Why is Besseleth such a threat to the region?",a="Besseleth is an exceptionally large and ruthless spider who stalks Sishir Canyon and the neighboring Webwinder Path. She and her brood prey upon travelers under the cover of night, threatening anyone attempting to reach Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"why kill besseleth","what did besseleth do"}},{q="What proof is required to claim the bounty?",a="You must slay Besseleth and sever one of her enormous two-foot fangs. Presenting Besseleth's Fang to Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat completes the bounty.",al={"besseleth proof","besseleth quest item","what drops from besseleth"}},{q="Is this quest available to the Alliance?",a="No. The bounty poster awards credit to Maggran Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat, which is a Horde encampment, making Arachnophobia exclusive to the Horde.",al={"can alliance do arachnophobia","alliance arachnophobia quest"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing out Besseleth stabilizes travel into Sun Rock Retreat, protecting the Horde's vital foothold in the central crags of Stonetalon.",["race:Tauren"]="Maggran Earthbinder bears the painful scar of Besseleth's venom, making the hunt a matter of honoring and assisting a fellow son of the earth.",["class:Hunter"]="Tracking down an elusive, colossal arachnid within the shadowed crags of Sishir Canyon offers a true test of mountain stalking."},kw={"arachnophobia","besseleth","bounty","maggran earthbinder","sishir canyon","spider","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","webwinder path"},rel={"subzone:sishir-canyon","npc:maggran-earthbinder","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:webwinder-path","zone:stonetalon","subzone:windshear-crag"},m={start="Wanted Poster: Besseleth",["end"]="Maggran Earthbinder",level="21",faction="Horde",id=6284},src={"Arachnophobia (quest)"}}
E["quest:6301"] = {t="quest",n="Cycle of Rebirth",z="stonetalon",s="Cycle of Rebirth is a Horde task assigned by Tammra Windfield at Sun Rock Retreat to gather rare Gaea seeds from the shores of Mirkfallon Lake. Distressed by the toll of industrial greed and ongoing warfare across Stonetalon, Tammra seeks to bless these resilient kernels with shamanic power to revive the mountain's ravaged soil. It forms the essential first step in a restoration effort aimed at healing the scarred wilderness.",h="Cycle of Rebirth is a Horde task assigned by Tammra Windfield at Sun Rock Retreat to gather rare Gaea seeds...",sec={{t="A Scarred Wilderness",b="The peaks of Stonetalon bear deep wounds from both commercial exploitation and relentless regional conflict. Between aggressive logging operations and clashes between rival factions, entire swaths of forest have been scorched, clear-cut, or reduced to ash. For the tauren stationed at Sun Rock Retreat, witnessing this rapid destruction of the natural world is a grievous wound. Rather than merely fighting to hold ground, shamans like Tammra Windfield look toward the ancient natural order, striving to enact the Earthmother's restorative cycle.",sp=0},{t="The Seeds of Mirkfallon",b="Restoring life to barren ground demands extraordinary vitality, which Tammra finds in the rare Gaea seeds found around Mirkfallon Lake. Situated to the north of Sun Rock Retreat, the lake's banks nurture these sturdy seed pods along the water's edge. Though the surrounding region is steeped in danger, these seeds hold an innate resilience unique to Stonetalon. Once retrieved, Tammra channels ancestral shamanistic blessings into each kernel, awakening their latent power to accelerate their growth for the work ahead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of collecting Gaea seeds?",a="Gaea seeds possess an exceptional natural vitality that makes them uniquely suited for restoring desolated land. Tammra Windfield gathers them so she can imbue them with Earthmother blessings and shamanistic power, preparing them to rapidly sprout and replenish parts of Stonetalon ruined by industry and war.",al={"why gaea seeds","what are gaea seeds for","cycle of rebirth purpose"}},{q="Where are the Gaea seeds located?",a="Gaea seeds can be found lying along the shoreline of Mirkfallon Lake, situated directly north of Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. They rest in the dirt near the water's edge all around the perimeter of the lake.",al={"gaea seed location","where to find gaea seeds","mirkfallon lake seeds"}},{q="Who is Tammra Windfield?",a="Tammra Windfield is a tauren shaman residing at Sun Rock Retreat. Deeply pained by the deforestation and devastation inflicted on Stonetalon by wartime conflict and logging syndicates, she devotes herself to healing the land through Earthmother blessings.",al={"who is tammra","tammra windfield lore"}},{q="What does Tammra do once the seeds are returned?",a="Upon receiving the ten Gaea seeds, Tammra begins a sacred chant to infuse the kernels with shamanistic energy, quickening their natural growth potential so they can be planted in devastated zones.",al={"what happens to seeds","turn in cycle of rebirth"}},{q="What quest follows Cycle of Rebirth?",a="Cycle of Rebirth leads directly into the quest 'New Life', where the empowered seeds are carried into the devastated Charred Vale to begin re-establishing plant life.",al={"cycle of rebirth follow up","next quest after cycle of rebirth","what is after cycle of rebirth"}},{q="Why is the land of Stonetalon in need of healing?",a="The Stonetalon Mountains have suffered severe environmental damage from continuous warfare and extensive clear-cutting by industrial lumber ventures, leaving scorched wastelands and scarred valleys that struggle to regrow naturally.",al={"why is stonetalon ruined","what happened to stonetalon"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Tammra's effort reflects the shamanic calling to mend ecological imbalance, showing that the spirits and the Earthmother can restore what industrial exploitation tears down.",["race:Tauren"]="For the Shu'halo, healing the wounded soil of Stonetalon is an act of spiritual duty to the Earthmother, answering the devastation caused by reckless logging and factional warfare.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will appreciate the parallel focus on natural cycles and seed cultivation, as restoring barren earth directly echoes Cenarion stewardship."},kw={"charred vale","cycle of rebirth","earthmother","gaea seed","mirkfallon lake","new life","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","tammra windfield"},rel={"npc:tammra-windfield","quest:6381","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Tammra Windfield",level="23",faction="Horde",id=6301},src={"Cycle of Rebirth"}}
E["quest:6381"] = {t="quest",n="New Life",z="stonetalon",s="New Life is a restorative Horde quest offered by Tammra Windfield in Sun Rock Retreat. Following the collection of enchanted seeds, the player journeys west into the ashen ruins of the Charred Vale to sow them into fertile earth. This ritual effort aims to spark the land's recovery amidst hostile elementals and harpies.",h="New Life is a restorative Horde quest offered by Tammra Windfield in Sun Rock Retreat.",sec={{t="Healing the Scorched Earth",b="The Charred Vale stands as a tragic testament to recent devastation, choked by soot, furious fire elementals, and scavenging harpies. Tammra Windfield refuses to let the region surrender to ruin. Relying on the ancient resilience of the Earth Mother, she dispatches travelers into the heart of the blackened valley to seek out Gaea Dirt Mounds—patches of fertile topsoil that survived the inferno.",sp=0},{t="A Foothold for the Future",b="The enchanted Gaea seeds planted in the scorched soil are bred to withstand lingering elemental corruption. By taking root, they begin weaving a vital ecological anchor that can resist decay and invite flora back into the valley. Tammra envisions a long-term healing process: as living roots slowly reclaim the basin, the agitated fire spirits will settle, the harpies will lose their desolate roost, and the Venture Company's rapacious logging operations will eventually be driven out.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of planting the Gaea seeds?",a="The enchanted Gaea seeds are designed to take root in the scarred earth of the Charred Vale. They resist corruption and establish an initial foothold of vibrant plant life, setting the foundation for the forest to gradually regrow and heal.",al={"why plant seeds","new life purpose","what do gaea seeds do"}},{q="Where do I need to go to plant the seeds?",a="You must travel west from Sun Rock Retreat into the Charred Vale. The seeds are planted into small Gaea Dirt Mounds scattered across the blackened basin.",al={"where is charred vale","where do i plant gaea seeds","seed locations"}},{q="Who is Tammra Windfield?",a="Tammra Windfield is a tauren naturalist residing in Sun Rock Retreat within the Stonetalon Mountains. She is dedicated to soothing the wounded spirits of the land and rehabilitating areas ravaged by elemental fury and industrial greed.",al={"who gives new life","tammra quest giver","tammra windfield lore"}},{q="What threats roam the Charred Vale while planting?",a="The Charred Vale is inhabited by rogue fire elementals stirred up by the recent devastation, as well as aggressive Bloodfury harpies that nest amidst the burnt trees.",al={"charred vale enemies","what attacks in charred vale","dangers in charred vale"}},{q="What quest comes before New Life?",a="New Life directly follows the quest Cycle of Rebirth, in which you help Tammra collect the vital materials required to prepare the enchanted Gaea seeds.",al={"new life prerequisite","cycle of rebirth quest","what leads to new life"}},{q="What does Tammra hope will happen to Stonetalon long term?",a="Tammra hopes the regrowing land will eventually calm the enraged fire elementals, crowd out the predatory harpies, and outlast the logging operations of the Venture Company, restoring the mountains to a lush and peaceful forest.",al={"future of stonetalon","tammra goal","what happens to charred vale"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren, sowing enchanted seeds into scarred soil is an act of spiritual communion with the Earth Mother, fulfilling their sacred duty to heal wounded lands.",["class:Druid"]="Druids share a close kinship with Tammra's mission, viewing the renewal of the Charred Vale as an essential restoration of nature's delicate balance.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman understand that the agitated fire elementals roaming the Vale will never find peace until the battered land itself begins to heal.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists appreciate the profound power of resilient seeds to bring forth thriving vegetation out of completely deadened soil."},kw={"bloodfury harpies","charred vale","cycle of rebirth","dirt mounds","fire elementals","gaea seeds","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","tammra windfield"},rel={"quest:6301","npc:tammra-windfield","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","quest:6282","quest:764"},m={start="Tammra Windfield",level="25",faction="Horde",id=6381},src={"New Life"}}
E["quest:6401"] = {t="quest",n="Kaya's Alive",z="stonetalon",s="Kaya's Alive is a short Horde quest in the Stonetalon Mountains that concludes the rescue of Kaya Flathoof. After escorting the young tauren safely past hostile Grimtotem bandits, you are sent to carry the joyful news of her survival to her worried aunt, Tammra Windfield, in Sun Rock Retreat.",h="Kaya's Alive is a short Horde quest in the Stonetalon Mountains that concludes the rescue of Kaya Flathoof.",sec={{t="A Breath of Relief",b="The mountains of Stonetalon are fraught with danger, especially along the contested trails where the Grimtotem tribe strikes without mercy. When their village fell under a brutal attack, young Kaya Flathoof was feared dead or captured by the renegades. Her survival and subsequent rescue provide a rare moment of triumph and relief amidst the ongoing tribal conflicts in the crags.",sp=0},{t="Reaching Sun Rock Retreat",b="Once Kaya is guided to safety, Makaba Flathoof charges you with carrying the word directly to Sun Rock Retreat. There, Kaya's aunt, Tammra Windfield, waits anxiously for news from the trails. Delivering word of Kaya's safety offers the fractured family solace and reinforces the vital role traveling champions play in keeping the remote Horde outposts connected.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaya Flathoof?",a="Kaya Flathoof is a young tauren who was separated and endangered following a violent assault on her settlement by rogue Grimtotem forces in Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who is kaya","kaya flathoof","kaya"}},{q="Who is Tammra Windfield?",a="Tammra Windfield is Kaya's aunt, residing at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. She had feared her niece perished in the Grimtotem attack.",al={"tammra windfield","who is tammra","kaya aunt"}},{q="Who attacked Kaya's village?",a="Kaya's village was ambushed by the aggressive Grimtotem clan, an isolationist tauren faction notorious for preying on both rival tribes and traveling wayfarers across the mountains.",al={"who attacked kaya","village attack","grimtotem attack"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="This quest immediately follows 'Protect Kaya', an escort mission where you defend Kaya Flathoof as she flees her captors and returns to safety.",al={"prerequisite","protect kaya","escort quest"}},{q="Where is Sun Rock Retreat located?",a="Sun Rock Retreat is nestled high in the central Stonetalon Mountains, accessed by following the main road westward and through a narrow mountain defile into a sheltered basin.",al={"sun rock retreat location","where is sun rock","find sun rock retreat"}},{q="Why does Makaba Flathoof send you instead of going himself?",a="Makaba remains behind to tend to Kaya and ensure the immediate perimeter is secure, relying on an able-bodied runner to swiftly reassure their family in Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"why makaba stays","why send me"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Stonetalon is a contested wilderness where Horde lines are stretched thin; delivering news of survivors helps maintain unity among scattered encampments.",["race:Tauren"]="The threat of the Grimtotem is a painful internal rift for the Shu'halo, making the preservation of innocent family members like Kaya deeply personal."},kw={"flathoof","grimtotem","kaya","makaba","protect kaya","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tammra","tauren","windfield"},rel={"quest:6523","npc:makaba-flathoof","npc:tammra-windfield","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Makaba Flathoof",["end"]="Tammra Windfield",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6401},src={"Kaya's Alive"}}
E["quest:6421"] = {t="quest",n="Boulderslide Ravine",z="stonetalon",s="Deep in the Boulderslide Ravine of the Stonetalon Mountains, local kobolds have begun frantically mining a rare subterranean mineral known as Resonite. Sensing a growing tension in the earth, the tauren Mor'rogal sends Horde adventurers to explore the ravine's cave system and retrieve mineral samples to uncover what lies buried beneath the rock.",h="Deep in the Boulderslide Ravine of the Stonetalon Mountains, local kobolds have begun frantically mining a...",sec={{t="Tension in the Stone",b="From his post at Sun Rock Retreat, the tauren Mor'rogal watches the peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains with deep concern. The land itself feels disturbed, an unnatural agitation radiating from the southeast. There, within the crags of Boulderslide Ravine, the local kobolds have abandoned their ordinary foraging to aggressively excavate a rare, subterranean mineral known as Resonite. To determine why these superstitious vermin are mining with such desperate frenzy, Mor'rogal enlists Horde scouts to push past their defenses, plumb the lowest depths of the cavern, and bring back unrefined mineral samples.",sp=0},{t="Awakening the Ancients",b="When the raw Resonite is inspected, its true nature becomes clear: the crystals hum with ancient Earthen magic. Kobolds digging blindly into the deep stone have breached an ancient layer of the world and unearthed an Earthen, one of the primordial stone-beings shaped by the Titans to sculpt the subterranean foundations of Kalimdor. What the kobolds treat as mere quarry has disturbed a relic of primordial history, forcing the tauren to intervene before whatever lies buried breaks free.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Boulderslide Ravine located?",a="Boulderslide Ravine cuts into the mountains southeast of Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. The ravine leads into a winding cave system overrun with Boulderslide kobolds.",al={"boulderslide ravine location","where is boulderslide ravine","how to find boulderslide ravine"}},{q="Who gives the quest Boulderslide Ravine?",a="The quest is given by Mor'rogal, a tauren located at Sun Rock Retreat, the primary Horde outpost in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who starts boulderslide ravine","quest giver boulderslide ravine","mor'rogal quest"}},{q="What are Resonite Crystals?",a="Resonite is a rare mineral found deep within the Boulderslide cave system. It carries lingering traces of Titan-forged Earthen magic, indicating that the crystals were formed in close proximity to subterranean Earthen relics.",al={"what is resonite","resonite lore","resonite crystals"},sp=1},{q="Why are the kobolds mining Resonite so frantically?",a="The kobolds stumbled upon Resonite while digging and, in their voracious search for shiny ores, penetrated deep beneath the mountains until they disturbed an ancient Earthen buried in the rock.",al={"why are kobolds mining","boulderslide kobolds goal","kobold plot stonetalon"},sp=1},{q="What is an Earthen according to tauren lore?",a="According to ancient lore recalled by Mor'rogal, the Earthen are stone-hewn creatures forged by the Titans long ago to carve and shape the very bedrock of the world.",al={"what are earthen","earthen titan connection","who are earthen"}},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Upon identifying the Earthen magic within the Resonite crystals, Mor'rogal prepares an enchanted countermeasure and offers the follow-up quest 'Earthen Arise', sending you back into the cavern to confront the awakened threat.",al={"next quest after boulderslide ravine","what follows boulderslide ravine","boulderslide ravine follow up"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren who revere the Earth Mother, unearthing ancient Titan workings beneath the mountains signals a dangerous disturbance in the natural balance of Stonetalon.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman who listen to the earth can sense the unnatural resonance vibrating through the rock as the kobolds unseal relics of primordial Titan elemental crafting.",["profession:Mining"]="The Resonite mined by the Boulderslide kobolds is not ordinary ore; its matrix is infused with ancient arcane residue left by subterranean builders of old."},kw={"boulderslide ravine","earthen","kobold","mor'rogal","resonite","resonite crystal","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","titan"},rel={"npc:mor-rogal","quest:6481","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","topic:kobold","topic:titan","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Mor'rogal",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6421},src={"Boulderslide Ravine (quest)"}}
E["quest:6461"] = {t="quest",n="Blood Feeders",z="stonetalon",s="Blood Feeders is a Horde hunting contract given by Xen'Zilla in the Darkspear settlement of Malaka'jin. The local trolls have found plentiful game along the slopes of Stonetalon, but the scent of their butchered meat has drawn swarms of predatory Deepmoss spiders down into their camps.",h="Blood Feeders is a Horde hunting contract given by Xen'Zilla in the Darkspear settlement of Malaka'jin.",sec={{t="Unwanted Dinner Guests",b="The trolls who established the frontier outpost of Malaka'jin in southeastern Stonetalon Mountains came seeking good hunting. The craggy slopes proved bountiful, but the meat and game they brought back soon drew the attention of nocturnal predators. Deepmoss spiders, aggressive arachnids native to the crags and canyons to the north, began slipping into the camp under cover of dark, seeking to scavenge their caches or turn the hunters into prey.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Crags",b="To keep the encampment safe and protect their supplies, Xen'Zilla asks adventurers to track the predators north into the mountain passes. The infestation of Deepmoss Creepers and Venomspitters is thickest around the rocky ravines and webs of the Cleft. Thinning their numbers pushes the brood back from Malaka'jin's borders and ensures the village can rest without fearing ambush from the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Blood Feeders?",a="Xen'Zilla, a Darkspear troll residing in the village of Malaka'jin in the southeastern Stonetalon Mountains, offers the task to traveling Horde champions.",al={"who gives blood feeders","blood feeders quest giver","xen'zilla quest"}},{q="Why are the spiders attacking Malaka'jin?",a="The trolls at Malaka'jin hunt the local game extensively. The scent of fresh kills and drying meat draws the Deepmoss spiders down from the mountain passes at night to steal provisions and hunt the villagers.",al={"why spiders attack","spider attacks malakajin","why are spiders invading"}},{q="Where are the Deepmoss spiders located?",a="Deepmoss Creepers and Venomspitters roam the central passes and crags north of Malaka'jin, with a particularly dense concentration dwelling within the web-strewn ravine known as the Cleft.",al={"where are deepmoss spiders","deepmoss creepers location","deepmoss venomspitter location"}},{q="What is Malaka'jin?",a="Malaka'jin is a Darkspear troll encampment located at the southern entrance of the Stonetalon Mountains, near the border with the Barrens, serving as a frontier hunting base and Horde outpost.",al={"what is malaka'jin","malakajin lore","troll village stonetalon"}},{q="Is there a greater threat tied to these spiders?",a="Deep inside the Cleft among the webs lives a massive, lethal spider matriarch. A warning signpost outside the canyon warns travelers of the danger and encourages groups to bring her down.",al={"big spider stonetalon","cleft elite spider","spider matriarch stonetalon"}},{q="What happens after the spiders are culled?",a="Culling the Creepers and Venomspitters gives Malaka'jin breathing room, allowing the troll hunters to secure their meat stores and walk their camps at night without constant ambush.",al={"blood feeders aftermath","does malakajin become safe"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The hunters of Malaka'jin are kin, striving to carve out self-sufficient territory in Kalimdor's rugged highlands without succumbing to the wilderness.",["faction:Horde"]="Malaka'jin anchors the Horde's access route into the Stonetalon Mountains from the northern Barrens; safeguarding the village secures the entire southern pass.",["class:Hunter"]="Tracking dangerous predators that out-hunt and harass friendly settlements is natural work for skilled trackers moving through the crags."},kw={"blood feeders","cleft","deepmoss creeper","deepmoss venomspitter","malaka'jin","spiders","stonetalon","xen'zilla"},rel={"subzone:malaka-jin","zone:stonetalon","subzone:cleft","quest:6284","topic:troll"},m={start="Xen'Zilla",level="19",faction="Horde",id=6461},src={"Blood Feeders"}}
E["quest:6481"] = {t="quest",n="Earthen Arise",z="stonetalon",s="Deep within Boulderslide Ravine, the shaman Mor'rogal discovers a slumbering Earthen named Goggeroc sealed inside a Resonite cask. Fearing the raw destructive power an ancient being of stone could unleash upon Kalimdor, he sends a champion to shatter the cask and strike Goggeroc down before the creature can recover its full strength.",h="Deep within Boulderslide Ravine, the shaman Mor'rogal discovers a slumbering Earthen named Goggeroc sealed...",sec={{t="A Slumber in Stone",b="While investigating the vermin infestation in Boulderslide Ravine, scouts discovered a strange relic nestled among the kobolds: a Resonite cask radiating unearthly force. Mor'rogal, an orc shaman stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains, recognized the container for what it truly was—a prison and sanctuary housing Goggeroc, a dormant Earthen. These primordial creations of stone possess strength that outmatches mortal warriors, making the prospect of Goggeroc roaming free an existential threat to the region.",sp=0},{t="The Resonite Crystal",b="Awakening an Earthen at full power would spell disaster for Stonetalon. To tilt the odds, Mor'rogal altered the mixture of resonite crystals brought to him, infusing them with shamanistic magic. The resulting enchanted crystal is designed to shatter the Resonite cask with enough force to shock Goggeroc awake in an acutely weakened state. It falls to the Horde's warriors to smash the container and strike down the disoriented titan-forged being before he can shake off centuries of torpor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mor'rogal?",a="Mor'rogal is an orc shaman stationed in the Stonetalon Mountains. He studies the disturbances in the region and uses his elemental magic to assess the bizarre ancient artifacts and threats unearthed by the local vermin.",al={"mor rogal","who is questgiver","orc shaman morrogal"}},{q="What is an Earthen?",a="Earthen are ancient beings forged from living stone, creations left behind by the Titans in the world's dawn. Imbued with deep ties to the earth and staggering physical might, they have slept buried across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms for millennia.",al={"what is earthen","earthen lore","who are earthen"}},{q="Why does Mor'rogal want Goggeroc dead?",a="Mor'rogal fears that the unmatched strength of an active Earthen would bring catastrophe to Stonetalon and all of Kalimdor. Because such primordial beings are unpredictable and immensely powerful, he believes destroying Goggeroc while he is weakened from his slumber is the only way to safeguard the land.",al={"why kill goggeroc","is goggeroc evil","why slay earthen"}},{q="Where is Goggeroc located?",a="Goggeroc is entombed inside a Resonite cask deep within the caves of Boulderslide Ravine, located in southeastern Stonetalon Mountains, surrounded by the Boulderslide kobolds who dig through the caverns.",al={"where is cask","goggeroc location","find resonite cask"}},{q="How do you awaken Goggeroc?",a="You use the Enchanted Resonite Crystal provided by Mor'rogal directly on the Resonite cask in the cave. The magically altered crystal fractures the container and forces the slumbering Earthen out into the open.",al={"how to summon goggeroc","use enchanted resonite crystal","open cask"}},{q="What happens after Goggeroc is slain?",a="Returning to Mor'rogal with news of Goggeroc's death relieves the shaman's deep dread. He hails you as a hero whose deed has averted a monumental disaster, earning you great honor and standing among the Tauren of Thunder Bluff.",al={"quest reward story","morrogal reaction","turn in earthen arise"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Mor'rogal channels shamanistic power to manipulate the resonite crystals and disrupt the elemental balance preserving the Earthen inside his cask.",["race:Tauren"]="Stonetalon is sacred ancestral hunting ground for the tribes of Thunder Bluff, and neutralizing an ancient destructive entity deep within its peaks protects the land from ruination.",["faction:Horde"]="By eliminating Goggeroc, Horde champions secure their presence in the contested crags of Stonetalon while earning the enduring respect of Thunder Bluff's leadership."},kw={"boulderslide ravine","earthen","earthen arise","goggeroc","mor'rogal","resonite cask","shaman","stonetalon mountains"},rel={"npc:mor-rogal","quest:6421","zone:stonetalon","zone:thunderbluff","topic:kobold"},m={start="Mor'rogal",level="20",faction="Horde",id=6481},src={"Earthen Arise"}}
E["quest:6523"] = {t="quest",n="Protect Kaya",z="stonetalon",s="Protect Kaya is a Horde escort quest in the Stonetalon Mountains. After discovering Kaya Flathoof held captive by hostile Grimtotem tauren, adventurers guide her through dangerous mountain trails to reach Camp Aparaje. Returning word of her survival brings immense relief to her anxious father, Makaba Flathoof.",h="Protect Kaya is a Horde escort quest in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Captive in the Crags",b="The Stonetalon Mountains harbor bitter rivalries among the tauren, none sharper than the tension surrounding the treacherous Grimtotem clan. Deep within hostile territory, Kaya Flathoof was captured and held prisoner. Escaping on foot requires navigating winding trails flanked by opportunistic predators and watchful enemies, making an armed escort her only realistic hope of reaching friendly soil.",sp=0},{t="Flight to Camp Aparaje",b="Camp Aparaje sits as a vital haven for Horde travelers and peaceful tauren seeking passage through Stonetalon. Kaya aims for this outpost, confident that once she reaches its perimeter, local allies can safeguard her journey home. Guiding her through the ambush-heavy paths ensures she avoids recapture before her captors realize she slipped away.",sp=0},{t="A Father's Relief",b="Awaiting news near the southeastern border of Stonetalon, Makaba Flathoof fears the absolute worst for his missing daughter. When runners arrive to deliver confirmation that Kaya safely reached Camp Aparaje, Makaba's despair turns to overwhelming gratitude toward the champions who stood between his child and her captors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kaya Flathoof?",a="Kaya Flathoof is a young tauren who was captured by hostile Grimtotem forces in the Stonetalon Mountains. She relies on passing Horde adventurers to break her out and shepherd her to safe ground.",al={"who is kaya","kaya flathoof lore","kaya"}},{q="Where does Kaya need to be escorted?",a="Kaya must be escorted safely along the trails leading to Camp Aparaje, a Horde refuge in Stonetalon where she can find reliable protection.",al={"kaya escort destination","where to take kaya","where does kaya go"}},{q="Who is Makaba Flathoof?",a="Makaba Flathoof is Kaya's father, waiting anxiously near the southeastern entrance of the Stonetalon Mountains. He despairs over his missing child until adventurers bring word of her rescue.",al={"who is makaba","makaba flathoof lore","kaya's father"}},{q="Who captured Kaya?",a="Kaya was taken prisoner by hostile Grimtotem tauren who maintain camps and ambushes across the crags of Stonetalon.",al={"who took kaya","who kidnapped kaya","kaya kidnappers"}},{q="What happens after Kaya reaches Camp Aparaje?",a="Once Kaya reaches Camp Aparaje, she can find her own way, and the player is tasked with returning to Makaba Flathoof to deliver the joyful news that she survived.",al={"after protect kaya","what next after escort","protect kaya follow up"}},{q="Is this quest available to Alliance players?",a="No. The Flathoof family belongs to the peaceful tauren aligned with the Horde, making this rescue mission exclusive to Horde adventurers.",al={"can alliance do protect kaya","is kaya horde only"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Rescuing Kaya directly aids fellow kin torn apart by the aggressive aggression of the Grimtotem clan.",["faction:Horde"]="Ensuring the safety of traveling families reinforces the Horde's hard-won footholds and supply routes in Stonetalon."},kw={"camp aparaje","escort","grimtotem","kaya flathoof","makaba flathoof","protect kaya","stonetalon","tauren"},rel={"quest:6401","npc:makaba-flathoof","subzone:camp-aparaje","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Kaya Flathoof",["end"]="Makaba Flathoof",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6523},src={"Protect Kaya"}}
E["quest:6542"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Kadrak",z="stonetalon",s="This military dispatch directs Horde warriors from Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains to Kadrak's watch post on the border of the northern Barrens. It marks the transition from defending the crags to reinforcing the Horde's contentious military campaign inside Ashenvale. By reporting to Kadrak, soldiers are marshaled to support forward encampments like Splintertree Post and the Zoram Strand.",h="This military dispatch directs Horde warriors from Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains to Kadrak's watch...",sec={{t="A Call to the Northern Front",b="In the craggy pass of Malaka'jin, the tauren Darn Talongrip keeps an eye on the Horde's southern and mountain frontiers. Yet the greatest military pressure lies northward in the ancient forests of Ashenvale, where night elf sentinels clash incessantly with Warsong lumber gatherers. Recognizing blooded fighters passing through Stonetalon, Darn directs capable recruits toward the northern Barrens watch tower to assist with ongoing campaigns.",sp=0},{t="Kadrak's Watch",b="Positioned squarely upon the northern threshold where the arid savannah meets the verdant canopy of Ashenvale, the orc Kadrak oversees Horde troop movement into contested territory. The Horde is aggressively securing its foothold, maintaining outposts at both the western Zoram Strand and Splintertree Post to the north. Kadrak serves as the vital junction for coordinating supplies, troops, and urgent reports across these embattled forest lines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Kadrak from Stonetalon?",a="Darn Talongrip, a tauren stationed at the Horde outpost of Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, offers this dispatch to capable adventurers heading toward the forest border.",al={"quest giver report to kadrak","who starts report to kadrak stonetalon","darn talongrip quest"}},{q="Where is Kadrak located?",a="Kadrak is stationed at the northern watch tower in the Barrens, guarding the primary road that crosses northward into Ashenvale.",al={"kadrak location","where is kadrak","find kadrak"}},{q="Why is the Horde recruiting warriors for Ashenvale?",a="The Horde needs lumber to sustain Orgrimmar and has established fortified positions such as the Zoram Strand and Splintertree Post. Because these efforts face intense resistance from the native night elves, commanders require constant reinforcements to secure the territory.",al={"why go to ashenvale","horde ashenvale campaign","why fight in ashenvale"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Kadrak?",a="Kadrak will brief you on the strategic situation in Ashenvale and task you with delivering and collecting military reports across the forest's contested outposts via The Warsong Reports.",al={"what next after kadrak","the warsong reports","kadrak follow up quest"}},{q="Is this quest different from the Barrens version?",a="Both are breadcrumb quests leading to Kadrak at the Ashenvale border. One is offered in the Barrens (at Crossroads) and this one in the Stonetalon Mountains; completing either one directs you into the Ashenvale storyline.",al={"barrens vs stonetalon kadrak","two report to kadrak quests","kadrak breadcrumb duplicate"}},{q="What is the Zoram Strand mentioned in the briefing?",a="The Zoram Strand is a coastal region in northwestern Ashenvale along the Veiled Sea. The Horde has established a fortified beach outpost there to support tactical movements and secure naval access.",al={"what is zoram strand","zoram strand outpost","ashenvale beach base"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This order integrates you into the Warchief's broader war effort, funneling frontier veterans into the active struggle for Ashenvale's resources.",["race:Orc"]="The campaign in Ashenvale is crucial for the Warsong clan and the survival of Durotar, making Kadrak's post a proving ground for young orc warriors.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren lookouts like Darn Talongrip guide travelers safely across the mountain borders, keeping the lines of communication open between bloodhoof lands and the Warchief's northern front."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","darn talongrip","kadrak","splintertree","stonetalon mountains","warsong reports","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:kadrak","npc:darn-talongrip","quest:6543","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:6541","topic:horde"},m={start="Darn Talongrip",["end"]="Kadrak",level="19",faction="Horde",id=6542},src={"Report to Kadrak (Stonetalon Mountains)"}}
E["quest:6548"] = {t="quest",n="Avenge My Village",z="stonetalon",s="Makaba Flathoof barely survived a vicious assault when raiders from the Grimtotem clan fell upon his village in the southeastern Stonetalon Mountains. Cut off from his kin and surrounded by the dead, he asks Horde travelers to strike back at the encampment of Grimtotem ruffians and hired sellswords to avenge his fallen people.",h="Makaba Flathoof barely survived a vicious assault when raiders from the Grimtotem clan fell upon his village...",sec={{t="Blood in the Crags",b="Near the border between the Barrens and the red stone passes of Stonetalon, Makaba Flathoof stands as a lone survivor of a brutal massacre. Raiders flying the dark banners of the Grimtotem clan descended without warning, slaughtering nearly everyone in his settlement. Though Makaba fought back fiercely and brought down several of the attackers, he was eventually driven into hiding with little more than his life and his wrath.",sp=0},{t="The Grimtotem Menace",b="The Grimtotem have long been an unruly, aggressive thorn in the side of the tauren tribes united under High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Unlike the peaceful nomads wandering Mulgore, Grimtotem warbands frequently employ ruthless ruffians and opportunistic mercenaries to carve out territory and strike at isolated settlements. For Makaba, diplomacy or tribal kinship holds no meaning now; only blood repaid with blood can bring measure to his grief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gave this quest?",a="Makaba Flathoof is a tauren survivor encamped near the southeastern pass into the Stonetalon Mountains. He survived the violent sacking of his nearby village by the Grimtotem clan and seeks retribution against the raiders.",al={"quest giver","makaba flathoof","who is makaba"}},{q="Why are the Grimtotem attacking other tauren?",a="The Grimtotem clan has never truly embraced the unity of the Horde or Cairne Bloodhoof's vision of peace. Fiercely territorial, xenophobic, and aggressive, they openly raid rival settlements, kill outsiders, and use armed thugs and hired mercenaries to claim dominion over regions like Stonetalon.",al={"why grimtotem hostile","tauren attacking tauren","grimtotem clan lore"}},{q="Where are the Grimtotem attackers located?",a="The Grimtotem ruffians and mercenaries are stationed in an encampment just west of Makaba Flathoof's position in southeastern Stonetalon, set among the rocky hills overlooking the pass.",al={"where are the mobs","grimtotem camp location","where to find ruffians"}},{q="Who are the Grimtotem Mercenaries?",a="The Grimtotem Clan frequently supplements its own warriors by hiring ruthless fighters and sellswords to bolster their warbands, ensuring they have sufficient muscle to terrorize and overrun isolated settlements.",al={"mercenaries","grimtotem sellswords","who are the mercs"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="After cutting down the frontline ruffians and mercenaries, Makaba asks you to strike at the leader behind the massacre, Grundig Darkcloud, in the follow-up quest 'Kill Grundig Darkcloud'.",al={"next quest","what follows avenge my village","kill grundig darkcloud"},sp=1},{q="Where was Makaba's village located?",a="Makaba's settlement was an isolated tauren encampment situated near the border passes of southeastern Stonetalon. It was thoroughly wiped out by the Grimtotem raid, leaving Makaba as one of the few known survivors.",al={"flathoof village","where was the village","what village was destroyed"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem clan's treachery hits tauren travelers hardest. Seeing fellow shu'halo butchered by their own kind reinforces the grim reality of clan division and the danger the Grimtotem pose to Cairne's united people.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on open, secure passes between the Barrens and Stonetalon. A rogue Grimtotem band murdering travelers and allied villages threatens the Warchief's supply lines through the mountains."},kw={"avenge my village","grimtotem","grimtotem mercenary","grimtotem ruffian","grundig darkcloud","makaba flathoof","stonetalon mountains"},rel={"npc:makaba-flathoof","quest:6629","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Makaba Flathoof",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6548},src={"Avenge My Village"}}
E["quest:6629"] = {t="quest",n="Kill Grundig Darkcloud",z="stonetalon",s="Kill Grundig Darkcloud is a Horde quest given by Makaba Flathoof along the southeastern path of Stonetalon Mountains. After culling the raiding Grimtotem reavers, Makaba directs you to strike down the leader responsible for sacking his home: Grundig Darkcloud. Eliminating Grundig and his retinue of brutes delivers justice for the devastated settlement.",h="Kill Grundig Darkcloud is a Horde quest given by Makaba Flathoof along the southeastern path of Stonetalon...",sec={{t="The Butcher of the Path",b="Makaba Flathoof managed to survive the sudden, violent assault on his settlement along the Stonetalon trail, but his sorrow remains raw. After testing your capability against the Grimtotem's foot soldiers, he points you toward the mastermind behind the bloodshed: Grundig Darkcloud. Unlike mere opportunistic raiders, Grundig commands a devoted retinue of brutes and spearheaded the slaughter that leveled the village.",sp=0},{t="Strike at Grimtotem Post",b="Grundig makes his camp at Grimtotem Post, situated further up the mountain road to the west. To avenge Makaba's kin and secure the pass from further violence, travelers must ascend into the stronghold, carve through Darkcloud's inner circle of brutes, and put an end to Grundig himself before his raiding party can descend upon other vulnerable camps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grundig Darkcloud?",a="Grundig Darkcloud is a violent Grimtotem commander based out of Grimtotem Post in southeastern Stonetalon Mountains. He directly orchestrated and led the brutal attack that destroyed Makaba Flathoof's village.",al={"grundig darkcloud","who is grundig","grimtotem leader"}},{q="Where can Grundig Darkcloud be found?",a="Grundig Darkcloud is located at Grimtotem Post, perched along the mountain trail just up the path to the west of Makaba Flathoof's camp near the Barrens border.",al={"grundig location","where is grundig","grimtotem post location"}},{q="What is Makaba Flathoof's motive for this task?",a="Makaba watched his home and clanmates slaughtered by the Grimtotem. Having already exacted preliminary vengeance on their scouts and reavers, he asks for the head of the ringleader, Grundig Darkcloud, to bring true closure and retribution.",al={"why kill grundig","makaba story","makaba revenge"}},{q="Why are the Grimtotem attacking peaceful settlements here?",a="The Grimtotem clan holds fierce disdain for the other tauren tribes, particularly those who have allied with the Horde or embrace gentler paths. They routinely use ambushes, raiding, and sheer brutality to drive competing clans off lands they wish to dominate.",al={"why grimtotem attack","grimtotem hostility"}},{q="What comes after killing Grundig Darkcloud?",a="Killing Grundig Darkcloud and his brutes is the conclusion of Makaba Flathoof's short vengeance chain. With the butcher slain, Makaba can at last mourn his village knowing justice was served.",al={"what next after grundig","flathoof chain continuation"}},{q="What is the prerequisite quest for this task?",a="You must first complete 'Avenge My Village,' in which Makaba Flathoof tests your resolve by having you strike down the Grimtotem mercenaries, reavers, and cutthroats stationed nearby.",al={"prereq kill grundig","quest before grundig"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem clan continues to sow discord among the tauren people, demonstrating through Grundig's slaughter that unity under the Horde will always be opposed by their cutthroat extremism.",["faction:Horde"]="Stonetalon is vital ground for the Horde's expansion into Kalimdor, and aggressive Grimtotem warlords like Grundig threaten supply routes linking the Barrens to Sun Rock Retreat."},kw={"brute","darkcloud","flathoof","grimtotem","grundig","makaba","post","stonetalon"},rel={"npc:makaba-flathoof","quest:6548","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Makaba Flathoof",level="18",faction="Horde",id=6629},src={"Kill Grundig Darkcloud"}}
E["subzone:battlescar-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Battlescar Valley",z="stonetalon",s="Battlescar Valley is a war-torn pass nestled between Cliffwalker Post and Farwatcher's Glen in the Stonetalon Mountains. Once a site of Horde logging operations, the area erupted into open violence when night elves assaulted the camp and sabotaged their heavy machinery. Today, skirmishes continue across ground shadowed by an ancient, enduring tree.",h="Battlescar Valley is a war-torn pass nestled between Cliffwalker Post and Farwatcher's Glen in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Clashing Front",b="Located in the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains, Battlescar Valley earned its name through violent escalation between the Horde and the Alliance. The Horde initially established a lumbering camp here, deploying advanced goblin-built machinery to harvest timber from the mountain forests. Night elf forces from nearby strongholds struck back swiftly, disrupting the harvesting efforts and setting a massive Super Reaper 6000 ablaze. The ruined machine now smolders as a monument to the clash, and the valley remains a contested battleground where neither side is willing to cede ground.",sp=0},{t="The Ancient at the Center",b="Despite the axes, fire, and ongoing bloodshed, the center of Battlescar Valley is dominated by a majestic ancient tree. Having endured through countless ages, the tree long served as a sanctuary of quiet learning and contemplation before the war arrived. Now caught directly in the crossfire of the faction conflict, it stands in stark contrast to the scorched earth, broken timber, and burning metal scattered across the valley floor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the valley called Battlescar Valley?",a="The valley earned its name after an aggressive night elf offensive struck a Horde lumbering outpost established in the pass. With machinery set ablaze and skirmishes constantly breaking out between the rival factions, the terrain has been thoroughly scarred by war.",al={"why battlescar","battlescar valley history","what happened in battlescar valley"}},{q="What is the burning machine in the valley?",a="The burning wreck is a Super Reaper 6000, a massive logging machine deployed by the Horde's goblin contractors. Night elf defenders attacked the outpost and set the harvester on fire to halt the clear-cutting of the mountain woods.",al={"burning harvester","super reaper 6000 battlescar","burning shredder"}},{q="What is the large tree standing in the middle of the valley?",a="It is an ancient tree that has survived for generations. Long before the Horde and Alliance brought their war to the valley, the tree served as a peaceful place of meditation and learning for the forest's stewards.",al={"battlescar valley tree","ancient tree stonetalon","big tree in battlescar"}},{q="Who controls Battlescar Valley right now?",a="Neither faction holds full control. The valley is an active contested zone situated between the night elf encampment at Farwatcher's Glen and the tauren settlement of Cliffwalker Post, resulting in constant friction.",al={"who controls battlescar valley","is battlescar valley alliance or horde"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the valley represents a critical defense against defilement, having successfully disabled destructive goblin timber machines to protect Stonetalon's sacred grounds.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde views Battlescar Valley as a contested resource hub and vital pass that must be held against unrelenting night elf ambushes."},kw={"ancient tree","battlescar valley","cliffwalker post","farwatcher's glen","logging","lumber","stonetalon mountains","super reaper 6000"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","quest:1093","subzone:farwatcher-s-glen","subzone:cliffwalker-post","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Battlescar Valley"}}
E["subzone:blackwolf-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackwolf River",z="stonetalon",s="Blackwolf River is a waterway flowing out of Cragpool Lake down through Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Once a clean mountain stream, its waters have become thoroughly polluted by the Venture Company's aggressive logging and industrial operations.",h="Blackwolf River is a waterway flowing out of Cragpool Lake down through Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="Industrial Runoff",b="Descending from Cragpool Lake, the Blackwolf River cuts across the basin of Windshear Crag. What should be a pristine alpine tributary has instead borne the brunt of unchecked goblin enterprise. As the Venture Company clears the surrounding woodlands with heavy machinery and buzzsaws, sludge, oil, and logging waste leach steadily into the current. The despoiled river stands as a vivid example of the commercial plunder threatening Stonetalon's wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Blackwolf River start and lead?",a="The river flows down out of Cragpool Lake in the upper reaches of the mountains and winds through the logged basin of Windshear Crag.",al={"blackwolf river source","where is blackwolf river","blackwolf river location"}},{q="Why is the river water polluted?",a="The Venture Company operates massive deforestation and mechanical logging rigs throughout Windshear Crag. Runoff from their steam machinery, waste, and clear-cutting drains directly into the watercourse.",al={"why is blackwolf river dirty","blackwolf river pollution","venture company pollution"}},{q="Who is currently operating along the river?",a="The Venture Company dominates the riverbank, utilizing the surrounding valley for heavy lumber harvesting and mechanical operations despite resistance from local wildlife and native inhabitants.",al={"who controls blackwolf river","who is at blackwolf river","enemies near blackwolf river"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The desecration of Blackwolf River by goblin timber operations is a sharp affront to the Cenarion Circle and all who revere the untamed waters of Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="Seeing the earth scarred and the waters fouled by profit-driven interlopers reinforces the tauren resolve to cleanse Stonetalon of reckless industrial blight."},kw={"blackwolf river","cragpool lake","logging","pollution","stonetalon mountains","venture co","venture company","windshear crag"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:cragpool-lake","topic:venture-company","zone:stonetalon","quest:764"},src={"Blackwolf River"}}
E["subzone:boulderslide-cavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderslide Cavern",z="stonetalon",s="Boulderslide Cavern is a subterranean warren tucked at the deepest end of Boulderslide Ravine in the Stonetalon Mountains. It serves as the primary den and excavation site for the local Boulderslide kobolds, who obsessively tunnel in search of glowing mineral formations.",h="Boulderslide Cavern is a subterranean warren tucked at the deepest end of Boulderslide Ravine in the...",sec={{t="The Resonite Dig",b="The Boulderslide kobolds have burrowed deep into the crags of Stonetalon, establishing Boulderslide Cavern as their stronghold. Unlike ordinary vermin merely seeking shelter, these kobolds mine frantically for resonite, a rare glowing purple crystal embedded throughout the stone. The crystals pulse with lingering earthen magic, driving the creatures into a defensive frenzy against any intruders who approach their dig.",sp=0},{t="The Slumbering Giant",b="Deeper inside the caverns, reckless excavation has breached ancient secrets. Embedded in the subterranean rock lies a resonite cask containing Goggeroc, a slumbering earthen from ages past. The kobolds' relentless digging around this mystical relic risks awakening a being imbued with primordial stone magic, posing a sudden danger to the entire ravine.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the kobolds mining here?",a="The kobolds are mining resonite, a rare purple crystal found embedded in the cavern's rock walls. The mineral hums with faint traces of earthen magic, making it a valuable prize and causing the kobolds to guard their caches fanatically.",al={"what is resonite","purple crystals stonetalon","why are kobolds mining"}},{q="Who is Goggeroc?",a="Goggeroc is an ancient earthen who lies dormant within a resonite cask deep inside the cavern. The kobolds' excavation around his resting place risks disturbing his centuries-long slumber.",al={"goggeroc lore","earthen in boulderslide","sleeping giant in cave"}},{q="Where is Boulderslide Cavern located?",a="The cavern entrance sits at the far end of Boulderslide Ravine, nestled in the craggy mountains of southern Stonetalon Mountains, just northeast of the path toward the Barrens.",al={"boulderslide cavern location","how to find boulderslide cavern","where is the cave"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in this cavern?",a="The Horde keeps watch on the cavern to curb the aggressive kobold infestation spilling into the ravine, and out of interest in the magical properties of the resonite crystals they mine.",al={"horde quests boulderslide","why send me to boulderslide"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The cavern is intensely worked by the Boulderslide clan, who tunnel relentlessly to uncover glowing veins of magical resonite.",["class:Shaman"]="The resonite crystals and the slumbering earthen Goggeroc both resonate with primordial earth magic, an echo of the world's ancient stone shapers."},kw={"boulderslide","cavern","earthen","goggeroc","kobold","resonite","stonetalon"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","quest:6421","quest:6481","topic:kobold"},src={"Boulderslide Cavern"}}
E["subzone:boulderslide-ravine"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderslide Ravine",z="stonetalon",s="Boulderslide Ravine is a rugged, secluded canyon tucked away in the central peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains, reached via Webwinder Path. Largely spared from the direct clashes between the Horde and Alliance, it serves as the rocky approach to Boulderslide Cavern and remains home to wild mountain beasts.",h="Boulderslide Ravine is a rugged, secluded canyon tucked away in the central peaks of the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Quiet Mountain Pass",b="Tucked away off Webwinder Path, Boulderslide Ravine is a narrow cut of rock in the Stonetalon heights. While loggers, night elves, and the Horde battle over timber and sacred glades throughout the region, this craggy pass remains relatively undisturbed by military forces. Wild mountain rams and roaming crag beasts like Cliff Stormers make up the local fauna, navigating the treacherous ledges and sheer stone walls. Prospectors also keep an eye on the ravine, as rich mineral veins frequently crop up along the rocky slopes leading deeper toward the cavern network.",sp=0},{t="Traces in the Stone",b="Opposite the entrance to Boulderslide Cavern lies a small, quiet cave overlooking the ravine. Lit by rough torches and stacked with weathered supply barrels, the shelter contains primitive tribal paintings across its interior walls. The crude artwork bears a striking resemblance to ancient tauren designs, suggesting that native tribes traveled or sought temporary shelter in these crags long before modern conflict swept into the mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Boulderslide Ravine located?",a="Boulderslide Ravine is located in the Stonetalon Mountains. It is reached by traveling along Webwinder Path into the higher crags.",al={"boulderslide ravine location","how to get to boulderslide ravine","where is boulderslide ravine"}},{q="What creatures inhabit Boulderslide Ravine?",a="The ravine is mainly populated by local wildlife, particularly mountain rams and dangerous crag stalkers such as Cliff Stormers.",al={"boulderslide ravine mobs","what is in boulderslide ravine"}},{q="What is the abandoned cave across from Boulderslide Cavern?",a="Facing the cavern entrance is a small alcove lit by torches and stocked with old barrels. Its stone walls display tribal pictographs that resemble traditional tauren art, pointing to past use by local wanderers or hunters.",al={"abandoned cave boulderslide","cave in boulderslide ravine","tauren cave stonetalon"}},{q="Why is Boulderslide Ravine significant?",a="It serves as the natural approach to Boulderslide Cavern, a subterranean lair deep in the mountains, and offers valuable mineral outcroppings for travelers passing through.",al={"what is boulderslide ravine for","boulderslide ravine purpose"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The steep rock walls of the ravine are a reliable place to spot mineral veins exposed by the mountain's shifting stone.",["race:Tauren"]="The faded art inside the small side cave bears the distinct touch of tauren tribal markers, hinting at ancestral paths through the Stonetalon heights."},kw={"boulderslide cavern","boulderslide ravine","cliff stormer","rams","stonetalon","webwinder path"},rel={"subzone:boulderslide-cavern","subzone:webwinder-path","quest:6421","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren"},src={"Boulderslide Ravine"}}
E["subzone:camp-aparaje"] = {t="subzone",n="Camp Aparaje",z="stonetalon",s="Camp Aparaje was once a peaceful tauren village nestled in the eastern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains. Today, it lies overrun and occupied by the hostile Grimtotem tribe, who slaughtered the original settlers and took the outpost for themselves.",h="Camp Aparaje was once a peaceful tauren village nestled in the eastern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Tragic Downfall",b="Perched along the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains, Camp Aparaje was established by peaceful tauren looking to live quietly in the highlands. That tranquility was shattered when raiders from the nearby Grimtotem Post, led by Grundig Darkcloud, launched a brutal and unprovoked assault. The villagers were butchered or driven away, and survivors such as Makaba Flathoof were left mourning the destruction of their home while dreading the fate of captive kin.",sp=0},{t="Under Grimtotem Sway",b="Now completely occupied by Grimtotem warriors, Camp Aparaje serves as a forward base of operations for the aggressive tribe in the region. Unlike typical Grimtotem settlements that fly blue markings, the great totem standing in Aparaje is carved with deep crimson paint, marking the bloody nature of its capture and the grim dominion of Grundig Darkcloud's brutes over the captured village.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who used to live at Camp Aparaje?",a="Camp Aparaje was inhabited by peaceful tauren affiliated with the Horde and Bloodhoof tribe, including Makaba Flathoof and his daughter Kaya, before the settlement was invaded.",al={"who lived here","camp aparaje original villagers","makaba flathoof village"}},{q="Why is the camp hostile to Horde players?",a="The village was violently seized by the Grimtotem tribe, a xenophobic and treacherous tauren clan that refuses allegiance to Cairne Bloodhoof and actively attacks outsiders, including members of the Horde.",al={"why are tauren attacking me","who controls camp aparaje","why is camp aparaje red"}},{q="Who led the assault on Camp Aparaje?",a="The raid was spearheaded by Grundig Darkcloud, a brutal Grimtotem chieftain operating out of Grimtotem Post who seeks to expand his tribe's violent grip over Stonetalon.",al={"who attacked aparaje","grundig darkcloud","who is the leader here"}},{q="What happened to the surviving villagers?",a="Most inhabitants were killed during the raid. A few managed to flee, while others, like young Kaya Flathoof, were captured by the Grimtotem and held hostage within the occupied camp.",al={"kaya flathoof","where are the survivors","are there survivors"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The ruins of Camp Aparaje serve as a bitter reminder of the cruelty of Magatha's Grimtotem tribe, proving that not all children of the Earth Mother share Cairne Bloodhoof's vision of honor and peace.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the Grimtotem from Camp Aparaje is a matter of vengeance and defense, ensuring the treacherous tribe is punished for butchering innocent Horde subjects in Stonetalon."},kw={"camp aparaje","grimtotem","grimtotem post","grundig darkcloud","kaya flathoof","makaba flathoof","stonetalon"},rel={"quest:6548","quest:6629","quest:6523","npc:makaba-flathoof","topic:grimtotem-tribe","zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Camp Aparaje"}}
E["subzone:charred-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Charred Vale",z="stonetalon",s="The Charred Vale is a smoldering valley in southwestern Stonetalon Mountains, devastated by the reckless deforestation and machinery of the Venture Company. Once a thriving haven for treants and chimaeras, it is now engulfed in flames, roving elementals, and hostile black dragonkin.",h="The Charred Vale is a smoldering valley in southwestern Stonetalon Mountains, devastated by the reckless...",sec={{t="A Scorched Woodland",b="Not long ago, this southwest basin was a flourishing alpine wood guarded by majestic treants and inhabited by native chimaeras and harpies. Its ruin began with the arrival of the Venture Company. The greedy goblin outfit clear-cut the forest with explosive machinery, corrupting the guardians and awakening chaotic fissure-born fire elementals. Though the treants eventually forced the goblins back, the land was left broken, scarred by fire, and tainted by whatever foul devices the retreating loggers deployed.",sp=0},{t="Struggles of Renewal",b="Today, blackened ancients wander blindly through smoke and ash alongside enraged elementals and nesting black whelps and drakes. Bloodfury harpies roost in the skeletal snags, defending what remains of their territory. Despite the hostility of the valley, druids from Sun Rock Retreat refuse to abandon the region, dispatching travelers to sow enchanted seeds and tend the corrupted ancients in a persistent campaign to reclaim the scorched earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Charred Vale on fire?",a="The devastation was caused by the Venture Company's ruthless logging operations. Their destructive machinery and aggressive deforestation enraged the primal spirits of the land and unleashed destructive fire elementals that spread across the valley.",al={"why is it burning","who burned charred vale","what happened to charred vale"}},{q="Can the forest in the Charred Vale ever recover?",a="Tauren druids from nearby Sun Rock Retreat believe it can. They task travelers with soothing the maddened treants and planting enchanted earthen seeds amidst the ash, hoping to coax green shoots from the ruined soil.",al={"is charred vale healing","druids charred vale"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Charred Vale?",a="The basin is crawling with hostile elemental fire spirits, blackened and vengeful ancients, Scorched Basilisks, and wild chimaeras. It is also plagued by Bloodfury harpies and dangerous broods of black drakes and whelps.",al={"monsters in charred vale","what lives in charred vale"}},{q="What was the Charred Vale called before it burned?",a="Its original name has been lost to time. Local trail signs have their older names covered over, but it was renowned as a lush woodland sanctuary long before goblin axes arrived.",al={"charred vale old name","original name of charred vale"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The devastation here serves as a harsh warning of what happens when natural balance is shattered by uncontrolled greed, making the valley a key focus for reclamation efforts.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating out of Sun Rock Retreat, Horde forces work closely with Cenarion allies to contain the elemental unrest and push back the corruptive lingering aftermath of the Venture Company."},kw={"blackened ancient","bloodfury","charred vale","chimaera","fire elemental","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","venture company"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","topic:venture-company","quest:1083","quest:1084","quest:6381","quest:1844","topic:druid"},src={"Charred Vale"}}
E["subzone:cliffwalker-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Cliffwalker Post",z="stonetalon",s="Cliffwalker Post is a secluded tauren settlement perched atop a high bluff in the northern reaches of the Stonetalon Mountains. Home to the peaceful Cliffwalker family, it stands as a serene, totem-lined haven looking down upon the crags and canyons below.",h="Cliffwalker Post is a secluded tauren settlement perched atop a high bluff in the northern reaches of the...",sec={{t="A Sanctuary on the Rise",b="Perched upon an elevated bluff, Cliffwalker Post serves as a home and watchpost for the Cliffwalker family and their kin. Its steep, rising approaches are marked by carved tauren totems that guide travelers and honor the earth. Tauren braves vigilantly patrol the high grounds and winding paths, keeping watch over the encroaching turmoil of the surrounding mountains while striving to maintain their quiet connection to the land.",sp=0},{t="Guarded Isolation",b="Because of its dramatic elevation, Cliffwalker Post is inherently defensible, sheltered from many of the landbound predators and territorial conflicts that ravage lower Stonetalon. Though the Cliffwalkers generally seek a calm, harmonious existence under the sun, strangers wandering near the foot of their rise are watched with intense scrutiny, and armed braves stand ready to descend upon anyone perceived as a threat to their home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Cliffwalker Post?",a="The post is inhabited by members of the tauren Cliffwalker family along with their brave defenders and elders who tend to the high bluff.",al={"who is at cliffwalker post","cliffwalker post residents","cliffwalker tribe"}},{q="Where is Cliffwalker Post located?",a="It is situated high up on a plateau in northern Stonetalon Mountains, overlooking the rugged crags and accessed via steep, totem-lined rises.",al={"cliffwalker post location","where is cliffwalker post","how to get to cliffwalker post"}},{q="Are the Cliffwalkers welcoming to outsiders?",a="While the Cliffwalkers are of a peaceful disposition, their sentinels are fiercely protective of their home. Armed braves aggressively confront suspicious travelers who approach unannounced.",al={"are cliffwalkers friendly","cliffwalker post alliance","can alliance go to cliffwalker post"}},{q="Why did the tauren build a settlement here?",a="The elevated vantage point provides both security from lowland threats and a serene place to commune with the spirits and the Earth Mother away from crowded settlements.",al={"why is cliffwalker post here","purpose of cliffwalker post"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Cliffwalker Post reflects the quiet resilience of your people, offering a traditional haven where totems watch over high mountain ridges.",["faction:Horde"]="The outpost represents one of the northernmost tauren enclaves in Stonetalon, keeping an eye on the treacherous mountain pathways."},kw={"braves","cliffwalker","cliffwalker post","horde","stonetalon","tauren","totems"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","topic:tauren","topic:horde","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Cliffwalker Post"}}
E["subzone:cragpool-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Cragpool Lake",z="stonetalon",s="Cragpool Lake is a body of water tucked inside Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Looming above its dark waters sits a massive timber structure erected by the Venture Company, while the depths below harbor a notoriously aggressive beast.",h="Cragpool Lake is a body of water tucked inside Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Industrial Encroachment and Deadly Depths",b="Nestled deep within Windshear Crag, Cragpool Lake lies directly beneath the towering logging apparatus built by the Venture Company. An enormous wooden structure spans above the water, once serving as the prime vantage point from which Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle commanded clear-cutting operations across the mountain valley. While much of the syndicate has scaled back their presence in the crag, holdouts and sentries linger across the catwalks and platforms overhead. Down below, the lake has been declared strictly off-limits by the goblins due to the arrival of Cragjaw, a massive and predatory fish prowling the murky water beneath the gears.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the massive wooden structure hanging over the lake?",a="It is an industrial superstructure erected by the Venture Company to manage their extensive logging and mining efforts in Windshear Crag. It connects platforms and heavy machinery spanning directly over the lake.",al={"venture co platform","cragpool scaffolding","cragpool bridge"}},{q="Who oversees the operations at Cragpool Lake?",a="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a key operative for the Venture Company, established his perch atop the high scaffolding to supervise the deforestation and resource extraction throughout Windshear Crag.",al={"who leads venture co here","who is the boss here","gerenzo wrenchwhistle"}},{q="Why is swimming in Cragpool Lake dangerous?",a="The lake was declared off-limits due to Cragjaw, an enormous, aggressive predatory fish that took up residence in the waters beneath the goblin scaffolding, attacking anything foolish enough to enter.",al={"why off limits","lake monster","what is in cragpool lake","cragjaw"}},{q="Has the Venture Company abandoned Cragpool Lake?",a="Although the bulk of the syndicate's broader force has withdrawn from parts of Windshear Crag, a stubborn contingent of armed overseers and operators remains firmly entrenched on the scaffolding above the water.",al={"is venture company gone","who lives at cragpool lake"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The towering timber scaffolding and cantilevered machinery above Cragpool Lake offer a textbook display of goblin industrial expediency—built quickly, heavily loaded, and indifferent to natural terrain.",["class:Druid"]="The runoff, timber platforms, and disruption around Cragpool Lake stand as an ugly scar in Stonetalon, warping the local ecosystem and displacing its native wildlife."},kw={"cragjaw","cragpool lake","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","stonetalon","venture company","windshear crag"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","quest:1096","topic:venture-company"},src={"Cragpool Lake"}}
E["subzone:deep-reaches"] = {t="subzone",n="Deep Reaches",z="stonetalon",s="The Deep Reaches is a disputed underground mine situated deep within the central Stonetalon Mountains. Both the Alliance and the Horde have tunneled into the cavern from opposing sides, sparking a deadly subterranean confrontation between dwarven prospectors and local orc forces.",h="The Deep Reaches is a disputed underground mine situated deep within the central Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Clashing Excavation",b="What began as separate excavation efforts quickly escalated into a subterranean warzone. The dwarven Explorers' League drove tunnels into the rock to claim the mountain's rich mineral veins, only to breach an opening directly into the rear approaches of the Horde stronghold at Krom'gar Fortress. With their base compromised from beneath, orc assassins surged into the shafts to silence the miners, leaving the surviving Alliance workers cut off and desperately attempting to collapse the tunnels to seal out the onslaught.",sp=0},{t="Chaos in the Deeps",b="The Horde's excavation efforts have fared little better. While their fighters push deeper into the dwarven shafts, the Horde's own workers accidentally disturbed the fragile subterranean balance, awakening Raging Earth Elementals. These furious stone spirits rampaged through the lower works, slaughtering miners and trapping hapless peons in isolated nooks. Now, both sides struggle to salvage equipment and rescue stranded personnel while fighting each other and the awakened earth itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Deep Reaches?",a="The Deep Reaches is a contested mine in the central Stonetalon Mountains where Alliance and Horde excavations accidentally breached each other's networks deep beneath the rock.",al={"deep reaches overview","what is this mine","deep reaches lore"}},{q="Who is currently fighting inside the mine?",a="The conflict primarily involves the Alliance's dwarven Explorers' League defending their dig sites against Horde assassins from Krom'gar Fortress, while both sides must contend with rampaging earth elementals.",al={"who is fighting here","deep reaches factions","enemies in deep reaches"}},{q="Why are there earth elementals inside the tunnels?",a="Aggressive digging on the Horde side of the excavation disturbed the subterranean spirits of Stonetalon, causing Raging Earth Elementals to awaken and overrun the lower tunnels.",al={"why are there elementals","deep reaches monsters","raging earth elementals"}},{q="Why are there Lordaeron flags near the Alliance entrance?",a="Alongside the standard Stormwind banners, flags bearing the crest of Lordaeron mark the expedition, representing northern refugees and veterans who joined the Alliance forces operating in Kalimdor.",al={"lordaeron flags","why lordaeron symbol","stormwind and lordaeron"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The rich stone of Stonetalon drew both factions to dig, but reckless excavation caused cave-ins and awakened violent earth elementals.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Explorers' League needs courageous fighters to rescue trapped dwarven miners and seal off the shafts before Krom'gar assassins completely overrun the site."},kw={"deep reaches","elementals","explorers' league","krom'gar","lordaeron","miners","peons","stonetalon"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:krom-gar-fortress","topic:explorers-league","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:lordaeron","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Deep Reaches"}}
E["subzone:farwatcher-s-glen"] = {t="subzone",n="Farwatcher's Glen",z="stonetalon",s="Farwatcher's Glen is an Alliance outpost tucked away in the rugged heights of the Stonetalon Mountains, southwest of Thal'darah Grove. Built with traditional night elf architecture, the camp serves as a defensive refuge and staging ground for Alliance forces navigating the treacherous crags of the region.",h="Farwatcher's Glen is an Alliance outpost tucked away in the rugged heights of the Stonetalon Mountains...",sec={{t="A Sentinel Bastion in the Heights",b="Nestled beneath towering cliffs southwest of Thal'darah Grove, Farwatcher's Glen stands as an Alliance settlement within the contested Stonetalon Mountains. Though fashioned in the graceful, open woodwork characteristic of night elf outposts, the glen shelters travelers and soldiers from across the Alliance. Roosting ravens dot the branches and rooftops, while sentries keep a vigilant watch over the surrounding ridges, monitoring Horde incursions and the wild threats that haunt the peaks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Farwatcher's Glen?",a="It is an Alliance settlement and outpost situated in the Stonetalon Mountains, positioned southwest of Thal'darah Grove and Thal'darah Overlook. It provides shelter, watchtowers, and a foothold for Alliance forces traversing the crags.",al={"farwatcher glen","what is this place","farwatchers glen stonetalon"}},{q="Which faction controls Farwatcher's Glen?",a="Farwatcher's Glen is entirely aligned with the Alliance. It features night elf architecture and houses various defenders and allies working together to secure the surrounding mountain passes.",al={"is this horde or alliance","farwatchers glen faction","who owns this town"}},{q="Why are there so many ravens around the glen?",a="A significant number of ravens nest and roost around Farwatcher's Glen. In night elf culture and druidic tradition, ravens often serve as watchful scouts and messengers, well-suited to the high crags of Stonetalon.",al={"ravens farwatchers glen","why all the ravens","birds in farwatchers"}},{q="Where does this settlement connect to in Stonetalon?",a="The outpost maintains regional connections across the Stonetalon Mountains, sitting in close proximity to Thal'darah Grove and Thal'darah Overlook, while keeping communication with northern strongholds like Nijel's Point and Windshear Hold.",al={"where to go from here","flight routes farwatcher","nearby towns"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Farwatcher's Glen provides a critical vantage point and haven in the hostile, contested heights of Stonetalon, protecting supply routes and monitoring enemy movements.",["race:NightElf"]="The glen's traditional architecture and avian watchers reflect the Kaldorei presence striving to safeguard Stonetalon's sacred groves and wilderness from exploitation."},kw={"alliance","farwatcher's glen","farwatchers glen","ravens","stonetalon","thal'darah"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:thal-darah-grove","subzone:thal-darah-overlook","subzone:nijel-s-point","subzone:windshear-hold","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Farwatcher's Glen"}}
E["subzone:greatwood-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Greatwood Vale",z="stonetalon",s="Greatwood Vale is a forested valley nestled in the eastern foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains, reached via the perilous Webwinder Path. It sits between the Horde outpost of Malaka'jin and the Alliance's Northwatch Expedition Base Camp, making its shaded woods a tense crossroads. Recently, the hostile Grimtotem tribe seized the vale, using it as a staging ground for bloody assaults on neighboring settlements.",h="Greatwood Vale is a forested valley nestled in the eastern foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains, reached via...",sec={{t="A Contested Valley",b="Tucked away off the Webwinder Path, Greatwood Vale has become a violent frontier. Its position places it squarely between the Alliance soldiers pushing down from the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp to the north and the Horde camp of Malaka'jin to the south. Yet it is neither human nor orc who dominates the canopy today. The Grimtotem tribe, under the ruthless leadership of Grundig Darkcloud, has moved into the vale in force, cutting off safe passage and bringing terror to the surrounding foothills.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of Camp Aparaje",b="The Grimtotem did not merely occupy Greatwood Vale; they used it to orchestrate the butchery of nearby Camp Aparaje. Sweeping out of the woods, Darkcloud's raiders slaughtered nearly every tauren inhabiting the encampment. Makaba Flathoof, one of the few survivors who managed to flee the carnage, now directs vengeful Horde warriors straight into the heart of Greatwood Vale to cut down the renegade Grimtotem and put an end to Grundig Darkcloud.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Greatwood Vale located?",a="Greatwood Vale is tucked into the foothills of the Stonetalon Mountains, accessible via the Webwinder Path. It lies directly north of the Horde outpost Malaka'jin and south of the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp.",al={"greatwood vale location","how to get to greatwood vale","where is greatwood vale"}},{q="Who controls Greatwood Vale right now?",a="The valley is occupied by the hostile Grimtotem tribe, led locally by Grundig Darkcloud. They hold the woods with warbands and spellcasters, menacing anyone attempting to travel the region.",al={"who lives in greatwood vale","greatwood vale enemies","grimtotem in greatwood vale"}},{q="What happened at Camp Aparaje?",a="The Grimtotem launched a surprise attack from Greatwood Vale upon Camp Aparaje, massacring most of its peaceful tauren residents. Makaba Flathoof survived the slaughter and now seeks vengeance against the raiders and their leader.",al={"camp aparaje lore","what happened to aparaje","why did grimtotem attack"}},{q="Why is the Horde fighting the Grimtotem here?",a="Although the Grimtotem are nominally part of the Horde through Thunder Bluff, their aggressive splinter factions attack fellow Horde members without hesitation. After the slaughter at Camp Aparaje, the Horde sanctions open warfare against Darkcloud's band in the vale.",al={"why kill grimtotem","makaba flathoof quest","avenge my village"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem's treacherous slaughter of fellow tauren at Camp Aparaje makes the cleansing of Greatwood Vale a deeply personal, sorrowful duty for Thunder Bluff's loyal children.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Greatwood Vale is essential to protect the fragile southern outpost of Malaka'jin from sudden flank attacks by rogue Grimtotem."},kw={"camp aparaje","greatwood vale","grimtotem","grundig darkcloud","makaba flathoof","malaka'jin","stonetalon","webwinder path"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:camp-aparaje","npc:makaba-flathoof","quest:6548","quest:6629","topic:grimtotem-tribe","subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:webwinder-path"},src={"Greatwood Vale"}}
E["subzone:krom-gar-fortress"] = {t="subzone",n="Krom'gar Fortress",z="stonetalon",s="Krom'gar Fortress is a heavily fortified Horde military stronghold established in Windshear Crag within the Stonetalon Mountains. Built directly opposite the Alliance stronghold of Windshear Hold, it serves as the staging ground for Horde forces contesting the region. Beneath the cliffs of the base lies access to the subterranean tunnels known as the Deep Reaches.",h="Krom'gar Fortress is a heavily fortified Horde military stronghold established in Windshear Crag within the...",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Crag",b="Perched amidst the craggy logging lands of Windshear Crag, Krom'gar Fortress serves as the primary military anchor for the Horde in central Stonetalon. Despite its modest construction—consisting primarily of a reinforced burrow, a working blacksmith, and two watchtowers—the post functions as a bristling frontline redoubt. It stands in direct defiance of the nearby Alliance forces at Windshear Hold, establishing a contested front over the resources and passages through the mountains.",sp=0},{t="Controlling the Reaches",b="Beyond its vantage over the surface warfare of Windshear Crag, the fortress commands critical subterranean access. Directly beneath the fortress cliffs sits the Horde-held entrance leading down into the Deep Reaches. Through this subterranean network, Horde troops maintain tactical passage while keeping watch over underground threats and the mineral-rich depths beneath the range.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Krom'gar Fortress?",a="It is a fortified Horde military redoubt located within Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. It acts as an operational hub against local Alliance advances.",al={"kromgar base","what is this place","stonetalon horde fort"}},{q="Where is the entrance to the Deep Reaches located?",a="The entrance to the Deep Reaches lies directly beneath the fortress cliffs at the base of the rock formation.",al={"deep reaches entrance","how to enter deep reaches","cave below fortress"}},{q="Who opposes the Horde at Krom'gar Fortress?",a="Alliance forces stationed across the valley at Windshear Hold directly contest Krom'gar Fortress for control over Windshear Crag.",al={"enemies nearby","who is the alliance here","windshear hold alliance"}},{q="What structures make up the fortress?",a="Despite the grand name, the outpost consists of a fortified subterranean burrow, a functioning blacksmith forge, and two watchtowers guarding the perimeter.",al={"what buildings are here","fortress size","layout of kromgar fortress"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The fortress provides a vital bastion in the contested Stonetalon Mountains, keeping the Alliance at Windshear Hold at bay and safeguarding subterranean supply lines.",["faction:Alliance"]="Directly facing Windshear Hold, this fortified encampment represents the primary obstacle to Alliance supremacy over Windshear Crag."},kw={"burrow","deep reaches","fortress","horde","krom'gar","stonetalon","windshear crag","windshear hold"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:deep-reaches","subzone:windshear-hold","zone:stonetalon","topic:horde","topic:alliance","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:malaka-jin"},src={"Krom'gar Fortress"}}
E["subzone:malaka-jin"] = {t="subzone",n="Malaka'jin",z="stonetalon",s="Malaka'jin is a small Horde encampment nestled in the lower hills of the Stonetalon Mountains, just south of the Grimtotem Post. Inhabited primarily by Darkspear troll hunters, the settlement serves as a rustic waystation and hunting outpost for travelers ascending into the rugged peaks from the Barrens.",h="Malaka'jin is a small Horde encampment nestled in the lower hills of the Stonetalon Mountains, just south of...",sec={{t="A Hunters' Refuge",b="Tucked away near the main path into the Stonetalon Mountains, Malaka'jin provides a welcome sanctuary for Horde wanderers venturing into contested heights. The village is home to a band of rugged troll hunters who eke out a living off the crags and scrublands. While living modestly, these hunters offer supplies, trade their fresh game to weary adventurers, and keep a wary eye on the hostile mountain wildlife and the belligerent Grimtotem tauren lurking further up the trails.",sp=0},{t="A Foothold in the Heights",b="Perched precariously near the boundary of the Barrens, Malaka'jin marks one of the earliest Horde presences established in Stonetalon. Though small and quiet compared to the major fortress at Sun Rock Retreat further north, it functions as a vital logistical anchor, allowing Horde trackers to monitor tribal unrest and secure the winding roads against encroaching threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Malaka'jin?",a="Malaka'jin is a small Horde village and outpost in the southern Stonetalon Mountains. It is inhabited by a community of Darkspear troll hunters who provide shelter, trade, and supplies to travelers climbing up from the Barrens.",al={"where is malakajin","what is this place","malakajin stonetalon"}},{q="Who lives in Malaka'jin?",a="The settlement is populated almost entirely by troll hunters. They sustain themselves by hunting the mountain game and trading meat and leather with passing adventurers.",al={"malakajin npcs","who is here","trolls in stonetalon"}},{q="What threats face the camp?",a="Aside from fierce mountain predators, the village is situated directly south of the hostile Grimtotem Post, leaving the small troll camp constantly vigilant against aggression from the antagonistic tauren tribe.",al={"malakajin enemies","who attacks malakajin"}},{q="Is there a flight master here?",a="No. In this era, Malaka'jin has no flight master. Adventurers traveling through the Stonetalon Mountains must rely on the flight master at Sun Rock Retreat further northwest or traverse the road on foot.",al={"malakajin flight path","fly to malakajin"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Malaka'jin is a proud demonstration of troll self-reliance and tracking prowess, carving out a home in the rugged heights far from Kalimdor's tropical shores.",["faction:Horde"]="Malaka'jin serves as the Horde's southernmost threshold in Stonetalon, offering a vital waystation on the trail between the Barrens and the northern mountain strongholds."},kw={"darkspear","grimtotem","horde","hunters","malaka'jin","outpost","stonetalon","trolls"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","topic:horde","topic:troll","topic:grimtotem-tribe"},src={"Malaka'jin"}}
E["subzone:mirkfallon-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirkfallon Lake",z="stonetalon",s="Mirkfallon Lake sits in a central highland basin in the Stonetalon Mountains, nestled beneath the sheer cliffs of Windshear Crag. Its waters and surrounding banks teem with native wildlife, including aggressive slimes, roaming thunder lizards, and descending wyverns.",h="Mirkfallon Lake sits in a central highland basin in the Stonetalon Mountains, nestled beneath the sheer...",sec={{t="A Highland Basin",b="Positioned at the geographic center of the Stonetalon range, Mirkfallon Lake rests between the mountain passes leading south toward the Webwinder Path and north toward Cliffwalker Post and Stonetalon Peak. Fed by highland runoff, the lake offers a fertile oasis amidst the craggy peaks, drawing thunder lizards down to drink and wyverns from their roosts high above. The waters are also inhabited by strange, bubbling slimes, turning an otherwise serene mountain tarn into a hazardous crossing for lone travelers.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of the Crag",b="Paths crisscross the lake basin in all directions. To the east, rocky tracks ascend into Windshear Crag and the logging operations running deep into the forested valleys. Travelers pressing north past the lake climb toward night elven sanctums and tauren heights, while those skirting south must contend with venomous spider hollows. As a result, the shores of Mirkfallon Lake often serve as an unpredictable crossing point for explorers and scouts navigating the contested mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live around Mirkfallon Lake?",a="The lake and its shoreline are home to roaming thunder lizards, noxious ooze slimes in the shallow waters, and mountain wyverns that hunt around the surrounding basin and nest in the heights overhead.",al={"mirkfallon lake beasts","mirkfallon wildlife","what is at mirkfallon lake"}},{q="Where does the lake lead?",a="Climbing north leads past Cliffwalker Post toward Stonetalon Peak. Heading south descends through Webwinder Path, while the rocky ascents to the east wind up into Windshear Crag.",al={"mirkfallon paths","where does mirkfallon go","mirkfallon lake directions"}},{q="Is Mirkfallon Lake safe to fish in?",a="The lake is rich with sagefish and floating salvage, making it tempting for anglers. However, aggressive beasts such as slimes and wyverns frequent the shoreline, making undisturbed fishing difficult.",al={"fishing mirkfallon lake","can i fish in mirkfallon"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The wild beasts around Mirkfallon Lake represent the delicate balance of Stonetalon's wilderness, situated uncomfortably close to the encroaching mechanical axes in the crag above."},kw={"mirkfallon","mirkfallon lake","stonetalon lake","stonetalon thunder lizards","windshear lake"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:webwinder-path","subzone:cliffwalker-post","subzone:stonetalon-peak"},src={"Mirkfallon Lake"}}
E["subzone:northwatch-expedition-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Northwatch Expedition Base Camp",z="stonetalon",s="Perched high on the ridges overlooking Greatwood Vale and Grimtotem Post, the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp is a fortified Alliance redoubt in the Stonetalon Mountains. Commanded by Force Commander Valen, it secures critical human military operations and shelters dwarven excavators probing the ancient earth below.",h="Perched high on the ridges overlooking Greatwood Vale and Grimtotem Post, the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp...",sec={{t="A Foothold on the Ridge",b="Tucked away in the mountains above Greatwood Vale, the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp serves as the forward staging ground for Theramore-aligned forces in Stonetalon. Under the firm command of Force Commander Valen, Northwatch Infantry hold the heights against Horde scouts and local threats, while an open stone pavilion serves weary soldiers and travelers as a rudimentary inn. From this vantage point, the Alliance surveys the volatile valleys below, keeping a watchful eye on both Horde movements and nearby Grimtotem encampments.",sp=0},{t="The Dig Below",b="The camp exists not merely as a military outpost, but to protect and sustain the Alliance's nearby mining and archeological operations. Troops stationed here defend the passages leading to the Unearthed Grounds and the cavernous shafts of the Deep Reaches. Dwarven scholars from the Explorers' League rely entirely on the camp's garrison to shield their deep digging from hostile counterattacks, turning the surrounding slopes into an active theater of border warfare.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is in charge of this camp?",a="The outpost is headed by Force Commander Valen, who coordinates the garrison's infantry and oversees the protection of the surrounding excavation sites.",al={"camp commander","valen","who runs northwatch base camp"}},{q="Why are Northwatch troops all the way up in Stonetalon?",a="Northwatch forces have pushed inland from the coast to establish strategic Alliance footholds in Kalimdor. Here, their primary mission is protecting the Explorers' League digs in the Unearthed Grounds and maintaining pressure on Horde operations across Stonetalon.",al={"why are theramore troops here","why northwatch stonetalon","alliance purpose here"}},{q="What are the Alliance digging for nearby?",a="Alliance miners and scholars from the Explorers' League are excavating the Deep Reaches and the Unearthed Grounds, searching for mineral riches and ancient relics buried beneath the Stonetalon crags.",al={"what is the excavation","why are dwarves digging","deep reaches dig"}},{q="Is there an inn here?",a="Yes, although it consists of an open stone gazebo rather than a proper building. Travelers can rest their boots and bind their hearthstones with the garrison's innkeeper.",al={"hearthstone here","innkeeper","can i bind here"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This camp represents one of the few safe havens for Alliance forces deep in central Kalimdor, providing vital support for operations against regional Horde incursions.",["faction:Horde"]="The camp acts as a hostile staging ground right in Stonetalon, fueling the unwanted Alliance expansion into the Deep Reaches and threatening nearby outposts."},kw={"base camp","deep reaches","expedition","explorers league","greatwood vale","northwatch","stonetalon","unearthed grounds","valen"},rel={"npc:force-commander-valen","subzone:unearthed-grounds","subzone:deep-reaches","subzone:greatwood-vale","zone:stonetalon","topic:explorers-league","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Northwatch Expedition Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-eldre-thar"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Eldre'thar",z="stonetalon",s="Tucked away inside Sishir Canyon in the Stonetalon Mountains lie the Ruins of Eldre'thar, the shattered remnants of an ancient Highborne settlement. Today, the sunken stonework is haunted by spectral night elves who linger by the waters, reliving their final arcane rituals.",h="Tucked away inside Sishir Canyon in the Stonetalon Mountains lie the Ruins of Eldre'thar, the shattered...",sec={{t="A Haunted Haven",b="Hidden deep within the winding defiles of Sishir Canyon, Eldre'thar stands as a quiet monument to the ancient kaldorei empire before the Great Sundering. Like many Highborne enclaves across Kalimdor, its marble arches and courtyards eventually fell into ruin, yet the spirits of its arcane practitioners never departed. Phantom sorcerers and spirits still glide along the lakeside, endlessly reenacting spells and rituals frozen in time. For travelers braving the crags of Stonetalon, the ruins offer a chilling glimpse into the stubborn memories of a bygone aristocratic caste.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Eldre'thar?",a="The Ruins of Eldre'thar are the ancient stone remains of a Highborne night elf settlement situated within Sishir Canyon in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"ruins of eldre'thar","eldrethar lore","what is this place"}},{q="Why are there ghosts here?",a="The spectral figures inhabiting the ruins are the restless ghosts of ancient Highborne elves. Bound to the site of their demise, they endlessly wander the shores and channel old magic.",al={"why are there spirits","highborne ghosts stonetalon","who are the spirits"}},{q="Where are these ruins located?",a="You can find Eldre'thar nestled inside Sishir Canyon, an enclosed rocky gorge within the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"eldrethar location","how to find eldre'thar","where is eldrethar"}},{q="What were the Highborne doing by the lake?",a="The spectral sorcerers are locked in ritualistic magic around the water's edge, echoing forgotten rites practiced by the Highborne before the Sundering shattered their civilization.",al={"lake rituals","why are sorcerers channeling","eldrethar sorcerers"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Eldre'thar serves as a somber reminder of the Highborne hubris that fractured kaldorei society and drew ancient catastrophe upon ancient Kalimdor.",["class:Mage"]="The ethereal rituals whispered along the waters show how deeply ingrained the arcane arts were in early night elf civilization before the Great Sundering."},kw={"eldre'thar","ghosts","highborne","ruins of eldre'thar","sishir canyon","sorcerers","stonetalon mountains"},rel={"subzone:sishir-canyon","zone:stonetalon","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Eldre'thar"}}
E["subzone:sishir-canyon"] = {t="subzone",n="Sishir Canyon",z="stonetalon",s="Sishir Canyon is a rugged gorge in the Stonetalon Mountains, carving an eastward path through the craggy heights. Thickly swarmed by monstrous Deepmoss spiders and choked in webbing, it serves as the dangerous approach to the Ruins of Eldre'thar. Travelers who brave its tangled depths must contend with venomous arachnids and their brooding matriarch.",h="Sishir Canyon is a rugged gorge in the Stonetalon Mountains, carving an eastward path through the craggy...",sec={{t="The Webbed Pass",b="Branching off the mountain roads of the Stonetalon range, Sishir Canyon is a treacherous natural corridor cutting toward the ancient Ruins of Eldre'thar. Rather than a quiet mountain trail, the gorge has been thoroughly overrun by Deepmoss spiders. Their sticky silken sheets and clusters of egg sacs smother the stony ground and rock walls, transforming the ravine into a living nest. Travelers and sentinels seeking the night elven ruins beyond must cut their way through swarms of aggressive webspinners.",sp=0},{t="Besseleth's Domain",b="Lurking in the deepest recess of the canyon is Besseleth, the massive and deadly matriarch of the Deepmoss brood. Her venom and monstrous size make her a terror to anyone attempting to secure the pass. Local forces in Stonetalon keep a wary watch on the canyon, warning adventurers that venturing into the webbed recesses means facing not just scattered spiders, but an apex predator fiercely guarding her brood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sishir Canyon?",a="Sishir Canyon is a spider-infested gorge in the Stonetalon Mountains that winds from the main mountain paths toward the ancient Ruins of Eldre'thar.",al={"where is sishir canyon","sishir canyon location"}},{q="What creatures live in the canyon?",a="The canyon is thoroughly claimed by predatory Deepmoss spiders. The arachnids have coated the ravine in dense webbing and egg sacs, preying on anything that enters their territory.",al={"monsters in sishir canyon","spiders in stonetalon canyon"}},{q="Who is Besseleth?",a="Besseleth is the formidable spider matriarch dwelling deep within Sishir Canyon. She leads the Deepmoss brood and poses the greatest threat to travelers passing through the area.",al={"besseleth location","giant spider sishir canyon"}},{q="Where does Sishir Canyon lead?",a="Following the canyon eastward leads directly out to the Ruins of Eldre'thar, an ancient night elven site tucked high in the mountains.",al={"what is at the end of sishir canyon","path through sishir canyon"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The overrun canyon cuts off easy, safe passage to the ancestral Ruins of Eldre'thar, requiring Kaldorei sentinels and scholars to fight through dense spider nests to reach their heritage.",["class:Hunter"]="The dangerous webbing and venomous Deepmoss spiders make Sishir Canyon a demanding testing ground for hunters tracking and trapping wild beasts in tight ravine quarters."},kw={"besseleth","deepmoss","eldre'thar","sishir canyon","spiders","stonetalon","webbing"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:ruins-of-eldre-thar"},src={"Sishir Canyon"}}
E["subzone:sludgewerks"] = {t="subzone",n="Sludgewerks",z="stonetalon",s="Sludgewerks is a small Horde industrial platform situated along the shores of Mirkfallon Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains. Operated by goblins, the facility balances crude industry with the nearby natural habitat of the region's native wyverns.",h="Sludgewerks is a small Horde industrial platform situated along the shores of Mirkfallon Lake in the...",sec={{t="Industrial Encroachment",b="Perched on the edge of Mirkfallon Lake, Sludgewerks represents the Horde's mechanical and logistical footprint in Stonetalon. Run primarily by goblins, the installation was constructed with the unusual intent of minimizing direct disruption to the surrounding wyvern population. In practice, however, building a mechanical platform squarely beneath a roost of wild flying beasts has created unforeseen hazards for the technicians, who must regularly contend with falling wyvern guano and the harsh realities of Kalimdor's wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sludgewerks?",a="Sludgewerks is an industrial Horde encampment located on the shores of Mirkfallon Lake in Stonetalon Mountains, overseen and maintained by goblin operators.",al={"sludgewerks purpose","what is this place","sludgewerks horde"}},{q="Who controls this camp?",a="The platform is controlled by the Horde, utilizing goblin labor, engineering, and logistics to establish a foothold near the lake.",al={"who runs sludgewerks","sludgewerks faction","horde or neutral"}},{q="Why is it located beneath a wyvern roost?",a="The facility was positioned intentionally near the native wyvern habitat with plans to operate without displacing the beasts, though this has resulted in the goblins enduring endless wyvern droppings directly on their equipment.",al={"wyverns at sludgewerks","why wyvern poop","sludgewerks beasts"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Sludgewerks provides vital logistical and mechanical infrastructure for Horde operations pushing deeper into the rugged terrain of Stonetalon.",["profession:Engineering"]="The goblin machinery operating by the lakeshore showcases classic, soot-belching engineering clashing head-on with Kalimdor's rugged wildlife."},kw={"goblin","horde","mirkfallon lake","platform","sludgewerks","stonetalon","wyvern"},rel={"subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:stonetalon","topic:horde","topic:goblin","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:cliffwalker-post"},src={"Sludgewerks"}}
E["subzone:stonetalon-peak"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonetalon Peak",z="stonetalon",s="Stonetalon Peak is an ancient night elven sanctuary tucked into a verdant alpine valley at the northwestern edge of the Stonetalon Mountains. Sacred to the kaldorei and cared for by local druids, it serves as the primary bastion of the Alliance in these craggy heights.",h="Stonetalon Peak is an ancient night elven sanctuary tucked into a verdant alpine valley at the northwestern...",sec={{t="A Sacred Mountain Vale",b="Perched high above the arid dust of the lower ranges, Stonetalon Peak opens into a lush, mist-shrouded sanctuary. Long considered sacred and steeped in ancient magic, the valley holds ruins dating back millennia to when the region housed temples honoring Queen Azshara before the Great Sundering. In the modern era, kaldorei Sentinels and druids have restored a measure of peaceful stewardship here, maintaining a tranquil refuge complete with a barrow den and a vital Alliance flight roost.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of Destiny",b="Beyond its idyllic forests and ancient ruins, Stonetalon Peak holds historic weight from the Third War. Guided by the visions of Medivh, both Jaina Proudmoore's human expedition and Thrall's Horde scaled these perilous heights in search of the elusive Oracle dwelling within the mountain's deep caverns. That fateful encounter forced mortal enemies to set aside their blades, laying the foundation for the uneasy pact that stood against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal. Today, the peak remains firmly under Sentinel watch, though Horde incursions in the lowlands keep the defenders vigilant.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Stonetalon Peak so green compared to the rest of the mountains?",a="Stonetalon Peak rests within a sheltered high-altitude basin suffused with ancient magic. The dedicated care of the night elves and the druids of the nearby Talon Den has preserved a vibrant, forested sanctuary where vegetation flourishes in sharp contrast to the charred, jagged cliffs below.",al={"why is stonetalon peak green","why forest in stonetalon peak","stonetalon peak weather"}},{q="What happened here during the Third War?",a="Led by the Prophet Medivh's prophetic warnings, both Jaina Proudmoore and Thrall traveled to Stonetalon Peak in search of the Oracle within the mountain's caverns. Their meeting deep inside the stone led them to forge a historic truce, uniting humans and orcs to confront the Burning Legion.",al={"what happened at stonetalon peak warcraft 3","jaina and thrall stonetalon","the oracle stonetalon"}},{q="Who controls Stonetalon Peak right now?",a="The peak is an Alliance outpost, protected and maintained by night elf Sentinels and druids. It serves as the primary safe haven, quest hub, and flight master connection for Alliance adventurers operating in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"is stonetalon peak alliance or horde","who lives at stonetalon peak","stonetalon peak faction"}},{q="What ancient ruins are located here?",a="The crumbling pillars and marble structures scattered through the vale are remnants of the ancient night elven empire, having once served as temple grounds dedicated to Queen Azshara before her descent into madness and the Great Sundering.",al={"stonetalon peak ruins","old temple stonetalon","azshara temple stonetalon peak"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Stonetalon Peak is your sole fortified foothold in the western mountains, offering vital respite, flight paths, and questing aid amidst hostile territory.",["class:Druid"]="The sanctuary is deeply intertwined with Cenarion history and the sacred Talon Den, making it an essential place of pilgrimage and defense for wardens of the wild."},kw={"jaina","kaldorei","night elf","oracle","sentinels","stonetalon","stonetalon peak","talon den","thrall"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","topic:night-elf","topic:sentinels","topic:druid","topic:third-war","npc:thrall","npc:jaina-proudmoore","quest:1088"},src={"Stonetalon Peak"}}
E["subzone:sun-rock-retreat"] = {t="subzone",n="Sun Rock Retreat",z="stonetalon",s="Sun Rock Retreat is a hidden Horde sanctuary nestled high within the central peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains, just south of Mirkfallon Lake. Dominated by tauren and orcish forces, it serves as the Horde's primary staging ground and supply post in the region. Beyond its strategic utility, the settlement rests upon sacred ground long revered by the tauren for its deep spiritual resonance.",h="Sun Rock Retreat is a hidden Horde sanctuary nestled high within the central peaks of the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Sacred Haven in the Peaks",b="Tucked away in a mountain basin south of Mirkfallon Lake, Sun Rock Retreat has long held spiritual importance for the tauren. According to ancient tradition, An'she, the Sun, kissed the very mountain peak where the village stands. For generations before the Horde's arrival, tauren shamans and pilgrims journeyed here to perform rituals bridging the mortal veil, drawing strength from the land's strong bond to the spirit world.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Outpost",b="Today, Sun Rock Retreat serves as the Horde's principal base of operations across the Stonetalon Mountains. Orcs and tauren work side by side to establish a secure foothold against hostile harpy broods, local night elf sentinels, and the industrial pillaging of the Venture Company. As a central hub connecting trade and flight routes between Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads, and the borders of Ashenvale, the retreat provides shelter, provisions, and spiritual guidance to those braving the crags.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Sun Rock Retreat is the primary Horde outpost in the Stonetalon Mountains. Inhabited mainly by tauren and orcs, it acts as a peaceful sanctuary, trading station, and command post for Horde champions working in the region.",al={"what is sun rock","sun rock retreat info","who runs sun rock retreat"}},{q="Why is this place sacred to the tauren?",a="Tauren legend holds that An'she, the Sun, touched the mountain where the retreat now stands. The land has an enduring connection to the spirit world, making it an ancient pilgrimage site for vision quests and communion with ancestors.",al={"why is sun rock sacred","anshe stonetalon","tauren sun rock lore"}},{q="What threats does the retreat face?",a="The retreat contends with aggressive territorial harpies, hostile night elves guarding the sacred woods, and the destructive mining and logging efforts of the Venture Company, which ravages the natural landscape.",al={"sun rock threats","who is attacking sun rock","stonetalon enemies"}},{q="Where does the local flight master connect?",a="Sun Rock Retreat provides wind rider service connecting travelers directly to major central Kalimdor locations, including the Crossroads in the Barrens and the tauren capital of Thunder Bluff.",al={"sun rock flight paths","flying to sun rock retreat","sun rock flight master"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Sun Rock Retreat is more than an outpost to the shu'halo; it is sacred ground blessed by An'she, where shamans have walked the spirit realm for centuries.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde's main staging hub in the Stonetalon Mountains, Sun Rock Retreat offers a vital resupply post and flight hub amidst contested peaks."},kw={"an'she","mirkfallon lake","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","sunrock","tauren","venture company"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:crossroads","topic:tauren","topic:horde","topic:venture-company","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Sun Rock Retreat"}}
E["subzone:talondeep-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="Talondeep Pass",z="stonetalon",s="Talondeep Pass is an artificial mountain breach carved out through heavy goblin excavation to connect southwestern Ashenvale with the crags of Stonetalon Mountains. Built over the older Talondeep Path, this passage serves as a vital transit corridor between two contested frontiers for both the Alliance and the Horde.",h="Talondeep Pass is an artificial mountain breach carved out through heavy goblin excavation to connect...",sec={{t="A Carved Chokepoint",b="Running between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains, Talondeep Pass represents goblin engineering at its most brutish. Workers blasted through the natural barrier of the Talondeep Path, opening up a direct overland link just east of Stardust Spire on the forest side, spilling out into Windshear Crag near the Fold on the Stonetalon side. The tunnel provides travelers and supply lines an alternative to traversing long, winding trails, but its tight confines make it an inherently dangerous corridor under constant threat of ambush.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Contention",b="Because the pass offers direct access to key tactical ground—including routes toward Trueshot Point for Alliance forces—control of the area has sparked fierce friction. Goblins originally tried to secure the passage with a dense minefield to deter intruders and protect their operations. Local night elves systematically disarmed the explosives, turning the excavated tunnel into an open, hotly contested thoroughfare used by scouts and warbands from both sides.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Talondeep Pass lead?",a="The pass connects southwestern Ashenvale, just east of Stardust Spire, directly with northeastern Windshear Crag and the Fold in the Stonetalon Mountains. It also features a side trail connecting to Trueshot Point.",al={"where does talondeep pass go","talondeep pass destination","talondeep pass connection"}},{q="Who created the pass?",a="Goblins excavated the pass using heavy mining and explosives, boring directly through the old Talondeep Path to create an easier transit route across the mountains.",al={"who dug talondeep pass","who made talondeep pass","talondeep pass creator"}},{q="Are there landmines inside the tunnel?",a="Although the goblins originally seeded the passage with an extensive minefield to guard their interests, the night elves managed to locate and disarm all the explosives, making transit safe from sudden blasts.",al={"talondeep pass mines","is talondeep pass mined","goblin minefield talondeep"}},{q="Is Talondeep Pass controlled by the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Neither faction holds undisputed control over the pass. It remains a neutral, contested passage utilized by both Alliance forces and Horde war parties maneuvering between the dense forests of Ashenvale and the logging operations in Stonetalon.",al={"who owns talondeep pass","is talondeep pass alliance or horde","talondeep pass faction"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The sheer stone walls and cleared minefields offer a stark look at goblin excavation methods—crude blasting powder and mechanical excavation cutting where natural passes failed.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces moving out of Ashenvale, this mountain breach provides a vital bypass toward strategic outposts like Trueshot Point."},kw={"ashenvale","goblin","mines","pass","stardust","stonetalon","talondeep","windshear"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","subzone:talondeep-path","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:stardust-spire","subzone:the-fold","subzone:trueshot-point","topic:goblin"},src={"Talondeep Pass"}}
E["subzone:talondeep-path"] = {t="subzone",n="Talondeep Path",z="stonetalon",s="Talondeep Path is a winding underground tunnel boring through the mountain ridge between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains. Devoid of hostile creatures or travelers, it serves as a tranquil, natural subterranean passage connecting Mystral Lake to Windshear Crag.",h="Talondeep Path is a winding underground tunnel boring through the mountain ridge between Ashenvale and the...",sec={{t="A Quiet Mountain Pass",b="Hidden beneath the rugged ridgeline separating Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains lies Talondeep Path, a quiet subterranean route. The passage links the forests just west of Mystral Lake directly to the northwestern reaches of Windshear Crag. Unlike the dangerous surface trails haunted by predators and warring factions, the tunnel interior remains eerily calm, free of hostile beasts or encampments, though riddled with twisting side pockets, crevices, and natural alcoves in the rock. Above ground, faint remnants of an ancient surface road still linger, hinting that travelers once scaled the high peaks before this sheltered cave became the preferred route through the stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Talondeep Path lead?",a="The tunnel connects southwestern Ashenvale to northeastern Stonetalon Mountains. Its northern entrance sits just west of Mystral Lake, while its southern mouth opens into the northwestern side of Windshear Crag.",al={"where does talondeep path go","talondeep path connections","talondeep tunnel exits"}},{q="Are there monsters or enemies inside the tunnel?",a="No. The interior of the cavern is uniquely peaceful and completely barren of hostile monsters, beasts, or friendly NPCs, making it a safe passageway for travelers traversing the mountain divide.",al={"is talondeep path safe","talondeep path mobs","talondeep path threats"}},{q="What are the ruins above the cavern?",a="Remnants of an overgrown surface road run along the mountain ridge directly above the cavern. It suggests an older, treacherous overland route across the crags predated the passage through the hollowed interior.",al={"road above talondeep path","overland path stonetalon"}},{q="Is Talondeep Path an Alliance or Horde tunnel?",a="Neither faction holds the tunnel. It is entirely unfortified and neutral wilderness, allowing safe foot passage for travelers of any allegiance moving between the contested forest and the mountains.",al={"who controls talondeep path","talondeep path faction"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The cavern's winding rock alcoves cut straight through the deep stone foundation of the mountain range, making it a natural landmark when navigating between mineral-rich Ashenvale and Stonetalon."},kw={"ashenvale","cave","mystral lake","stonetalon","talondeep","talondeep path","tunnel","windshear crag"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:mystral-lake"},src={"Talondeep Path"}}
E["subzone:thal-darah-grove"] = {t="subzone",n="Thal'darah Grove",z="stonetalon",s="Thal'darah Grove is an ancient druidic sanctuary and school sheltered beneath a towering tree in Stonetalon Mountains. For generations, it has served as a place of peaceful study where both night elf and tauren druids gather to learn the ways of the wild.",h="Thal'darah Grove is an ancient druidic sanctuary and school sheltered beneath a towering tree in Stonetalon...",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Wild",b="Thal'darah Grove stands as an enduring refuge of learning nestled within the Stonetalon Mountains. At its center rises a massive, sacred tree whose roots have anchored druidic instruction for generations. In a region frequently unsettled by boundary skirmishes and logging operations, the grove remains dedicated strictly to the communion of nature, welcoming novices who look beyond mortal rivalries to study the teachings of the Cenarion Circle.",sp=0},{t="A Shared Bond",b="Unlike many settlements in Kalimdor divided strictly along faction lines, Thal'darah Grove represents the profound spiritual ties between night elves and tauren. Here, young druids of both races study side by side under shared mentors, setting aside the tensions between the Alliance and the Horde to revere the balance of the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Thal'darah Grove?",a="Thal'darah Grove is an ancient druidic sanctuary centered around a towering tree in the Stonetalon Mountains. It serves as an academy of nature worship and training for young druids.",al={"what is thaldarah grove","what is this place","thaldarah tree"}},{q="Who lives and trains in the grove?",a="The grove is inhabited by druid initiates and mentors, welcoming both night elves and tauren who gather to study the ways of Cenarius and the wild.",al={"who is here","who trains here","who lives in thaldarah"}},{q="Does Thal'darah Grove belong to the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Thal'darah Grove is a neutral druidic sanctuary. Both night elves and tauren train together here in peace, focusing on communion with nature rather than faction politics.",al={"is thaldarah alliance or horde","who controls thaldarah","thaldarah faction"}},{q="Where in Stonetalon Mountains is the grove located?",a="Thal'darah Grove is located within the rugged valleys of the Stonetalon Mountains, sheltered beneath a colossal ancient tree.",al={"thaldarah location","where is thaldarah grove","find thaldarah"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The grove represents the timeless connection between tauren and night elf druids, serving as living proof that reverence for the balance transcends political allegiance.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren walk-paths, the sanctuary is an honored site where shamans and druids recognize ancient shared traditions nurtured peacefully alongside night elven tutors."},kw={"ancient tree","battlescar","cenarion","druid school","stonetalon","thal'darah","thaldarah grove"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","topic:druid","topic:tauren","topic:alliance","topic:horde","subzone:battlescar-valley"},src={"Thal'darah Grove"}}
E["subzone:thal-darah-overlook"] = {t="subzone",n="Thal'darah Overlook",z="stonetalon",s="Thal'darah Overlook is an Alliance encampment nestled high in the northern ridges of the Stonetalon Mountains, situated just south of sacred Stonetalon Peak. Anchored by a shimmering moonwell and gentle wisps, it serves as a secluded refuge for night elf sentinels watching the mountain trails.",h="Thal'darah Overlook is an Alliance encampment nestled high in the northern ridges of the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Sentinel Watch in the Heights",b="Perched along the craggy heights just south of Stonetalon Peak, Thal'darah Overlook acts as an essential outpost for the night elves. The high vantage point lets watchers survey the winding mountain paths below, where tensions with the Horde and the Venture Company continually press toward Kaldorei lands. Beneath the canopy of sacred woods, the encampment centers around a quiet moonwell, where wisps flutter between ancient boughs and sentinels keep vigil over the mountain passes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Thal'darah Overlook located?",a="Thal'darah Overlook is located in the northern region of the Stonetalon Mountains, nestled just south of the sacred sanctuary of Stonetalon Peak.",al={"location of thaldarah overlook","where is thal'darah overlook","thaldarah overlook map"}},{q="What faction holds Thal'darah Overlook?",a="The outpost is controlled by the Alliance, specifically maintained by night elf sentinels and druids guarding the approaches to Stonetalon Peak.",al={"is thaldarah alliance","who controls thaldarah overlook","who lives at thaldarah overlook"}},{q="What landmarks are found in the camp?",a="The camp features an open-air night elf pavilion surrounding a consecrated moonwell, maintained alongside resident wisps that tend the nearby trees.",al={"thaldarah moonwell","what is at thaldarah overlook"}},{q="How far is the Overlook from the Charred Vale?",a="Navigating the perilous trails through the craggy heights down to the blighted Charred Vale is a rugged journey that takes roughly two full days on foot.",al={"distance to charred vale","travel from charred vale"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the overlook is a tranquil and sacred staging ground safeguarding the sacred peak from encroaching industrial loggers and Horde incursions.",["faction:Alliance"]="The camp provides Alliance wayfarers with a peaceful haven and a vital strategic vantage point overlooking Stonetalon's contested central pathways."},kw={"moonwell","night elves","sentinels","stonetalon mountains","stonetalon peak","thal'darah overlook","wisps"},rel={"subzone:stonetalon-peak","zone:stonetalon","subzone:charred-vale","topic:alliance","subzone:astranaar","subzone:nijel-s-point"},src={"Thal'darah Overlook"}}
E["subzone:the-fold"] = {t="subzone",n="The Fold",z="stonetalon",s="The Fold is a minor Horde military encampment nestled near Talondeep Pass in the Stonetalon Mountains. It serves as a vital staging post and early rest stop for Horde soldiers marching into the craggy peaks from Ashenvale.",h="The Fold is a minor Horde military encampment nestled near Talondeep Pass in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Foothold Beyond the Pass",b="Tucked away near the mountain pass connecting Stonetalon to Ashenvale, The Fold functions as the Horde's front door to these rugged heights. Troops moving southward through Talondeep Pass rely on this small fortified camp to catch their breath, resupply, and coordinate reconnaissance before venturing deeper into the contested terrain of the mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Fold?",a="The Fold is a small Horde forward camp situated in the northern reaches of Stonetalon Mountains, sitting right near the exit of Talondeep Pass.",al={"the fold stonetalon","what is this camp","the fold purpose"}},{q="Why is this camp important to the Horde?",a="It serves as the initial staging point and safe haven for Horde travelers and forces entering Stonetalon Mountains from the forested territory of Ashenvale.",al={"why is the fold here","horde role in the fold"}},{q="Is The Fold safe for Alliance travelers?",a="No. The Fold is an active Horde military position, and any Alliance travelers attempting to pass through will be attacked on sight by the stationed guards.",al={"can alliance enter the fold","alliance friendly"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde warriors advancing out of the dense canopy of Ashenvale, The Fold provides an essential first haven to rearm before pressing into the crags of Stonetalon.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts charting paths across Talondeep Pass must steer clear of The Fold to avoid provoking Horde sentries stationed at the mountain threshold."},kw={"ashenvale","encampment","horde camp","stonetalon","talondeep pass","the fold"},rel={"subzone:talondeep-pass","zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},src={"The Fold"}}
E["subzone:trueshot-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Trueshot Point",z="stonetalon",s="Trueshot Point is a secluded Alliance encampment perched high along the northern heights of the Stonetalon Mountains near Talondeep Pass. Overlooking the valleys below, the vantage point is completely inaccessible from Stonetalon itself, reached only by trailing down from Stardust Spire in Ashenvale.",h="Trueshot Point is a secluded Alliance encampment perched high along the northern heights of the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Precarious Perch",b="Tucked away high above the craggy ridges of northern Stonetalon Mountains, Trueshot Point serves as a secluded Alliance post. Despite technically resting within Stonetalon's borders near the mouth of Talondeep Pass, sheer cliff faces prevent any ascent from the valley below. Scouts and travelers wishing to reach the outpost must hike in through Stardust Spire in neighboring Ashenvale. Anchored by the marksman Kalen Trueshot, this windswept eyrie provides night elf sentries and their allies with an elevated line of sight over the crags, keeping watch over contested territory while perched high above the reach of ground patrols.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get to Trueshot Point?",a="You cannot reach Trueshot Point from the lowlands of Stonetalon Mountains. The only foot path winds along the ridgeline coming out of Stardust Spire in southwestern Ashenvale, leading out onto the overlook.",al={"how to reach trueshot point","getting to trueshot point","trueshot point path"}},{q="Who lives at Trueshot Point?",a="The outpost is manned by Alliance forces, most notably the night elf marksman Kalen Trueshot, who maintains a vigil overlooking the pass and surrounding valleys.",al={"who is at trueshot point","trueshot point npcs","kalen trueshot"}},{q="Why is this camp located here?",a="Its extreme elevation near Talondeep Pass gives Alliance scouts an unassailable vantage point over the northern reaches of Stonetalon Mountains, monitoring movement while remaining shielded by sheer cliff drop-offs.",al={"purpose of trueshot point","why trueshot point"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers traversing southwestern Ashenvale, Trueshot Point provides a secure ridge-top staging ground and scenic viewpoint looking south into Stonetalon.",["class:Hunter"]="Living up to its name, this cliffside aerie exemplifies the long-range scouting and elevated marksmanship favored by wilderness trackers like Kalen Trueshot."},kw={"ashenvale","kalen trueshot","stardust spire","stonetalon mountains","talondeep pass","trueshot point"},rel={"subzone:talondeep-pass","subzone:stardust-spire","zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","topic:alliance"},src={"Trueshot Point"}}
E["subzone:unearthed-grounds"] = {t="subzone",n="Unearthed Grounds",z="stonetalon",s="The Unearthed Grounds is an excavation site nestled north of Greatwood Vale in the Stonetalon Mountains. Originally established by the dwarven Explorers' League to unearth ancient fossils and relics, the dig has since been overrun and seized by the Horde.",h="The Unearthed Grounds is an excavation site nestled north of Greatwood Vale in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Contested Digsite",b="Tucked away in the rugged heights of the Stonetalon Mountains, the Unearthed Grounds began as a promising survey site for the dwarven Explorers' League. Intrigued by the primeval history preserved in Kalimdor's rock layers, dwarven prospectors began excavating the hillside for ancient fossils. However, operating so close to expanding Horde operations made the camp an immediate target. Horde forces attacked the dig, violently driving out the researchers and seizing control of the overturned earth, leaving behind a scarred, contested hillside in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Unearthed Grounds?",a="It is an excavation site in the Stonetalon Mountains, located just north of Greatwood Vale and east of the Northwatch Expedition Base Camp. It was carved out to uncover ancient fossils and artifacts buried in the slopes.",al={"what is unearthed grounds","unearthed grounds purpose","stonetalon digsite"}},{q="Who dug up this site originally?",a="The site was founded by prospectors and scholars belonging to Ironforge's Explorers' League, who ventured across the sea to uncover Kalimdor's prehistoric secrets.",al={"who built unearthed grounds","who started the digsite","dwarves in stonetalon"}},{q="Why is the Horde here now?",a="The Horde drove out the dwarven researchers to check Alliance expansion within the Stonetalon Mountains and secure tactical ground near Greatwood Vale.",al={"why did horde attack unearthed grounds","who controls unearthed grounds"}},{q="What are they looking for here?",a="The dig primarily targets ancient fossils embedded in the mountain strata, as the Explorers' League sought to catalog Kalimdor's primordial natural history.",al={"what is buried here","what kind of dig is unearthed grounds"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The loss of the digsite to the Horde strikes a painful blow to the Explorers' League's efforts to study the ancient, untapped history of Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Seizing the excavation stopped Alliance operatives from establishing a lasting logistical foothold right above Greatwood Vale."},kw={"digsite","dwarf","explorers league","fossil","greatwood vale","stonetalon","unearthed grounds"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","subzone:greatwood-vale","subzone:northwatch-expedition-base-camp","topic:explorers-league","topic:horde"},src={"Unearthed Grounds"}}
E["subzone:webwinder-path"] = {t="subzone",n="Webwinder Path",z="stonetalon",s="Webwinder Path is a winding mountainous road in the Stonetalon Mountains connecting the troll outpost of Malaka'jin to Mirkfallon Lake. It cuts through rugged crags and dense highland woods inhabited by aggressive arachnids and native beasts.",h="Webwinder Path is a winding mountainous road in the Stonetalon Mountains connecting the troll outpost of...",sec={{t="A Treacherous Thoroughfare",b="Running from the Horde settlement of Malaka'jin toward Mirkfallon Lake, Webwinder Path serves as one of the primary roadways carving through the lower Stonetalon Mountains. True to its name, the route is notorious for the thick cobwebs strung high among the canopy and jagged cliff sides. Travelers along this winding stretch must constantly watch their step, sharing the beaten path with prowling mountain spiders, aggressive thunder lizards, and territorial rams.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Webwinder Path lead?",a="Webwinder Path stretches between the Darkspear troll outpost of Malaka'jin in the south and Mirkfallon Lake further up the mountain to the north.",al={"webwinder path location","where is webwinder path","what does webwinder path connect"}},{q="Why is it called Webwinder Path?",a="The road earns its name from the sheer abundance of arachnids inhabiting the region. Spiders spin vast labyrinths of glittering silk high in the trees and along rocky ledges flanking the roadway.",al={"why webwinder","why is it called webwinder"}},{q="What creatures wander the path?",a="Aside from the venomous spiders that weave webs above the road, travelers frequently encounter roaming thunder lizards, highland rams, and ordinary mountain critters.",al={"what lives here","webwinder path beasts","mobs on webwinder path"}},{q="Is Webwinder Path safe to travel?",a="It is far from safe. The local predators are fierce and territorial, and the road passes directly past the Horde camp at Malaka'jin, making it perilous for Alliance wayfarers venturing up from the Barrens.",al={"is webwinder path dangerous","can alliance travel webwinder path"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The path is a crucial overland artery right on the doorstep of Malaka'jin, connecting your scouts to the deeper valleys of Stonetalon.",["class:Hunter"]="The path is home to robust thunder lizards, sturdy mountain rams, and venomous web-spinners, making it an excellent trail for scouting and taming Stonetalon beasts."},kw={"malaka'jin","mirkfallon lake","road","spiders","stonetalon","webwinder","webwinder path"},rel={"subzone:malaka-jin","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:stonetalon","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Webwinder Path"}}
E["subzone:windshear-crag"] = {t="subzone",n="Windshear Crag",z="stonetalon",s="Windshear Crag is a heavily despoiled valley in the central Stonetalon Mountains, stripped of its ancient timber by the Venture Company. Once a lush forest, the region is now an industrial wasteland dominated by whirring shredders, murky runoff, and aggressive logging crews. In the shadows of the machinery, local kobolds burrow for ore while mountain passes connect the scarred landscape to Ashenvale.",h="Windshear Crag is a heavily despoiled valley in the central Stonetalon Mountains, stripped of its ancient...",sec={{t="Industrial Devastation",b="Not long ago, Windshear Crag was a thick, old-growth woodland flanking the slopes of Stonetalon. That tranquil wilderness vanished when the Venture Company arrived in search of profit. Today, the basin is filled with severed stumps, acrid smog, and clanking machinery. The entire logging enterprise is overseen by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a leper gnome whose engineering genius produced the Super Reaper 6000—a mechanical terror capable of reducing massive trunks to kindling in moments. From an elevated platform above the polluted Cragpool Lake, Gerenzo directs an unchecked operation that strips the mountain bare, earning the hostility of rival engineers and local inhabitants alike.",sp=0},{t="Mines and Mountain Passes",b="Beyond the active timberyards, Windshear Crag holds other hazards and crossroads. To the southeast lies Windshear Mine, where territorial kobolds dig through the rock for Smoky Iron Ingots, fiercely attacking anyone who nears their haul. In the crag's northeast reaches, travelers can find the Talondeep Path, an underground cavern tunnel threading straight beneath the ridges into Ashenvale. Stationed near this shadowed portal stands the tauren elder Braug Dimspirit, who tests the historical wisdom and resolve of Horde wayfarers venturing through the contested peaks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is running the logging operation here?",a="The logging venture is commanded on-site by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a brilliant but contaminated leper gnome engineer. Operating under contract with the Venture Company, he watches over the crag from a timber platform raised directly over Cragpool Lake.",al={"who leads venture co here","who is the boss of windshear","gerenzo wrenchwhistle lore"}},{q="What is the Super Reaper 6000?",a="The Super Reaper 6000 is an advanced mechanical logging prototype engineered by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle. Designed to clear timber at unprecedented speeds, it can grind ancient mountain trees into sawdust within moments, accelerating the company's clear-cutting.",al={"super reaper 6000","what is the big shredder","venture co reaper"}},{q="Why is the Undermine Tinkers' Union targeting Gerenzo?",a="Director Riddlevox of the Tinkers' Union in Undermine dispatched the goblin Ziz Fizziks to recover Gerenzo's stolen designs and execute him. The Union considers Gerenzo's unauthorized modifications to their shredder schematics a blatant theft of intellectual property.",al={"why kill gerenzo","ziz fizziks motives","tinkers union vendetta"}},{q="Where does the cave in the northeast lead?",a="The cave in the northeast corner is the Talondeep Path. It cuts through the subterranean roots of the mountains, providing a foot route between Windshear Crag and the dense forests of Ashenvale.",al={"talondeep path destination","windshear cave exit","tunnel in windshear crag"}},{q="Who are the kobolds digging in the southeast?",a="The Windshear kobolds have overrun the local mine in the southeastern corner of the crag. They vigorously defend their subterranean claim, excavating deposits of Smoky Iron Ingots used by regional smiths.",al={"windshear mine kobolds","why are kobolds here","smoky iron ingots"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The industrial equipment throughout the crag showcases cutthroat goblin trade secrets and Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle's lethal Super Reaper designs.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde travelers heading toward Ashenvale encounter Braug Dimspirit near the Talondeep Path, where he tests their knowledge of Kalimdor's history."},kw={"braug dimspirit","cragpool lake","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","super reaper 6000","talondeep path","venture company","windshear crag","windshear mine","ziz fizziks"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","topic:venture-company","subzone:cragpool-lake","subzone:talondeep-path","quest:1096","quest:1093","quest:1483","quest:1152"},src={"Windshear Crag"}}
E["subzone:windshear-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Windshear Hold",z="stonetalon",s="Windshear Hold is a fortified Alliance settlement situated within the contested crags of the Stonetalon Mountains. Built using traditional night elf craftsmanship, the outpost serves as a central staging ground for diverse Alliance forces contending with nearby threats.",h="Windshear Hold is a fortified Alliance settlement situated within the contested crags of the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Crag",b="Perched within the rugged heights of Windshear Crag, Windshear Hold provides the Alliance with a vital foothold in the heart of Stonetalon. Though rooted in night elven architecture and forest sensibilities, the hold gathers soldiers and travelers of all Alliance races under one banner. It acts as a defensive anchor against hostile encroachers and coordinates regional communication through its aerial courier networks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Windshear Hold?",a="It is an Alliance outpost situated within Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Constructed using night elf architectural designs, it houses members of multiple Alliance races and offers refuge for regional travelers.",al={"windshear hold","what is windshear hold","about windshear hold"}},{q="Who controls this settlement?",a="The settlement belongs entirely to the Alliance. While night elf builders laid its foundations, it is garrisoned and utilized by various races of the faction cooperating in Stonetalon.",al={"who owns windshear hold","is windshear hold alliance","windshear hold faction"}},{q="What services are available at Windshear Hold?",a="Travelers can find shelter and lodging at the Fallowmere Inn. The hold also functions as a travel hub with flight networks connecting to outposts across the region such as Nijel's Point and Farwatcher's Glen.",al={"windshear hold services","fallowmere inn","what is here"}},{q="Where in the Stonetalon Mountains is it located?",a="The hold is positioned in Windshear Crag, a mountainous and contested portion of the Stonetalon Mountains often troubled by logging and territorial skirmishes.",al={"windshear hold location","where is windshear hold","find windshear hold"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Windshear Hold serves as your vital redoubt in central Stonetalon, offering shelter at Fallowmere Inn and flight connections to northern bases like Nijel's Point.",["race:NightElf"]="Built from ancestral craft to defend the peaks of Kalimdor, this outpost integrates your sister races into guarding the sacred mountains."},kw={"alliance","fallowmere inn","stonetalon","windshear crag","windshear hold"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","subzone:nijel-s-point","subzone:farwatcher-s-glen","subzone:stardust-spire","subzone:thal-darah-overlook","topic:alliance","topic:night-elf"},src={"Windshear Hold"}}
E["subzone:windshear-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Windshear Valley",z="stonetalon",s="Windshear Valley is a rugged depression nestled within Windshear Crag in the central Stonetalon Mountains. In this era, the valley remains an untamed wilderness dominated by predatory spiders, roaming thunder lizards, and hardy mountain beasts rather than military encampments.",h="Windshear Valley is a rugged depression nestled within Windshear Crag in the central Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Wild Valley",b="Tucked away among the slopes of Windshear Crag, Windshear Valley represents the wild, unsettled heart of the Stonetalon Mountains. While nearby logging operations and conflicts between the Alliance, the Horde, and the Venture Company draw blood across the crags, this valley remains largely left to nature. Dangerous deepmoss creepers spin webs between craggy stone outcrops, while thunder lizards stalk the scrubland, making it a hazardous route for solitary travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live in Windshear Valley?",a="The valley is primarily home to venomous spiders such as deepmoss creepers, thunder lizards, and hardy Stonetalon rams that graze upon the rocky heights.",al={"windshear valley mobs","monsters in windshear valley","what is here"}},{q="Is Windshear Valley controlled by the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Neither faction holds a fortified presence within Windshear Valley itself. It remains an untamed wilderness, though both factions operate camps and patrols across the broader region of Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"who controls windshear valley","alliance in windshear valley","horde presence"}},{q="How does Windshear Valley relate to Windshear Crag?",a="Windshear Valley is a lower, forested depression situated directly within the larger region known as Windshear Crag.",al={"is this windshear crag","windshear crag connection"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The valley's rugged beasts, from tough thunder lizards to mountain rams, make it a natural training ground for trackers and beastmasters passing through Stonetalon."},kw={"rams","spiders","stonetalon","thunder lizards","windshear crag","windshear valley"},rel={"subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","topic:alliance"},src={"Windshear Valley"}}
E["zone:stonetalon"] = {t="zone",n="Stonetalon Mountains",z="stonetalon",s="The Stonetalon Mountains are a rugged, wind-carved chain of craggy peaks bordering Ashenvale, the Barrens, and Desolace. Revered by both the night elves and the tauren as a sacred sanctuary, the region's sacred heights stand in sharp contrast to the smoke and machinery choking its lower canyons. Today, the mountains are torn by deforestation, volatile elemental devastation, and simmering border hostilities.",h="The Stonetalon Mountains are a rugged, wind-carved chain of craggy peaks bordering Ashenvale, the Barrens...",sec={{t="The Ill Winds and the Peaks",b="Rising sharply out of central Kalimdor, the Stonetalon range catches the moisture drifting from the western seas, giving birth to sudden downpours and treacherous, rain-slick sandstone trails. The dominant feature of the lower valleys is the incessant scouring gale known as the Ill Winds, capable of blinding travelers with grit or throwing the careless straight off sheer cliffsides. Higher up, evergreen forests mantle the ridges surrounding Stonetalon Peak, where the night elves tend ancestral barrows and glades, watching over the sacred roosts of wyverns and hippogryphs that nest along Mirkfallon Lake.",sp=0},{t="Industry and Intrusion",b="The peaceful solitude of the range has been violently disrupted by the arrival of the Venture Company. Setting up sprawling logging camps and digging deep strip mines in Windshear Crag, the goblins—aided by the deranged leper gnome Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle—have clear-cut old-growth timber, blackened the skies with furnace smoke, and poured industrial sludge into the mountain runoff. Their greed has provoked swift retaliation: local shamans from Orgrimmar answered the agonized cries of the mountain spirits, while small Alliance camps stationed nearby fight back against the defilers to protect what remains of the highlands.",sp=0},{t="Scars of the Past",b="To the south lies the Charred Vale, once a blossoming wilderness, now reduced to an ash-covered wasteland churning with rogue fire elementals, black dragonspawn, and harpies. While the peaks were the historic site where the Horde and Alliance forged an uneasy truce during the Third War under the guidance of the mysterious Oracle, current relations are fraying. Renegade Grimtotem tauren operate out of seized encampments, and Darkspear trolls in Malaka'jin clash with Alliance incursions pushing outward from the Barrens and Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Most travelers enter via the Talondeep Pass, a mountain trail cutting into the range from southwestern Ashenvale. There are also high trails leading south into Desolace and routes descending eastward directly into the northern expanses of the Barrens.",al={"stonetalon entrance","how to get to stonetalon","stonetalon road"}},{q="Why is the Charred Vale burned and ruined?",a="The Charred Vale was once a lush haven, but cataclysmic devastation consumed the valley in flames. It has been reduced to a smoldering ruin crawling with aggressive fire elementals, rogue drakes, and deadly harpies.",al={"charred vale fire","what happened to charred vale","why charred vale burnt"}},{q="What is the Venture Company doing in Windshear Crag?",a="The Venture Company is ruthlessly clear-cutting timber and drilling deep into the mountainside for mineral wealth. Their operations have fouled Cragpool Lake with engine grease, stripped the valleys bare, and enraged the local spirits and native inhabitants.",al={"venture co stonetalon","windshear crag goblins","why are goblins cutting trees"}},{q="Where are the main flight masters located?",a="Alliance heroes use the flight master perched at the high sanctuary of Stonetalon Peak in the north, while Horde adventurers base themselves in the central mountain village of Sun Rock Retreat.",al={"stonetalon flight path","where is flight point stonetalon","stonetalon fp"}},{q="What happened at Stonetalon Peak during the Third War?",a="Guided by visions of the Prophet Medivh, Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore climbed the caverns of Stonetalon Peak in search of the Oracle. There, the two faction leaders forged the historic temporary alliance that united against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal.",al={"stonetalon peak lore","the oracle stonetalon","third war stonetalon"}},{q="Who are the Grimtotem in Stonetalon?",a="The Grimtotem are a ruthless, renegade tauren tribe hostile to outsider influence. In the Stonetalons, they have occupied a mountain post near the border of the Barrens, terrorizing local travelers and taking prisoners.",al={"grimtotem post","grimtotem stonetalon"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers rely on the secluded refuge of Sun Rock Retreat and the southern troll post of Malaka'jin to curb Venture Company industrial pollution and root out treacherous Grimtotem outlaws.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stationed high atop Stonetalon Peak and in hidden camps around Windshear Crag, the Alliance defends ancient kaldorei barrows from goblin machines and encroaching territorial rivals.",["class:Druid"]="The desecration of Windshear Crag and the scorched corruption of the Charred Vale serve as a grave summons for druids seeking to soothe enraged nature spirits and protect sacred roosts.",["class:Shaman"]="The cry of the mountain spirits under assault by goblin drills can be heard as far as Orgrimmar, calling shamans to quell rampaging rock elementals and restore balance to the peaks."},kw={"charred vale","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","malaka'jin","stonetalon","stonetalon peak","sun rock retreat","talondeep pass","windshear"},rel={"subzone:stonetalon-peak","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","subzone:windshear-crag","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:malaka-jin","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","zone:desolace"},m={levels="15-27"},src={"Stonetalon Mountains (Classic)","Stonetalon Mountains"}}
